tus":"completed","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/642\n{\"body\":\"## Problem and resulting behavior\\n\\nVC-2 shell snapshots already detected some large test-file changes, but the obligation observer discarded changes without retained raw text. Incomplete 20,000-entry scans were not reflected in the obligation record. This records either condition as an `unverifiable-change` for active obligations; ordinary complete scans still record only actual, classifiable changes.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/regression_obligations_agent.test.ts test/verification_shell_guard.test.ts` — 21 passed, 0 failed at `ab5a382e1957a5ed59130da1a959562728375685` after building the worktree-local Rust core. The first attempt was run before the core binary existed and is superseded by this successful run.\\n- `npm run build --prefix cli` — passed at the same revision.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed before commit.\\n- Hosted CI for this PR is queued. The 20,000-entry negative case took about 45 seconds locally; the existing full CI suite has not yet completed on this revision.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- Queried `xerj search --prefix nexus-cli \\\"finishVerificationShellGuard shellChangeObserver recordTestEdit\\\" -k 4`; it located the snapshot and recording paths.\\n- Queried `xerj code opencode \\\"detect test file edits before after snapshots verification command\\\" -k 4 --full 900`; results contained no relevant bounded verification snapshot analogue, so no peer design was adopted.\\n- The XERJ report was submitted through its fallback endpoint after the GitHub fork path was unavailable.\\n\\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\\n\\nNo persisted schema migration is required: the weakening record is an additive string kind. This does not claim the test body ran or block a shell command; it records that the edit could not be assessed. A complete scan and a small file continue using the existing exact-text weakening checks.\\n\\n## Documentation and coordination\\n\\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\\n- [ ] Relevant checks pass, or blockers are explicitly identified. Hosted CI is queued.\\n- [x] No secrets, private task payloads, or unrelated changes are included.\\n- [x] Shared-file ownership and dependencies are coordinated where applicable.\\n\\nNo independent reviewer is available for this single-user repository; that does not block publication per the owner's direction. The VC-2 backlog row in PR #639 should be reconciled after that PR lands.\\n\\n## Needs from other slices\\n\\nAfter PR #639 merges, update its VC-2 row to describe this behavior and retain the separate runner-output authenticity gap.\\n\",\"headRefOid\":\"ab5a382e1957a5ed59130da1a959562728375685\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44611609826/job/135869395950\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-19T20:43:46Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44611609577/job/135869396889\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-19T20:43:46Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44611609826/job/135869395476\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-19T20:43:46Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-19T20:44:05Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44611609826/job/135869396040\",\"name\":\"cloudf