{"timestamp":"2026-11-19T20:52:03.757Z","ordinal":28399,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_007c6624f07d1d76016aff6166925887d1928b4942276e7d2c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_12534d1edaea4df6aafac80af56bd56e","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/nexus-pr-642-body.md <<'EOF'\\n## Problem and resulting behavior\\n\\nVC-2 shell snapshots detected some large test-file changes but the obligation observer discarded changes without retained raw text. Incomplete 20,000-entry scans were not reflected in the obligation record. Changes to verification files larger than the 2 MiB fingerprint bound also could be missed because only metadata was compared.\\n\\nThe change records large test-file edits as `unverifiable-change` against active obligations, records incomplete workspace scans, and refuses shell execution before it starts in `verificationPaths: \\\"block\\\"` mode when the initial scan is incomplete. Complete scans and small files retain the existing exact-text weakening checks.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/regression_obligations_agent.test.ts test/verification_shell_guard.test.ts` — 22 passed, 0 failed at `061dc68c` after building the worktree-local Rust core.\\n- `npm run build --prefix cli` — passed at the prior source commit `ab5a382e`; the final additions were type-checked by the 22-test run's TypeScript execution.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed before each commit.\\n- Hosted CI for this updated head is starting. The 20,000-entry negative case took about 32 seconds on the latest local run. The full CLI suite has not yet completed on this revision.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- Queried `xerj search --prefix nexus-cli \\\"finishVerificationShellGuard shellChangeObserver recordTestEdit\\\" -k 4`; it located the snapshot and recording paths.\\n- Queried `xerj code opencode \\\"detect test file edits before after snapshots verification command\\\" -k 4 --full 900`; results contained no relevant bounded verification snapshot analogue, so no peer design was adopted.\\n- The XERJ report was submitted through its fallback endpoint after the GitHub fork path was unavailable.\\n\\n## Compatibility, security, and recovery\\n\\nNo persisted schema migration is required: the weakening record adds a string kind. Unknown edits are recorded, not claimed to be proven weakenings. For the explicit block policy, incomplete initial snapshots refuse shell execution before any command side effect occurs.\\n\\n## Documentation and coordination\\n\\n- [x] Scope and documentation match the final implementation.\\n- [ ] Relevant checks pass, or blockers are explicitly identified. Hosted CI is queued.\\n- [x] No secrets, private task payloads, or unrelated changes are included.\\n- [x] Shared-file ownership and dependencies are coordinated where applicable.\\n\\nNo independent reviewer is available for this single-user repository; that does not block publication per the owner's direction. The VC-2 backlog row in PR #639 should be reconciled after this PR lands.\\n\\n## Needs from other slices\\n\\nAfter PR #642 merges, update the VC-2 backlog row in PR #639 to describe this behavior and retain the separate runner-output authenticity gap.\\nEOF\\ngh pr edit 642 --body-file /tmp/nexus-pr-642-body.md; gh pr view 642 --json headRefOid,baseRefOid,statusCheckRollup,url\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v1-2x-vc2-large-shell-edits\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:2200}); text(r.output); if(r.session_id) text(`SESSION ${r.session_id}`)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f580-fbbd-7c63-b412-737898b1a440","create_time":1795121510.7313917}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":12522,"sampled_through_sequence":12520,"client_authored":false}}
