opencode' (index 19d old)\nCite file:line for anything you rely on.\nWARNING: the index for 'opencode' was NOT verified complete (autoindex exit 1, kept unverified). A miss here might mean 'not indexed yet', not 'does not exist'. Re-run `xerj corpus index opencode` to resume or confirm it.\n\n─── USER_MANUAL.md:569  (score 1001.00)\n    ACT=1`, which prints a notification whenever a new rule is recorded into `<workspace>/.nexus/knowledge.json`.\n    - **MCP Server Environment**: MCP servers start with basic process, locale, proxy (`HTTPS_PROXY`, `NO_PROXY`, …) and CA-trust (`SSL_CERT_FILE`, `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, …) variables only — not Nexus's own credentials. Give a server the token it needs in its `env` block in `mcp.json`.\n    - **Build Identity**: `nexus --version` and `nexus doctor` show the commit the running build was made from, its branch, and whether the source had uncommitted changes (`1.2.1 (cc177be91d15-dirty, feat/tui-su\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── v1.2.1/PLAN.md:84  (score 1001.00)\n    non-withdrawals, and after the synchronous path can hold a steer while a judge answers (the pilot gateway judge took a median of about 17 s per message) | M | P2 (v1.2.2, gated) |\n    \n    ### CS: containment and security\n    \n    | Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n    |---|---|---|---|---|\n    | CS-1 | Containment by default: use the existing bubblewrap path by default when available (fall back to review mode with a visible notice when not); keep `--sandbox none` | decision D1; default flips only with an opt-out and a release-notes line; doctor reports the effective containment | M | P1 |\n    | CS-2 | Hard stop for s\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md:120  (score 1001.00)\n    Disposition: **P0** must-have for v1.2.1; **P1** should-have; **P2** stretch, may roll to v1.2.2; **DEF** deferred with a decision requested; **NO** deliberately not copied. Unit ids are defined in `PLAN.md`.\n    \n    | ID | Gap | Evidence | D