{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T03:49:13.235Z","ordinal":28697,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f70b-846a-7860-9aa2-ec3e0d5fdc10","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_05793ea695c2aa2c016affc32ddd1887d29d8c9e44cb6efd2d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The v1.2.x work does **not** need a second maintainer. I’ve treated this as a single-user repository: no paid reviewer or suspended account is required, and that should not hold up publishing.\n\n### Decisions still needed\n\n- **Benchmark scope and spending cap (MQ-1/2):** choose the task subset and maximum model spend. Until then, the benchmark adapter can be developed against a mock gateway, but no external performance claim can be made.\n- **Extra runner cost (RD-1/2):** decide whether to pay for macOS and arm64/musl runners. The corresponding artifacts depend on access to those runners.\n- **Worktree-bound session forks (RD-6):** decide whether a fork should create a separate checkout. The current behavior refuses that operation to avoid two sessions sharing a checkout.\n- **Blocked-requirement contract and steering conflicts (VC-9):** decide the user-facing contract for a blocked requirement and how conflicting steering should be resolved.\n- **Masking defaults (CX-4):** choose whether to set a default output-masking threshold; there is no safety measurement supporting one yet.\n- **Reasoning-off model aliases (WM-3):** define how those aliases should be judged, then run repeat measurements.\n\n### Resources or access needed\n\n- A local scheduler that can reach the gateway, plus a prepared configuration, for MQ-4’s first scheduled conformance run.\n- A container-capable benchmark environment, pinned benchmark tasks, and the model budget for MQ-1/2.\n- Paid or otherwise available macOS and arm64/musl runners for RD-1/2.\n- Anthropic API access for live cache validation; Bedrock access if Bedrock caching is in scope (CX-6).\n- Runner time for the CI duration investigation (PC-1).\n\n### Work that can proceed without those decisions\n\nTwo PRs are open: [#642](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/642) for VC-2 and [#639](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/639) for backlog reconciliation. Their required checks were still running at my latest check; both need green Node 22, Node 24, and Linux checks before merging. The CI “Entire” check is not a merge gate under the current instructions.\n\nThe backlog also has implementation or verification work that does not require new paid resources, including VC-6/VC-9 details, CX-7, CS-6 server pinning, and reconciling Claude’s unfinished candidate work against current `main`. Some of that work overlaps active branches, so it needs to be picked up after checking those branch changes rather than copied wholesale. The old candidate contains held-out evaluation material, which must stay excluded.\n\nThe local `main` checkout is clean at `f873787a`. My list above is based on the current backlog and open PRs; exact CI and branch status can change while those checks run."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"content_token_count":617,"started_at_ms":1795146541944,"completed_at_ms":1795146553235}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T03:49:13.284Z","ordinal":28698,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_05793ea695c2aa2c016affc32ddd1887d29d8c9e44cb6efd2d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The v1.2.x work does **not** need a second maintainer. I’ve treated this as a single-user repository: no paid reviewer or suspended account is required, and that should not hold up publishing.\n\n### Decisions still needed\n\n- **Benchmark scope and spending cap (MQ-1/2):** choose the task subset and maximum model spend. Until then, the benchmark adapter can be developed against a mock gateway, but no external performance claim can be made.\n- **Extra runner cost (RD-1/2):** decide whether to pay for macOS and arm64/musl runners. The corresponding artifacts depend on access to those runners.\n- **Worktree-bound session forks (RD-6):** decide whether a fork should create a separate checkout. The current behavior refuses that operation to avoid two sessions sharing a checkout.\n- **Blocked-requirement contract and steering conflicts (VC-9):** decide the user-facing contract for a blocked requirement and how conflicting steering should be resolved.\n- **Masking defaults (CX-4):** choose whether to set a default output-masking threshold; there is no safety measurement supporting one yet.\n- **Reasoning-off model aliases (WM-3):** define how those aliases should be judged, then run repeat measurements.\n\n### Resources or access needed\n\n- A local scheduler that can reach the gateway, plus a prepared configuration, for MQ-4’s first scheduled conformance run.\n- A container-capable benchmark environment, pinned benchmark tasks, and the model budget for MQ-1/2.\n- Paid or otherwise available macOS and arm64/musl runners for RD-1/2.\n- Anthropic API access for live cache validation; Bedrock access if Bedrock caching is in scope (CX-6).\n- Runner time for the CI duration investigation (PC-1).\n\n### Work that can proceed without those decisions\n\nTwo PRs are open: [#642](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/642) for VC-2 and [#639](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/639) for backlog reconciliation. Their required checks were still running at my latest check; both need green Node 22, Node 24, and Linux checks before merging. The CI “Entire” check is not a merge gate under the current instructions.\n\nThe backlog also has implementation or verification work that does not require new paid resources, including VC-6/VC-9 details, CX-7, CS-6 server pinning, and reconciling Claude’s unfinished candidate work against current `main`. Some of that work overlaps active branches, so it needs to be picked up after checking those branch changes rather than copied wholesale. The old candidate contains held-out evaluation material, which must stay excluded.\n\nThe local `main` checkout is clean at `f873787a`. My list above is based on the current backlog and open PRs; exact CI and branch status can change while those checks run.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f70b-846a-7860-9aa2-ec3e0d5fdc10","create_time":1795146541.8953974,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":12661,"sampled_through_sequence":12659,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_05793ea695c2aa2c016affc32ddd1887d29d8c9e44cb6efd2d","turn_id":"01a1f70b-846a-7860-9aa2-ec3e0d5fdc10","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1f712-97c4-7a81-b8ac-fcde326a0fb7","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":736}}
