n lines reported; settled tool calls only\n- [x] Failures visible (CLI/TUI); turn stopped (PERSISTENCE_FAILED) on auto-commit failure\n- [x] /compact queued during work; ack + outcome; dedupe, bound, cancel, shutdown, turn-end; --llm too\n- [x] Thrash detection across steps (low-yield hold), separate from repetition\n- [x] (live finding) tracking record shared in place, never replaced mid-turn\n\n## D. Provider capabilities and token accounting\n- [x] Discover context/output/limits_version from /models (gateway, vLLM max_model_len); refresh on change\n- [x] Count via /v1/tokenize when advertised, with the exact outbound payload builder\n- [x] Sources: exact_admitted, exact_sampled_worker, gateway_conservative, client_estimate\n- [x] Strict counting opt-in; standalone defaults; headroom policy labelled as policy\n\n## Validation / deliverables\n- [x] Tests per area (65 new tests across 4 files); full `make test` on final snapshot (see review)\n- [x] Live local-inference multistep run across compaction boundaries (3 runs; run 3 completed)\n- [x] Operator + developer docs, acceptance ledger, gateway capability handoff\n\n## Review\n- Live runs found two real defects scripted tests had missed (re-reads after compaction stopped as loops; compaction\n  orphaning the live tracker) plus a wasted second count per step. All fixed with regression tests.\n- Not done: commit/merge (operator's decision), live standalone run against a non-gateway server, live capacity /\n  worker-change observation, `graphify update` (no graph in the worktree; the main checkout was not touched).\n\n# Output-truncation recovery (2026-10-14)\n\nBranch `fix/output-truncation-recovery` from main 1c3afbd. Trigger: live session `session_20261014_074807_hmo7` ended\n`FAILED / INFERENCE_FAILED (output_truncated/client)` at step 54 when one reply used the whole 8192-token output\nallowance inside a tool call (about 173 s of generation); output_truncated was always fatal to the turn.\n\n- [x] 1. Truncated reply → bounded retry: nothing from it runs; a Nexus note names the tool/path, the allowance, and asks\n      for the content in parts; the turn continues at the next step (new request id)\n- [x] 2. Bound: a second consecutive truncation ends the turn exactly as before; the truncated step counts as no progress\n- [x] 3. Prevention: write_file/edit_file descriptions say a reply's output is limited and long content goes in parts\n- [x] 4. Tests: truncated tool call → chunked write completes; two in a row → fails as before; truncated prose never\n      accepted as final; no tool from a truncated reply runs\n- [ ] Full `make test` on a snapshot; docs (USER_MANUAL / COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY) updated\n\n# Post-v1.1.3 housekeeping (2026-11-05)\n\nBranch `chore/housekeeping-post-v113` from main 46fd5045 (v1.1.3 stable, published).\n\n- [x] Root clutter (check-in scripts, session dumps, continuity-validation, stale root package-lock.json) moved to\n      `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/root-clutter/`; `.gitignore` now ignores `/nexus-session-*.json`\n- [x] 220 stale claims renamed `*.released-<UTC>` and logged; `GATEWAY` (codex-root, RC15 E5, 2026-10-31) left active\n- [x] Worktrees 875 → 137: 657 clean removed; 81 dirty archived to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/worktrees/`\n      (tracked.patch + untracked.tgz + meta.txt) then removed; 136 detached-HEAD trees kept (commits on no ref)\n- [x] Local branches 596 → 206: 364 merged into main deleted; 31 unmerged with a remote copy deleted\n- [x] Owner follow-up: kept only branches with roadmap/planning content not on main (`v1/docs-v11-layered-memory`,\n      `backup/agent-work-product-ae474637` with LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md) plus `v1/v113-plan`; the other 202 local branches\n      bundled to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/unmerged-branches.bundle` (tips in `branch-tips.txt`) then deleted\n- [x] Last stale claim (`GATEWAY`) released; no unreleased claims remain\n- [x] 4 stashes archived (`~/nexus-archive/house