{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T03:56:01.220Z","ordinal":28961,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f712-aaf3-7db1-9f93-ddce93b124cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4d900d7c-7f0a-499c-9434-6bfd6d82385f","process_id":"17773","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show v1/invariants-audit:tasks/todo.md | awk '/previous content follows/{exit} {print}' | nl -ba | tail -105"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show v1/invariants-audit:tasks/todo.md | awk '/previous content follows/{exit} {print}' | nl -ba | tail -105"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    62\t| D7 | DOC | SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md header/line cites stale; ARCHITECTURE.md Rust file list stale; EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md header stale | L | correct; no append-only history |\n    63\tNot found/credited: reviewer cannot self-accept; failover authorization per endpoint; cancellation path; slash/protocol dispatch rejects unknown.\n    64\t\n    65\t### Merged execution order (correctness first; style last)\n    66\t1 U1,U2(+D5),U3,U4 (side effects/unknown outcome)  2 L1,L2,L3,E1 (state integrity)  3 R1,D6,D3,D2,D1 (acceptance + authorization)  4 P1..P4 (providers)  5 R2,R3 (review/agent guidance, existing contracts)  6 A1,A2,A4/A5,E2,E3,E4,D4 (invariant/consolidation with tests)  7 scenarios A..H in CERI fixture + diff_boundary eval tasks  8 INVARIANTS/rationale doc (code<->test<->rationale table, checked by a script like check_requirements) + roadmap rows + CHANGELOG  9 regression vs baseline, tsc, node 22/24 note.\n    67\tScenario plan (follow-up §11): A..H become CERI `multi_file_refactoring`/`scoped_implementation` fixture entries driven deterministically (diff_boundary + test commands on fixture repos); real-Nexus runs only if the gateway claim is available (reported separately from fixture-only results).\n    68\t\n    69\t## Review (measured 2026-11-17; nothing pushed or merged)\n    70\tBranch `v1/invariants-impl` (merged forward into `v1/invariants-audit`), based on origin/main 65c76b28; origin/main has since moved (e.g. #582), so a merge needs the owner's rebase/conflict pass (CHANGELOG, PLAN.md, agent.ts are the likely overlaps).\n    71\tRegression (all runs on this host, one at a time, throwaway HOME):\n    72\t- Clean base 65c76b28, Node 24: 4030 tests, 4014 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (`eval_version_probe_storage`: needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT`, only CI sets it).\n    73\t- Branch at b2418684 (before the last EI-3/EI-4/EI-7 changes), Node 24: 4082 tests, 4066 pass, 15 skipped, same single failure.\n    74\t- Branch at f7aa3919 (final), Node 24: 3441 tests in the completed segments, 3426 pass, same single failure; `compaction_continuity` timed out in the runner under host load (it also timed out in the first, untouched-base attempt) and passed alone: 34/34 in ~5 min. The branch adds no new failure.\n    75\t- Node 22.22.2 (nvm), final tree 91f69fb1 (code identical to f7aa3919; docs only since): 4089 tests, 4073 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (the same environment-only `eval_version_probe_storage`), no timeouts. An earlier Node 22 run on b2418684 had three files time out under host load (load average above 20 from other processes); each passed alone.\n    76\t- `tsc` clean; `scripts/check_invariants.mjs` and the leak-guard ratchet pass. CI matrix (test-matrix 22/24, linux-x86_64) not run: GitHub only.\n    77\tDone (rule ids in `docs/INVARIANTS.md`): U1 I-EFFECT-1; U2/D5 I-EFFECT-2; U3/U4 I-EFFECT-3; L1/L2/L3/E1/D4 I-LIFE-1; D3 I-AUTH-1; D1 I-AUTH-2 (reproduced at runtime first: every MCP call returned FAIL-001); A4 I-AUTH-3; D6 I-ACCEPT-1; E4 I-ACCEPT-2; P2 I-PROVIDER-1; P3 I-PROVIDER-2; D2 I-EFFECT-4; R2 I-CHANGE-2; R3 I-CHANGE-1; E3 one success predicate; A2 durable private writers; scenarios A-H (mechanism-level); INVARIANTS.md + checker + CI step; AGENTS.md; roadmap rows EI-1..7; CHANGELOG; stale doc headers (D7).\n    78\tWithdrawn/reclassified: R1 withdrawn (behaviour matches stated policy); P1 by design (probe means \"serving\"; 401 must surface, not be waited out).\n    79\tEI-2 closed (audit premise disproved: the state store already fsyncs file and directory on every write; pinned). EI-3 partly done: plugin args mutation (I-AUTH-4) and the in-process OAuth refresh race (I-AUTH-5) were reproduced with failing tests and fixed. EI-1 decided (not a gap): the intent write stays fail-open because the failure is loud and fails operation units (see `docs/INVARIANTS.md`, Decided).\n    80\tNot done, recorded as residual risk with roadmap rows: (EI-3 and EI-4 are done: cross-process OAuth refresh I-AUTH-5, restore journal event, upgrade and doctor lock liveness I-LIFE-3), A5 duplicate Copilot headers (unverified), P4 tools-ignored flag and tools-ignored flag (EI-6 remainder; browser_click is now mutating), spine production hooks / E2 guards (EI-7), live-model runs of the change-cost tasks (EI-5) done 2026-11-18: base and branch tie at 37/50 (10 runs per cell); an earlier 14/25 vs 20/25 (5 runs per cell) did not replicate, so there is no evidence the prompt rule changes model behaviour; see `docs/evidence/change-cost-live-2026-11-18/README.md` (scenarios A-H in CERI remain mechanism-level).\n    81\tLessons: see `tasks/lessons.md` (process liveness via pgrep). A prompt addition changed context-budget tests: a 150-token rule broke `context_convergence`; shortened rather than retuned.\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t---\n    85\t(previous content of this file follows)\n    86\t\n    87\t# Compaction and task-continuity hardening (2026-10-13)\n    88\t\n    89\tWorktree `/home/mike/nexus-cc`, branch `feat/compaction-continuity` from `origin/main` a58f860.\n    90\t`~/nexus-code` (installed launcher target) is left untouched: it held foreign uncommitted edits written during this\n    91\tsession (instruction-precedence work, plus a partial unbounded-budget change), so this work is isolated.\n    92\t\n    93\tGateway reference (read-only): `/home/mike/Projects/aihost` fb1a2cd, deployed release t5820-gateway-b72a4f5.\n    94\t\n    95\t## A. Continuity without a step ceiling\n    96\t- [x] Default continuation unbounded (no 300-step / 120-min default); explicit operator limits still apply\n    97\t- [x] No \"step N of M, finish now\" notes unless the operator set a step limit\n    98\t- [x] spawn_subagent loop: progress-based, parent cancellation, no 8/15 cap\n    99\t- [x] team / work units: inherit unbounded continuation; work-unit capacity no longer defaults to 65536\n   100\t- [x] Persisted objective-scoped execution tracking in the ledger (bounded, loop evidence never evicted)\n   101\t- [x] Unstructured objective continued by \"continue\"-style follow-up keeps its tracking; new objective resets\n   102\t\n   103\t## B. State-aware repetition\n   104\t- [x] Action identity (canonical args), outcome identity (volatile tokens, duration_ms, exit_code), state identity (content + index + deps)\n   105\t- [x] Progress = new state / new information / new ledger state; not plan edits, reformatted args, identical writes\n   106\t- [x] Transient vs deterministic failures; polling backoff; unknown state reported as unknown\n   107\t- [x] (live finding) re-reads after compaction are re-acquisition / context thrash, not repetition\n   108\t\n   109\t## C. Durable compaction boundary\n   110\t- [x] Commit order: archive (fsync) → task state → session, synced; compaction ids named in each record\n   111\t- [x] Recovery: uncommitted archive entries filtered; torn lines reported; settled tool calls only\n   112\t- [x] Failures visible (CLI/TUI); turn stopped (PERSISTENCE_FAILED) on auto-commit failure\n   113\t- [x] /compact queued during work; ack + outcome; dedupe, bound, cancel, shutdown, turn-end; --llm too\n   114\t- [x] Thrash detection across steps (low-yield hold), separate from repetition\n   115\t- [x] (live finding) tracking record shared in place, never replaced mid-turn\n   116\t\n   117\t## D. Provider capabilities and token accounting\n   118\t- [x] Discover context/output/limits_version from /models (gateway, vLLM max_model_len); refresh on change\n   119\t- [x] Count via /v1/tokenize when advertised, with the exact outbound payload builder\n   120\t- [x] Sources: exact_admitted, exact_sampled_worker, gateway_conservative, client_estimate\n   121\t- [x] Strict counting opt-in; standalone defaults; headroom policy labelled as policy\n   122\t\n   123\t## Validation / deliverables\n   124\t- [x] Tests per area (65 new tests across 4 files); full `make test` on final snapshot (see review)\n   125\t- [x] Live local-inference multistep run across compaction boundaries (3 runs; run 3 completed)\n   126\t- [x] Operator + developer docs, acceptance ledger, gateway capability handoff\n   127\t\n   128\t## Review\n   129\t- Live runs found two real defects scripted tests had missed (re-reads after compaction stopped as loops; compaction\n   130\t  orphaning the live tracker) plus a wasted second count per step. All fixed with regression tests.\n   131\t- Not done: commit/merge (operator's decision), live standalone run against a non-gateway server, live capacity /\n   132\t  worker-change observation, `graphify update` (no graph in the worktree; the main checkout was not touched).\n   133\t\n   134\t# Output-truncation recovery (2026-10-14)\n   135\t\n   136\tBranch `fix/output-truncation-recovery` from main 1c3afbd. Trigger: live session `session_20261014_074807_hmo7` ended\n   137\t`FAILED / INFERENCE_FAILED (output_truncated/client)` at step 54 when one reply used the whole 8192-token output\n   138\tallowance inside a tool call (about 173 s of generation); output_truncated was always fatal to the turn.\n   139\t\n   140\t- [x] 1. Truncated reply → bounded retry: nothing from it runs; a Nexus note names the tool/path, the allowance, and asks\n   141\t      for the content in parts; the turn continues at the next step (new request id)\n   142\t- [x] 2. Bound: a second consecutive truncation ends the turn exactly as before; the truncated step counts as no progress\n   143\t- [x] 3. Prevention: write_file/edit_file descriptions say a reply's output is limited and long content goes in parts\n   144\t- [x] 4. Tests: truncated tool call → chunked write completes; two in a row → fails as before; truncated prose never\n   145\t      accepted as final; no tool from a truncated reply runs\n   146\t- [ ] Full `make test` on a snapshot; docs (USER_MANUAL / COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY) updated\n   147\t\n   148\t# Post-v1.1.3 housekeeping (2026-11-05)\n   149\t\n   150\tBranch `chore/housekeeping-post-v113` from main 46fd5045 (v1.1.3 stable, published).\n   151\t\n   152\t- [x] Root clutter (check-in scripts, session dumps, continuity-validation, stale root package-lock.json) moved to\n   153\t      `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/root-clutter/`; `.gitignore` now ignores `/nexus-session-*.json`\n   154\t- [x] 220 stale claims renamed `*.released-<UTC>` and logged; `GATEWAY` (codex-root, RC15 E5, 2026-10-31) left active\n   155\t- [x] Worktrees 875 → 137: 657 clean removed; 81 dirty archived to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/worktrees/`\n   156\t      (tracked.patch + untracked.tgz + meta.txt) then removed; 136 detached-HEAD trees kept (commits on no ref)\n   157\t- [x] Local branches 596 → 206: 364 merged into main deleted; 31 unmerged with a remote copy deleted\n   158\t- [x] Owner follow-up: kept only branches with roadmap/planning content not on main (`v1/docs-v11-layered-memory`,\n   159\t      `backup/agent-work-product-ae474637` with LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md) plus `v1/v113-plan`; the other 202 local branches\n   160\t      bundled to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/unmerged-branches.bundle` (tips in `branch-tips.txt`) then deleted\n   161\t- [x] Last stale claim (`GATEWAY`) released; no unreleased claims remain\n   162\t- [x] 4 stashes archived (`~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/stashes/`) and dropped; ~154 ancestor-merged remote branches deleted\n   163\t      (`v1/integration` is rule-protected and stays); 136 orphaned detached worktrees removed (22 dirty ones archived; all 118\n   164\t      distinct heads bundled in `orphan-heads.bundle`); missing orphan fixes recorded as v1.1.4 WP-1306 (local anchors `recovery/orphan-*`)\n   165\t- [x] Issue #69 (Harness2) review written: `docs/v1.1.4/HARNESS2-REVIEW.md` on PR #404 (WP-1307)\n   166\t- [ ] Open: 47 remote branches that are not ancestors of main (4 have merged PRs); issue #69 stays open until the write-up merges\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31703}},"started_at_ms":1795146961219,"completed_at_ms":1795146961220}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T03:56:01.342Z","ordinal":28962,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f718-d1bd-7053-b838-86a590536527","call_id":"call_b91a921a041b4bd593a40310d032fad4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    62\t| D7 | DOC | SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md header/line cites stale; ARCHITECTURE.md Rust file list stale; EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md header stale | L | correct; no append-only history |\n    63\tNot found/credited: reviewer cannot self-accept; failover authorization per endpoint; cancellation path; slash/protocol dispatch rejects unknown.\n    64\t\n    65\t### Merged execution order (correctness first; style last)\n    66\t1 U1,U2(+D5),U3,U4 (side effects/unknown outcome)  2 L1,L2,L3,E1 (state integrity)  3 R1,D6,D3,D2,D1 (acceptance + authorization)  4 P1..P4 (providers)  5 R2,R3 (review/agent guidance, existing contracts)  6 A1,A2,A4/A5,E2,E3,E4,D4 (invariant/consolidation with tests)  7 scenarios A..H in CERI fixture + diff_boundary eval tasks  8 INVARIANTS/rationale doc (code<->test<->rationale table, checked by a script like check_requirements) + roadmap rows + CHANGELOG  9 regression vs baseline, tsc, node 22/24 note.\n    67\tScenario plan (follow-up §11): A..H become CERI `multi_file_refactoring`/`scoped_implementation` fixture entries driven deterministically (diff_boundary + test commands on fixture repos); real-Nexus runs only if the gateway claim is available (reported separately from fixture-only results).\n    68\t\n    69\t## Review (measured 2026-11-17; nothing pushed or merged)\n    70\tBranch `v1/invariants-impl` (merged forward into `v1/invariants-audit`), based on origin/main 65c76b28; origin/main has since moved (e.g. #582), so a merge needs the owner's rebase/conflict pass (CHANGELOG, PLAN.md, agent.ts are the likely overlaps).\n    71\tRegression (all runs on this host, one at a time, throwaway HOME):\n    72\t- Clean base 65c76b28, Node 24: 4030 tests, 4014 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (`eval_version_probe_storage`: needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT`, only CI sets it).\n    73\t- Branch at b2418684 (before the last EI-3/EI-4/EI-7 changes), Node 24: 4082 tests, 4066 pass, 15 skipped, same single failure.\n    74\t- Branch at f7aa3919 (final), Node 24: 3441 tests in the completed segments, 3426 pass, same single failure; `compaction_continuity` timed out in the runner under host load (it also timed out in the first, untouched-base attempt) and passed alone: 34/34 in ~5 min. The branch adds no new failure.\n    75\t- Node 22.22.2 (nvm), final tree 91f69fb1 (code identical to f7aa3919; docs only since): 4089 tests, 4073 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (the same environment-only `eval_version_probe_storage`), no timeouts. An earlier Node 22 run on b2418684 had three files time out under host load (load average above 20 from other processes); each passed alone.\n    76\t- `tsc` clean; `scripts/check_invariants.mjs` and the leak-guard ratchet pass. CI matrix (test-matrix 22/24, linux-x86_64) not run: GitHub only.\n    77\tDone (rule ids in `docs/INVARIANTS.md`): U1 I-EFFECT-1; U2/D5 I-EFFECT-2; U3/U4 I-EFFECT-3; L1/L2/L3/E1/D4 I-LIFE-1; D3 I-AUTH-1; D1 I-AUTH-2 (reproduced at runtime first: every MCP call returned FAIL-001); A4 I-AUTH-3; D6 I-ACCEPT-1; E4 I-ACCEPT-2; P2 I-PROVIDER-1; P3 I-PROVIDER-2; D2 I-EFFECT-4; R2 I-CHANGE-2; R3 I-CHANGE-1; E3 one success predicate; A2 durable private writers; scenarios A-H (mechanism-level); INVARIANTS.md + checker + CI step; AGENTS.md; roadmap rows EI-1..7; CHANGELOG; stale doc headers (D7).\n    78\tWithdrawn/reclassified: R1 withdrawn (behaviour matches stated policy); P1 by design (probe means \"serving\"; 401 must surface, not be waited out).\n    79\tEI-2 closed (audit premise disproved: the state store already fsyncs file and directory on every write; pinned). EI-3 partly done: plugin args mutation (I-AUTH-4) and the in-process OAuth refresh race (I-AUTH-5) were reproduced with failing tests and fixed. EI-1 decided (not a gap): the intent write stays fail-open because the failure is loud and fails operation units (see `docs/INVARIANTS.md`, Decided).\n    80\tNot done, recorded as residual risk with roadmap rows: (EI-3 and EI-4 are done: cross-process OAuth refresh I-AUTH-5, restore journal event, upgrade and doctor lock liveness I-LIFE-3), A5 duplicate Copilot headers (unverified), P4 tools-ignored flag and tools-ignored flag (EI-6 remainder; browser_click is now mutating), spine production hooks / E2 guards (EI-7), live-model runs of the change-cost tasks (EI-5) done 2026-11-18: base and branch tie at 37/50 (10 runs per cell); an earlier 14/25 vs 20/25 (5 runs per cell) did not replicate, so there is no evidence the prompt rule changes model behaviour; see `docs/evidence/change-cost-live-2026-11-18/README.md` (scenarios A-H in CERI remain mechanism-level).\n    81\tLessons: see `tasks/lessons.md` (process liveness via pgrep). A prompt addition changed context-budget tests: a 150-token rule broke `context_convergence`; shortened rather than retuned.\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t---\n    85\t(previous content of this file follows)\n    86\t\n    87\t# Compaction and task-continuity hardening (2026-10-13)\n    88\t\n    89\tWorktree `/home/mike/nexus-cc`, branch `feat/compaction-continuity` from `origin/main` a58f860.\n    90\t`~/nexus-code` (installed launcher target) is left untouched: it held foreign uncommitted edits written during this\n    91\tsession (instruction-precedence work, plus a partial unbounded-budget change), so this work is isolated.\n    92\t\n    93\tGateway reference (read-only): `/home/mike/Projects/aihost` fb1a2cd, deployed release t5820-gateway-b72a4f5.\n    94\t\n    95\t## A. Continuity without a step ceiling\n    96\t- [x] Default continuation unbounded (no 300-step / 120-min default); explicit operator limits still apply\n    97\t- [x] No \"step N of M, finish now\" notes unless the operator set a step limit\n    98\t- [x] spawn_subagent loop: progress-based, parent cancellation, no 8/15 cap\n    99\t- [x] team / work units: inherit unbounded continuation; work-unit capacity no longer defaults to 65536\n   100\t- [x] Persisted objective-scoped execution tracking in the ledger (bounded, loop evidence never evicted)\n   101\t- [x] Unstructured objective continued by \"continue\"-style follow-up keeps its tracking; new objective resets\n   102\t\n   103\t## B. State-aware repetition\n   104\t- [x] Action identity (canonical args), outcome identity (volatile tokens, duration_ms, exit_code), state identity (content + index + deps)\n   105\t- [x] Progress = new state / new information / new ledger state; not plan edits, reformatted args, identical writes\n   106\t- [x] Transient vs deterministic failures; polling backoff; unknown state reported as unknown\n   107\t- [x] (live finding) re-reads after compaction are re-acquisition / context thrash, not repetition\n   108\t\n   109\t## C. Durable compaction boundary\n   110\t- [x] Commit order: archive (fsync) → task state → session, synced; compaction ids named in each record\n   111\t- [x] Recovery: uncommitted archive entries filtered; torn lines reported; settled tool calls only\n   112\t- [x] Failures visible (CLI/TUI); turn stopped (PERSISTENCE_FAILED) on auto-commit failure\n   113\t- [x] /compact queued during work; ack + outcome; dedupe, bound, cancel, shutdown, turn-end; --llm too\n   114\t- [x] Thrash detection across steps (low-yield hold), separate from repetition\n   115\t- [x] (live finding) tracking record shared in place, never replaced mid-turn\n   116\t\n   117\t## D. Provider capabilities and token accounting\n   118\t- [x] Discover context/output/limits_version from /models (gateway, vLLM max_model_len); refresh on change\n   119\t- [x] Count via /v1/tokenize when advertised, with the exact outbound payload builder\n   120\t- [x] Sources: exact_admitted, exact_sampled_worker, gateway_conservative, client_estimate\n   121\t- [x] Strict counting opt-in; standalone defaults; headroom policy labelled as policy\n   122\t\n   123\t## Validation / deliverables\n   124\t- [x] Tests per area (65 new tests across 4 files); full `make test` on final snapshot (see review)\n   125\t- [x] Live local-inference multistep run across compaction boundaries (3 runs; run 3 completed)\n   126\t- [x] Operator + developer docs, acceptance ledger, gateway capability handoff\n   127\t\n   128\t## Review\n   129\t- Live runs found two real defects scripted tests had missed (re-reads after compaction stopped as loops; compaction\n   130\t  orphaning the live tracker) plus a wasted second count per step. All fixed with regression tests.\n   131\t- Not done: commit/merge (operator's decision), live standalone run against a non-gateway server, live capacity /\n   132\t  worker-change observation, `graphify update` (no graph in the worktree; the main checkout was not touched).\n   133\t\n   134\t# Output-truncation recovery (2026-10-14)\n   135\t\n   136\tBranch `fix/output-truncation-recovery` from main 1c3afbd. Trigger: live session `session_20261014_074807_hmo7` ended\n   137\t`FAILED / INFERENCE_FAILED (output_truncated/client)` at step 54 when one reply used the whole 8192-token output\n   138\tallowance inside a tool call (about 173 s of generation); output_truncated was always fatal to the turn.\n   139\t\n   140\t- [x] 1. Truncated reply → bounded retry: nothing from it runs; a Nexus note names the tool/path, the allowance, and asks\n   141\t      for the content in parts; the turn continues at the next step (new request id)\n   142\t- [x] 2. Bound: a second consecutive truncation ends the turn exactly as before; the truncated step counts as no progress\n   143\t- [x] 3. Prevention: write_file/edit_file descriptions say a reply's output is limited and long content goes in parts\n   144\t- [x] 4. Tests: truncated tool call → chunked write completes; two in a row → fails as before; truncated prose never\n   145\t      accepted as final; no tool from a truncated reply runs\n   146\t- [ ] Full `make test` on a snapshot; docs (USER_MANUAL / COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY) updated\n   147\t\n   148\t# Post-v1.1.3 housekeeping (2026-11-05)\n   149\t\n   150\tBranch `chore/housekeeping-post-v113` from main 46fd5045 (v1.1.3 stable, published).\n   151\t\n   152\t- [x] Root clutter (check-in scripts, session dumps, continuity-validation, stale root package-lock.json) moved to\n   153\t      `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/root-clutter/`; `.gitignore` now ignores `/nexus-session-*.json`\n   154\t- [x] 220 stale claims renamed `*.released-<UTC>` and logged; `GATEWAY` (codex-root, RC15 E5, 2026-10-31) left active\n   155\t- [x] Worktrees 875 → 137: 657 clean removed; 81 dirty archived to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/worktrees/`\n   156\t      (tracked.patch + untracked.tgz + meta.txt) then removed; 136 detached-HEAD trees kept (commits on no ref)\n   157\t- [x] Local branches 596 → 206: 364 merged into main deleted; 31 unmerged with a remote copy deleted\n   158\t- [x] Owner follow-up: kept only branches with roadmap/planning content not on main (`v1/docs-v11-layered-memory`,\n   159\t      `backup/agent-work-product-ae474637` with LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md) plus `v1/v113-plan`; the other 202 local branches\n   160\t      bundled to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/unmerged-branches.bundle` (tips in `branch-tips.txt`) then deleted\n   161\t- [x] Last stale claim (`GATEWAY`) released; no unreleased claims remain\n   162\t- [x] 4 stashes archived (`~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/stashes/`) and dropped; ~154 ancestor-merged remote branches deleted\n   163\t      (`v1/integration` is rule-protected and stays); 136 orphaned detached worktrees removed (22 dirty ones archived; all 118\n   164\t      distinct heads bundled in `orphan-heads.bundle`); missing orphan fixes recorded as v1.1.4 WP-1306 (local anchors `recovery/orphan-*`)\n   165\t- [x] Issue #69 (Harness2) review written: `docs/v1.1.4/HARNESS2-REVIEW.md` on PR #404 (WP-1307)\n   166\t- [ ] Open: 47 remote branches that are not ancestors of main (4 have merged PRs); issue #69 stays open until the write-up merges\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f712-aaf3-7db1-9f93-ddce93b124cb","create_time":1795146961.3418896}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":12778,"sampled_through_sequence":12774,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
