ll finds the originals\");\ncli/test/readonly_home.test.ts:35:describe(\"ACC-SAFE-04 & REQ-SEC-104: Read-only HOME masking and workspace path confinement\", () => {\ncli/test/spine.test.ts:369:    // The 36 baseline capabilities, read_findings, read_archive and enable_tools (every agent's), and the top-level agent's own\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/before_compaction.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/after_resume.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/after_tool_call.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ndocs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:110:  `run_tests`), completion attempts, Nexus's memory reads (`read_findings`, `read_objective`, `read_archive`), any read\ndocs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:216:  the covered ids; that compaction's archived messages are not served to `read_archive`. The saved conversation is used\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/before_resume.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/first_turn.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/retry_note.json:29:      \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/retry_note.json:87:      \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/retry_note.json:161:      \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/retry_note.json:237:      \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/fixtures/request_shape/after_compaction.json:28:    \"read_archive\",\ncli/test/recover_worktree_conversation.test.ts:132:    const readArchive = resumed.getSpine().getHandler(\"read_archive\");\ncli/test/recover_worktree_conversation.test.ts:133:    assert.ok(readArchive, \"read_archive handler was not registered\");\ncli/src/core/agent_support.ts:208:/** Archived originals kept searchable with read_archive (oldest dropped first). */\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:2: * CX-4: old tool results above a token threshold are replaced, in the request only, by a marker carrying a content id;\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:3: * the full output stays in the conversation and the archive and resolves with read_archive. Opt-in\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:4: * (NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS); the pinned ledger, findings and the independent reviewer's evidence are never masked.\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:54:    for (const name of [\"read_archive\", \"read_findings\", \"read_objective\"]) {\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:66:    assert.equal(maskThresholdFromEnv({ NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS: \"abc\" }), undefined);\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:67:    assert.equal(maskThresholdFromEnv({ NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS: \"0\" }), undefined);\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:68:    assert.equal(maskThresholdFromEnv({ NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS: \"250\" }), 250);\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:79:  test(\"the independent reviewer's evidence package does not change with masking, and the review module does not depend on it\", () => {\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:94:    previousMask = process.env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS;\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:100:    if (previousMask === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS; else process.env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS = previousMask;\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:112:    if (mask === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS; else process.env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS = mask;\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:122:        return { kind: \"tools\", calls: [{ name: \"read_archive\", args: { query: `tool-output:${id}` } }] };\ncli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts:148:    assert.ok(retrieved && retrieved.includes(\"line 0 of the big output\"), \"read_archive returned the full output by id\");\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:2: * CX-4: tool-output masking. In the messages a request carries, an old tool result above a token threshold is replaced by\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:4: * resolves with `read_archive` (\"tool-output:<id>\").\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:10: *  - retrieval results (read_archive, read_findings, read_objective) are never masked, so a retrieval is not undone;\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:13: * Opt-in: NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS=<n> (a positive integer). Unset, 0 or invalid leaves requests unchanged.\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:20:const NEVER_MASKED = new Set([\"read_archive\", \"read_findings\", \"read_objective\"]);\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:30:  const raw = env.NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS?.trim();\ncli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts:51:    return { ...message, content: `${MASK_MARKER_PREFIX} ${message.name ?? \"tool\"} returned ~${tokens} tokens (${text.length} characters), which you have already acted on. Full output: read_archive with query \"tool-output:${maskedOutputId(text)}\". Begins: ${preview}…]` };\ncli/test/approval_policy.test.ts:33:  read_findings: \"internal\", read_archive: \"internal\", enable_tools: \"internal\",\ncli/test/context_convergence.test.ts:1645:  test(\"archive: what compaction replaced is searchable with read_archive, verbatim and bounded\", async () => {\ncli/test/context_convergence.test.ts:1671:      assert.ok(agent.getEffectiveTools().some((t) => t.function.name === \"read_archive\"));\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:187:          { invocationId: `archive_${marker}`, taskId: info.taskId, actor: \"agent\", executionDomain: \"agent_orchestration\", toolName: \"read_archive\", args: { query: marker } },\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:190:        assert.equal(result.success, true, `read_archive succeeds for ${marker}`);\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:526:  test(\"ACC-CONT-03: work unit compaction writes archive lines and read_archive returns originals after resume\", async () => {\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:573:        // read_archive on resumed agent returns the original replaced messages\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:575:          { invocationId: \"call_archive\", taskId, actor: \"agent\", executionDomain: \"agent_orchestration\", toolName: \"read_archive\", args: { query: \"impl.txt\" } },\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:579:        assert.ok(readResult.output.length > 0, \"read_archive must return archived originals\");\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:372:These stop conditions protect implementation agents from improvising architecture or masking underlying failures.\ncli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:362:  \"read_findings\", \"read_objective\", \"read_archive\", \"git_status\", \"git_diff\", \"git_log\", \"semantic_search\",\ncli/src/agent.ts:333:  /** Every original compaction replaced in this conversation (bounded), searchable with read_archive. */\ncli/src/agent.ts:2150:    // CX-4: old tool results the model already acted on are masked last, so presence checks above see the stored ones.\ncli/src/agent.ts:3072:      if (!key || !wanted.has(key) || key.startsWith(\"read_findings \") || key.startsWith(\"read_objective \") || key.startsWith(\"read_archive \") || pending.some((item) => item.key === key) || !text || text.startsWith(\"Error executing \")) return;\ncli/src/agent.ts:3489:  /** A resumed conversation's archived originals (from the session's archive file), so read_archive still finds them. */\ncli/src/core/findings.ts:213:  id: \"orchestrate_read_archive\",\ncli/src/core/findings.ts:214:  modelToolName: \"read_archive\",\ncli/src/core/findings.ts:223:      name: \"read_archive\",\ncli/src/core/findings.ts:240:/** What read_archive returns for `args` from the archived (compacted-away) messages, oldest first. */\ncli/src/core/findings.ts:243:  if (!query) return { ok: false, text: \"read_archive needs a query.\" };\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts:771:  this.spine.registerHandler(\"read_archive\", async (args: any) => {\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts:772:    // CX-4: \"tool-output:<id>\" names a masked tool result; it resolves to the full output (live conversation, then archive).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:76:- Read-only HOME masking.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:120:### 5.4 Read-only HOME masking\ndocs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md:42:| Compaction | Cline: append-only transcript, compaction state stored separately and hash-validated on resume (`sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`). Gemini CLI: probe verification and tool-output masking (`chatCompressionService.ts:770`, `toolOutputMaskingService.ts:25`). opencode: background precompute with a headroom budget (`session/compaction.ts:127-173`) | `/compact [--llm]`; summary enters a system message unlabelled (G-SI-6) |\ndocs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md:123:| GA-18 | Compaction: unlabelled summaries, no integrity binding, no probe, no tool-output masking, no precompute | §2.2; G-SI-6 | P1 | CX-1…CX-4 |\ndocs/v1.2.1/GAP_ANALYSIS.md:150:| GA-45 | `search_code`, `list_dir` and `file_tree` results: a capped result is indistinguishable from an exact one (`total_matches: matches.len()`, `search.rs:189,264,361`), `line_text` is the whole trimmed line (`search.rs:175`, a 200 KB minified line is returned whole), and no `require_git(false)` so `.gitignore` does not apply in a non-git workspace (`grep require_git core/src`: none) | `tools_persistence.md` T16 (REPRODUCED DEFECT on `3727938`); `context.md` CTX-04 (the same absence-from-truncated-output class, whose shell-limiter part is fixed) | P2 | no unit (nearest CX-4) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1.1/CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT-20261028/README.md:80:  retrieval tool; `read_archive`/`read_findings` remain the only recall paths.\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:107:| CX-4 | Tool-output masking above a token threshold, with the full output retrievable by id (references: Gemini CLI `toolOutputMaskingService.ts:25`, Cline cached tool results). A masked output stays in the evidence store, and the independent reviewer's package (requirements, scope, diff, verifier receipts) does not depend on conversation context, so masking cannot remove evidence (read in `independent_review.ts`, 2026-11-15) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves; the reviewer package is identical before and after masking | S | P2 | Note 2026-11-18: PARTIAL, opt-in. Done: `NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS=<n>` masks, in the request only, a tool result above n estimated tokens once the model has acted on it (a later assistant message exists); the marker names a content id and the full output resolves with `read_archive` query `tool-output:<id>` (live conversation, then archive). Never masked: results not yet acted on, `read_archive`/`read_findings`/`read_objective` results, the pinned ledger, findings and durable records (system messages). Stored conversation and sessions are unchanged. `cli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts`, `cli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts` (request-shape marker, id resolves, ledger intact, off by default). The reviewer package is built from the diff and verifier receipts (`operation_runner_execution.ts` `reviewEvidence`), not the conversation, and the review module does not import masking; the test pins that, but it is a structural guard, not an end-to-end review run. Decision: default off, because safe-by-default would need a measured threshold on real tasks (masking can cost the model a retrieval step); a retrieved output enters the conversation whole and is not masked again. Not done: a dedicated id-read tool (the existing archive tool is reused), a default threshold, masking measured on the eval set.\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:188:Phase 3 (v1.2.2): native protocols PR-6 (Gemini), PR-7 (Bedrock), PR-8 (Vertex), PR-10; CS-9, CS-10, VC-8, RD-7 (added 2026-11-15 from the old-backlog review); MQ-7 slices D, E, F, G; RD-1 (macOS arm64; D6 default is Linux x86_64 only, so this waits for a decision), MT-1, MT-2, VC-2, VC-3, VC-6, VC-7, CX-4, CX-6, RD-2, RD-5, RD-6, CS-5, CS-6, PC-4, PC-5, PC-6, MQ-8 (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2), VC-10 (gated on a larger evaluation).\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:58:1. **Workspace path jail (file tools).** The Rust file tools (read, write, edit, delete, list, search) canonicalize every path against the workspace root and reject `..`, absolute paths and symlink escapes, rechecking the opened descriptor. *Limit:* for `run_command`, path protection is advisory. Host commands have the user's filesystem access unless the sandbox (`--sandbox`) or read-only HOME masking (`--read-only` with `bwrap`) is enabled.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:109:- When running in `--read-only` mode with `bwrap` container sandboxing, `$HOME` is mounted with `--tmpfs $HOME`, completely masking `~/.ssh`, shell profiles, and user dotfiles from `run_command`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:38:- a. Compaction happens in memory only, with no archive. The next `persistProgress` writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines. The originals are lost, and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume. This contradicts `docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:150:| ACC-CONT-03 | Operation rig with a small `contextLimit` forcing compaction; SIGKILL; resume. `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the compaction id, and `read_archive` returns the originals. |\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:21:| CX-4 | Opt-in masking (`NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS`) with ids resolved through `read_archive` | A default threshold (not shown safe); a dedicated id-read tool; measurement of masking on real tasks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:26:| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:114:- Nexus memory reads (`read_findings`, `read_objective`, `read_archive`);\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:157:    # Subtest: ACC-CONT-03: work unit compaction writes archive lines and read_archive returns originals after resume\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:158:    ok 7 - ACC-CONT-03: work unit compaction writes archive lines and read_archive returns originals after resume\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RECOVER-WORKTREE-CONVERSATION-20261026/README.md:60:  archived message is restored and searchable through the resumed agent's `read_archive` handler. `npm ci --prefix cli`,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md:76:- The ACC-CONT-03 test exercises exactly this on a depth-1 work-unit agent and asserts `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the compaction id and `read_archive` returns originals after recovery (`cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:359-419`, construction at :374, assertions at :396-412).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md:95:> | ACC-CONT-03 | Operation rig with a small `contextLimit` **forcing compaction**; **SIGKILL**; resume. `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the compaction id, and `read_archive` returns the originals. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md:105:**Does the evidence cover the AC as written?** No. Element-by-element: (1) \"small contextLimit **forcing** compaction\" — not covered on a work unit (manual trigger); pressure-forced auto compaction is exercised only on a depth-0 agent with a mocked client, asserting admission state (`state=auto_compacted`) rather than durable records (`cli/test/context_auto_compaction.test.ts:73-129`). (2) \"SIGKILL\" — covered only at depth 0, with operator-invoked compaction. (3) \"resume + history id + read_archive originals\" — covered on the work unit (`durable_continuity.test.ts:396-412`) but without (1) and (2). Mitigation, as prep noted: all triggers funnel through the single `commitCompaction` (`agent.ts:3328`), so the commit machinery is shared; the gap is in the trigger/boundary path, not the commit logic.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md:107:**The missing test.** Extend the operationRig (`durable_continuity.test.ts:152-178`): small `contextLimit` with a gateway returning large tool outputs so the **auto** path (`agent.ts:3051`, `trigger: \"auto\"`) commits compaction mid-turn on the depth-1 `durable: true` work-unit agent; kill the agent process (crash-child pattern as in `compaction_continuity.test.ts:536-541`) at the commit boundary; resume via a fresh executor + `recoverFromTaskState`; assert `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the auto compaction id, `read_archive` returns the originals, and no action is replayed (cf. the no-replay assertion `compaction_continuity.test.ts:566`). This requires running the suite (SUITE claim) → **deferred to execution; the test specification itself is statically closable now.**\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/review-prep.md:128:- **P7.** Tests are substantive, not weak: ACC-CONT-01 asserts codeword presence in the second request + taskId equality (durable_continuity.test.ts:282-309); ACC-CONT-03 asserts `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the compaction id and `read_archive` returns originals after recovery (359-419); ACC-CONT-05 asserts exactly one task file and stats ≥ gateway requests (535-576); real SIGKILL child at 3 commit-boundary points asserting record consistency and no replay (compaction_continuity.test.ts:533-573); persistence-failure truthfulness incl. ENOSPC/EACCES injection (433+). (VQ-12, VQ-14)\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/dispositions.md:23:- **Disposition: implemented (`PLAN-04 PR-4g`, commit `79ed3ce`).** Added `work_unit_pressure` mode in `cli/test/helpers/compaction_crash_child.ts` and `cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts` (`\"ACC-CONT-03: pressure compaction of a work unit survives SIGKILL and restores archived markers\"`): runs a work unit through `AgentWorkUnitExecutor` / `driveOperation` with `contextLimit: 18_000` forcing automatic pressure compaction during the work-unit turn, kills the child with `SIGKILL` immediately after `<task>.history.jsonl` and task state are committed, and verifies in a fresh resumed work-unit agent (`recoverFromTaskState`) that `<task>.history.jsonl` contains the compaction id and `read_archive` returns the archived originals.\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:12:  archive, and checkpointed in a fixed order; `read_archive` returns originals after resume.\ndocs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md:40:   local, opt-in index. Retrieval is evidence-returning (`read_archive`, `read_findings` semantics), never a silent\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:48:| 9 | Read-only HOME masking: bwrap `--tmpfs $HOME --ro-bind <ws> <ws>`. Without bwrap, path-confine the allowlisted commands (reject `~`, `$`, absolute paths, and `..` that escapes). | `sandbox.ts:131-181`; `core/authority.ts:44-136` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:61:5. **PR-1e** (tasks 9-11): read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:95:| Work-unit compaction loss (AGT-02) | Operation rig (durable_continuity.test.ts `operationRig`) with `contextLimit` small enough to force compaction; kill and resume; assert `<task>.history.jsonl` has the compaction id and `read_archive` returns originals. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:106:| AGT-R2 | Every durable unit (depth-0 turn and work unit) commits compactions via archive→switch→records and stops on non-durable compaction; only in-turn subagents are memory-only. | continuity (AGT-02) | BLOCKER | Work-unit compaction + kill + resume test asserting archive lines and `read_archive`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:54:- Use the `operationRig` with a small `contextLimit`, SIGKILL, then resume. Assert the archive lines and `read_archive` (ACC-CONT-03), plus loop persistence (ACC-CONT-04).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":42593}},"started_at_ms":1795147627957,"completed_at_ms":1795147627958}}
