{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:08:55.143Z","ordinal":29417,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f712-aaf3-7db1-9f93-ddce93b124cb","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_05793ea695c2aa2c016affc7d1c3b487d2b92afe68473ce35e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m continuing the v1.2.x work; it isn’t complete yet.\n\n- Published [PR #643](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/643) to pin the CS-6 language-server toolchains. Its hosted run passed all 10 real-server tests with no skips or failures. Its required PR checks are still running.\n- PRs [#642](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/642) and [#639](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/639) also still need their required checks to finish before merging.\n- Verified the existing CX-7 import tests pass: 10 passed. The Claude candidate’s provider tool-call warning tests also pass: 18 passed.\n- I tried applying Claude’s invariant-map documentation separately, but its checker fails against current `main` because the implementation and tests it references are missing. I aborted that change rather than publish a broken check; reconciling the remaining candidate work is still outstanding.\n- The local `main` checkout remains clean and synced. I removed the temporary worktree from that failed cherry-pick and kept the active and held-out worktrees intact.\n\nI’ve sent you two decision questions about cost-dependent work and worktree-bound session forks. Meanwhile I’ll keep advancing work that doesn’t depend on those answers. No second maintainer is required."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"content_token_count":291,"started_at_ms":1795147729810,"completed_at_ms":1795147735143}}
