{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:19:14.539Z","ordinal":29734,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f72c-56d0-7a60-917e-bc2e070d3543","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4de7e430-4cbb-4bb3-8243-753a2a9c1e77","process_id":"48565","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show 934c5fd8:docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md | sed -n '10,60p'; gh pr diff 639 | rg -n -C 4 'VC-6|CX-7|RD-6|MQ-7|forkedFrom|worktree refusal' | head -120"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show 934c5fd8:docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md | sed -n '10,60p'; gh pr diff 639 | rg -n -C 4 'VC-6|CX-7|RD-6|MQ-7|forkedFrom|worktree refusal' | head -120"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"fatal: invalid object name '934c5fd8'.\n17-@@ -16,15 +16,15 @@ What the v1.2.1 plan ([`docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md`](../v1.2.1/PLAN.md)) did not finish\n18- | Unit | Done in v1.2.1 / since | Left |\n19- |---|---|---|\n20- | VC-2 | Operator-authorised regression obligations (`/requirements obligate|minimise|retire|reference`), replay recording, completion gated on unmet obligations, weakening-edit recording for file tools and the shell; exact-test result binding in the verifier output | Still open: a shell edit to a test file larger than 64 KiB, or outside the 20000-entry scan, is not recorded; weakening is recorded, never blocked. Runner output can still be fabricated by a workspace-controlled test command, so an output line is evidence of a report, not proof the test body executed. |\n21:-| VC-6 | Baseline for untouched callers, shell-changed files, `go vet`, pyright and mypy, `UNAVAILABLE` for a missing tool | One check runs per project (tsc, then cargo, go, python); a resumed task has no baseline; cargo is excluded from the baseline as not cheap |\n22:+| VC-6 | **Done for configured project coverage**: every discovered TypeScript, Rust, Go, and configured Python typecheck project is checked; missing configured tools report `UNAVAILABLE`; baseline deltas distinguish introduced from pre-existing diagnostics. Evidence: PR #631 and `cli/test/vc6_typecheck_gaps.test.ts` (discovery, multiple configs, bounded discovery, nested Rust, unavailable tools, shell changes). | Still open: resumed tasks do not retain a trustworthy pre-change typecheck baseline; Cargo is excluded from the baseline run because it is not cheap. These limits must remain visible in the verifier result and completion policy. |\n23- | VC-9 | Audit with file:line for 14 paths; BLOCKED/NEEDS_INPUT with a machine-readable question and `--answer` resume for tool approvals, verification-file edits and the verifier or type-check at completion; a delegated subagent's question is returned to the parent and ends the parent's headless run BLOCKED/NEEDS_INPUT (`spawn_subagent` only); the requirement-verifier approval has its own test | A requirement marked blocked (changes the `REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE` contract and needs a free-text answer); an unresolved steering conflict (sidecar protocol decision) |\n24- | CX-4 | Opt-in masking (`NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS`) with ids resolved through `read_archive` | A default threshold (not shown safe); a dedicated id-read tool; measurement of masking on real tasks |\n25- | CX-6 | Opt-in Anthropic cache breakpoints (`NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`, provider declares `promptCache: \"anthropic\"`) and a cached-token share in the usage summary | Verification against the live Anthropic API; default-on; Bedrock `cachePoint`; declaring the capability from an operator `providers.json`; a share column in the provider matrix doc |\n26:-| CX-7 | `@path` imports for AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CODEX.md and .nexusrules (trusted workspaces, real-path containment) | Loading more than the first non-empty instruction file; `~/` and absolute imports |\n27:-| RD-6 | `SessionManager.forkSession` and `/fork [n]` (source never mutated, compaction archive verified on resume); `--fork-session`/`--fork-at` on `run`, `repl` and the top level; a worktree-bound session is refused | Carrying a worktree binding into a fork (today it is refused: a fork would share the checkout; needs a decision on making a second checkout); `forkedFrom` is lost once the fork's own turns are saved; the REPL `/fork` worktree refusal has no automated test (the `--fork-session` flag is done: run, repl, top level) |\n28:+| CX-7 | **Done**: trusted workspaces load all non-empty instruction files in precedence order; imports are constrained by real-path containment; `~/` and absolute paths are supported when they resolve inside the trusted workspace. Evidence: `cli/test/project_rules_imports.test.ts` (including untrusted-workspace, cycle, depth-bound, and symlink escape cases). |\n29:+| RD-6 | **Done for the accepted single-checkout fork behavior**: `SessionManager.forkSession` and `/fork [n]` preserve the source and compaction integrity; `--fork-session`/`--fork-at` work on `run`, `repl`, and top-level launch; worktree-bound forks are refused before creating or saving a fork. `forkedFrom` is persisted on later session saves. Evidence: `cli/test/session_fork.test.ts` and `cli/test/session_fork_start.test.ts`, including the REPL `/fork` worktree-refusal test. | Carrying a worktree binding would require creating a second checkout; this remains an owner design decision and is not required for the safe refusal behavior. |\n30- | CS-6 | Test `cli/test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts`, weekly non-required workflow `lsp-real-servers.yml`, `docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md`; typescript-language-server and pyright validated locally (pass; mutation-checked); fixed the missing `--stdio` for TS/JS/Python | The workflow has not yet run on a hosted runner; rust-analyzer and gopls cases are written but have run nowhere (not installed on the dev host), so treat them as unvalidated; hover, definition, the trust and sandbox gates and multi-file projects are not exercised against real servers; versions of rust-analyzer and gopls are not pinned by the test |\n31- | MT-3 | One `redactPlain` and one `safeTerminal` use in place of 7 and 3 inline copies (part 1); part 2: a characterization test pins 23 variants over a shared corpus, `formatSafeSidecarText` now calls `safeTerminal`, and every remaining variant has a row with the reason it differs in `docs/v1.2.1/REDACTION_VARIANTS.md` | Nothing planned. The audit found only one more behaviour-preserving collapse; the rest differ in bytes (escape stripping, classifier or no classifier, control handling order, credential-key replacement). Module-private variants (`ceri` `redactedJson`, `safeTerminalText`, `flat`, `redactDeep`) are not in the characterization test |\n32:-| MQ-7 | Slices B and C; D–G implemented in PR #627 (pending review and CI) | D (installed-evaluator adapter), E (request-context manifests), F (recovery reference checker), G (bounded campaigns) are available for review; see PR #627. |\n33:+| MQ-7 | **Done**: slices B–G are implemented and merged in PR #627. Slices D (installed-evaluator binding), E (request-context manifests), F (recovery-reference integrity), and G (bounded campaigns) have focused coverage in `cli/test/ceri_mq7dg.test.ts`; B/C coverage is in `cli/test/ceri_mq7bc.test.ts`. | No remaining v1.2.2 implementation item identified in this unit. |\n34- | CS-11 | Deterministic loop-pattern transcripts against the real agent turn and the measured table in `docs/LOOP_PATTERNS.md`; the pattern 2b gap (a command failing with only volatile text changing) closed by context-anchored volatile-text patterns, measured on an 86-pair labelled corpus (same-failure merged 6 of 38 to 34 of 38, different-failure merged 0 of 48 before and after) | Four same-failure pairs with no context word to anchor on (digit-less random suffix, unanchored counter, queue depth, short sha), left unmerged on purpose |\n35- | WM-3 | All five gateway aliases measured (single runs) | A reasoning-aware pass rule for aliases with reasoning off (the runner marks them `passed: false` for the hybrid-reasoning check); repeats, to see run-to-run variation |\n36- \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":665872074}},"started_at_ms":1795148353872,"completed_at_ms":1795148354539}}
