t-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:94:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:114:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:134:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json:41:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json:62:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json:83:        \"cachedInputTokens\": 0,\nV1_RC15_PROVIDER_VERIFY_20261031.released-20261105T142659Z\nV1_RC10_CHATGPT_PROVIDER_EVIDENCE_20261028.released-20261105T142659Z\nSEC_CODEQL_PROVIDER_CLI_REDACTION.released-20261105T142659Z\nV1_DEFECT_PROVIDER_CLI_ENDPOINT_REDACTION.released-20261105T142659Z\nV1_RC11_E5_PROVIDER_EVIDENCE.released-20261105T142659Z\nV1_DEFECT_PROVIDER_CACHE_ORIGIN.released-20261105T142659Z\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":42963}},"started_at_ms":1795148408197,"completed_at_ms":1795148408197}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:20:08.328Z","ordinal":29767,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f72e-e608-77f1-b8d5-5c83e065739c","call_id":"call_f1c3fc67e37b46d5966244685c27e85c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 19562)\nTotal output lines: 126\n\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:107:| CX-4 | Tool-output masking above a token threshold, with the full output retrievable by id (references: Gemini CLI `toolOutputMaskingService.ts:25`, Cline cached tool results). A masked output stays in the evidence store, and the independent reviewer's package (requirements, scope, diff, verifier receipts) does not depend on conversation context, so masking cannot remove evidence (read in `independent_review.ts`, 2026-11-15) | request-shape snapshot shows the mask marker; the id resolves; the reviewer package is identical before and after masking | S | P2 | Note 2026-11-18: PARTIAL, opt-in. Done: `NEXUS_TOOL_OUTPUT_MASK_TOKENS=<n>` masks, in the request only, a tool result above n estimated tokens once the model has acted on it (a later assistant message exists); the marker names a content id and the full output resolves with `read_archive` query `tool-output:<id>` (live conversation, then archive). Never masked: results not yet acted on, `read_archive`/`read_findings`/`read_objective` results, the pinned ledger, findings and durable records (system messages). Stored conversation and sessions are unchanged. `cli/src/core/tool_output_mask.ts`, `cli/test/tool_output_mask.test.ts` (request-shape marker, id resolves, ledger intact, off by default). The reviewer package is built from the diff and verifier receipts (`operation_runner_execution.ts` `reviewEvidence`), not the conversation, and the review module does not import masking; the test pins that, but it is a structural guard, not an end-to-end review run. Decision: default off, because safe-by-default would need a measured threshold on real tasks (masking can cost the model a retrieval step); a retrieved output enters the conversation whole and is not masked again. Not done: a dedicated id-read tool (the existing archive tool is reused), a default threshold, masking measured on the eval set.\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:109:| CX-6 | Prompt caching: request cache hints for providers that support them; measure cached-token share | share reported in the matrix | S | P2 | Note 2026-11-18: PARTIAL. Done: Anthropic `cache_control` breakpoints (system prompt, pinned ledger) behind the provider's declared `promptCache` capability and the operator's `NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`; request-shape test shows the marker; the usage summary reports the cached share (`cached N of M input tokens (P%)`). Not done: default-on (needs live Anthropic verification, none made), Bedrock `cachePoint`, operator `providers.json` declaration of the capability, a cached share in the provider matrix doc. OpenAI and Gemini cache implicitly and need no hint.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:56:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. Commits through `0d506762` connect strict function schemas on the **vLLM request path only**; llama.cpp and Ollama requests keep their native tool schemas (no grammar or format constraint), and the hybrid reasoning grammars in the roadmap are not implemented. The owner-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **REDUCED SCOPE DELIVERED; SOURCE GATES PASS; INDEPENDENT REVIEW REQUEST CHANGES, FINDINGS WAIVED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX NOT MEASURED** | Open items are listed in [the release notes](v1.1.2.md#provider-handling-wp-1107): no expiry for the server-kind cache, `X-Task-Class` can reach a replaced non-gateway server, null normalisation gaps, request counting can turn off, matrix provenance not bound to checkout content. G1.1-4 was not measured. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:95:**Not done in this record.** No release package for the final stable version was built here, installed, or acceptance-tested (the package rows below are for earlier source). The supported-provider matrix (G1.1-4) was not run. Release-level PTY evidence and installed trace capture on the final artifact were not collected.\n…17562 tokens truncated…ns\":23,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:3:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:57:54.986Z\",\"requestId\":\"47be294b-3f0d-41fb-a6ab-e0a76db8f6b5\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"chatgpt\",\"selectedModel\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"effectiveModel\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://chatgpt.com\",\"protocol\":\"openai-responses\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"resp_0493b5984a5d0128016adb92122b6c819eb6ef4d100d45e0f1\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":139,\"outputTokens\":17,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:5:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:04.677Z\",\"requestId\":\"24a6aab0-d91f-443f-a225-6abf69debe3b\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"REDACTED\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":24,\"outputTokens\":54,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":50,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\"