{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:13.526Z","ordinal":29856,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-87648414-9775-4882-9b64-e174a5366d0f","process_id":"99538","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"cache|cached|provider matrix|usage summary|Anthropic|Bedrock\" docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md; if test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md\"; then cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md/owner.json\"; else echo unclaimed; fi; ps -p 1151293 -o pid=,stat=,args="],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n \"cache|cached|provider matrix|usage summary|Anthropic|Bedrock\" docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md; if test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md\"; then cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md/owner.json\"; else echo unclaimed; fi; ps -p 1151293 -o pid=,stat=,args="}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:12:| PC-1 | Median PR CI under 40 minutes (measured 37 to 45 minutes) | Time on the runners | Shard the CLI suite and cache toolchains; the parallel `linux-x86_64` job is already in place |\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:22:| CX-6 | Opt-in Anthropic cache breakpoints (`NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`, provider declares `promptCache: \"anthropic\"`) and a cached-token share in the usage summary | Verification against the live Anthropic API; default-on; Bedrock `cachePoint`; declaring the capability from an operator `providers.json`; a share column in the provider matrix doc |\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:10:| `anthropic` | Anthropic Messages | `https://api.anthropic.com/v1` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:142:(OpenAI reasoning effort), `NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_THINKING_BUDGET` (Anthropic extended thinking, ≥ 1024),\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:206:(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:215:Prompt caching is opt-in: with `NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`, the built-in Anthropic provider (the only one that declares `promptCache: \"anthropic\"`) sends `cache_control` breakpoints on the system prompt and the pinned ledger. It has not been verified against the live API and Anthropic ignores a prefix below its minimum cacheable length, so a short prompt shows no cache hits. Other protocols cache automatically on the provider side (OpenAI, Gemini) or need provider-specific markers not implemented here (Bedrock `cachePoint`). The usage summary reports `cached N of M input tokens (P%)` whenever a provider reported cache counts.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:237:## Amazon Bedrock (native Converse, SigV4)\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:243:{ \"providers\": { \"bedrock\": { \"label\": \"Amazon Bedrock\", \"protocol\": \"bedrock-converse\", \"auth\": \"sigv4\",\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:247:Use the Bedrock model id (or inference-profile id) as the model. Requests go to `/model/<id>/converse` or\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:258:`credential_process`, instance or container metadata, and Bedrock API keys; use the OpenAI-compatible `bedrock-openai`\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:280:and killed after 15 s. Tokens are cached and refreshed one minute before expiry; concurrent requests share one refresh;\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:284:workload identity federation, the metadata server, and Anthropic models on Vertex. Verified against fixtures and a local\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:289:- Implemented: OpenRouter, OpenAI (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic OpenAI-compatible, ChatGPT plan and\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:291:  declared in `providers.json` (Azure OpenAI and other OpenAI-compatible endpoints), and Amazon Bedrock over the native\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:292:  Converse protocol and Google Vertex AI over the Gemini protocol (see below). Not implemented: Anthropic Claude Pro/Max sign-in, GitHub Enterprise Copilot.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:296:- Model catalog lists are cached per provider in `~/.cache/nexus/models` and used as fallback when offline; no embedded per-model pricing metadata: set `--context-limit` for large windows.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:328:above, and writes `~/.cache/nexus/models-snapshot.json` (mode 600). The cache exists only after the operator ran\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:330:tool-choice modes (`api.json` carries none), and a failed refresh changes nothing. An unreadable cache is ignored.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:331:`nexus providers` shows whether the bundled snapshot or a cache is in use, with its date. To regenerate the bundled file, fetch the data by hand, then run the offline generator:\nunclaimed\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":40843}},"started_at_ms":1795148533526,"completed_at_ms":1795148533526}}
