{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:46.101Z","ordinal":29891,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-24345dd5-16f9-4961-8fd3-dbc3068fafa1","process_id":"30345","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '198,220p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md\" && cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md/owner.json\" || true; test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.2.2_BACKLOG.md\" && cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.2.2_BACKLOG.md/owner.json\" || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '198,220p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md\" && cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md/owner.json\" || true; test -d \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.2.2_BACKLOG.md\" && cat \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.2.2_BACKLOG.md/owner.json\" || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"discards the partial output and no tool call from it runs. Explicit selections are strict — there is no automatic\nswitch to another provider or model, including after a refusal.\n\n## Usage, cost and limits\n\nEvery provider request (main, planner/coder, subagent, compaction, verification) records a receipt in\n`<workspace>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`: role, provider, selected and effective model, origin, protocol,\noutcome, provider request id, reported usage, and cost confidence. Cost is recorded only when the provider reports it\n(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\n`run -j` adds `cloudUsage`.\n\nProcess-wide limits, shared by all roles and subagents and enforced before each provider-connection request (a plain\n`--endpoint` that happens to be a cloud host is disclosure-gated but neither metered nor limited):\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS`, `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS` (reported tokens plus in-flight reservations),\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_COST_USD` (only for providers that report cost; with any other provider the request is refused\nrather than guessed). These are budgets, not a guarantee of the provider's invoice.\n\nPrompt caching is opt-in: with `NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`, the built-in Anthropic provider (the only one that declares `promptCache: \"anthropic\"`) sends `cache_control` breakpoints on the system prompt and the pinned ledger. It has not been verified against the live API and Anthropic ignores a prefix below its minimum cacheable length, so a short prompt shows no cache hits. Other protocols cache automatically on the provider side (OpenAI, Gemini) or need provider-specific markers not implemented here (Bedrock `cachePoint`). The usage summary reports `cached N of M input tokens (P%)` whenever a provider reported cache counts.\n\nPer-provider limits (`NEXUS_CLOUD_LIMITS`) are a JSON object keyed by provider id, applied on top of the process-wide limits:\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_LIMITS='{\"openrouter\":{\"maxCostUsd\":5,\"maxTokens\":2000000},\"groq\":{\"maxRequests\":200}}'`. Keys per provider are\n`maxRequests`, `maxTokens` and `maxCostUsd`; each counts only that provider's requests. A provider that reports no cost is priced\nfrom the models snapshot (price per million tokens for the model that ran); the refusal says how many requests were estimated.\n.git\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41877}},"started_at_ms":1795148566101,"completed_at_ms":1795148566101}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:46.228Z","ordinal":29892,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f731-4ed4-7770-8f5a-08e1fd3ed23b","call_id":"call_3e8bce74c44643ea972bab590f5d6b5c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"discards the partial output and no tool call from it runs. Explicit selections are strict — there is no automatic\nswitch to another provider or model, including after a refusal.\n\n## Usage, cost and limits\n\nEvery provider request (main, planner/coder, subagent, compaction, verification) records a receipt in\n`<workspace>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`: role, provider, selected and effective model, origin, protocol,\noutcome, provider request id, reported usage, and cost confidence. Cost is recorded only when the provider reports it\n(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\n`run -j` adds `cloudUsage`.\n\nProcess-wide limits, shared by all roles and subagents and enforced before each provider-connection request (a plain\n`--endpoint` that happens to be a cloud host is disclosure-gated but neither metered nor limited):\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS`, `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS` (reported tokens plus in-flight reservations),\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_COST_USD` (only for providers that report cost; with any other provider the request is refused\nrather than guessed). These are budgets, not a guarantee of the provider's invoice.\n\nPrompt caching is opt-in: with `NEXUS_PROMPT_CACHE=1`, the built-in Anthropic provider (the only one that declares `promptCache: \"anthropic\"`) sends `cache_control` breakpoints on the system prompt and the pinned ledger. It has not been verified against the live API and Anthropic ignores a prefix below its minimum cacheable length, so a short prompt shows no cache hits. Other protocols cache automatically on the provider side (OpenAI, Gemini) or need provider-specific markers not implemented here (Bedrock `cachePoint`). The usage summary reports `cached N of M input tokens (P%)` whenever a provider reported cache counts.\n\nPer-provider limits (`NEXUS_CLOUD_LIMITS`) are a JSON object keyed by provider id, applied on top of the process-wide limits:\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_LIMITS='{\"openrouter\":{\"maxCostUsd\":5,\"maxTokens\":2000000},\"groq\":{\"maxRequests\":200}}'`. Keys per provider are\n`maxRequests`, `maxTokens` and `maxCostUsd`; each counts only that provider's requests. A provider that reports no cost is priced\nfrom the models snapshot (price per million tokens for the model that ran); the refusal says how many requests were estimated.\n.git\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","create_time":1795148566.2285676}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":13190,"sampled_through_sequence":13186,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
