{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:53.345Z","ordinal":29896,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05793ea695c2aa2c016affcb1b6f2087d2be912cf278aa5496","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d21e2d82829f422f846f752d159686e4","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,55p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; ls \\\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\\\" | rg 'CLOUD_PROVIDERS|v1\\\\.2\\\\.2_BACKLOG|docs'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":2500}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","create_time":1795148571.4367468}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":13192,"sampled_through_sequence":13190,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:53.369Z","ordinal":29897,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","response_id":"resp_05793ea695c2aa2c016affcb16a2d087d295139ca2d11d08c5","usage":{"input_tokens":71872,"cached_input_tokens":70400,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":348,"reasoning_output_tokens":233,"total_tokens":72220},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":642630,"cached_input_tokens":623232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3080,"reasoning_output_tokens":1745,"total_tokens":645710},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":625478177,"cached_input_tokens":618476800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1343156,"reasoning_output_tokens":708702,"total_tokens":626821333}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:22:53.523Z","ordinal":29898,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-637e7c2e-9a13-4402-96a6-60137ebafed3","process_id":"72521","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,55p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; ls \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" | rg 'CLOUD_PROVIDERS|v1\\.2\\.2_BACKLOG|docs'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,55p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; ls \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" | rg 'CLOUD_PROVIDERS|v1\\.2\\.2_BACKLOG|docs'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Cloud inference providers\n\nNexus runs against the local appliance by default. Cloud providers are opt-in, selected explicitly by the operator,\nand use their own credentials. Nothing in this document changes how the appliance is reached.\n\n| Provider id | Protocol | Default base URL | Credential variable |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `openrouter` | OpenAI Chat Completions (+ usage/cost reporting) | `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` | `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` |\n| `openai` | OpenAI Responses (stateless, `store: false`) | `https://api.openai.com/v1` | `OPENAI_API_KEY` |\n| `anthropic` | Anthropic Messages | `https://api.anthropic.com/v1` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\n| `compatible` | OpenAI Chat Completions, any service | none — must be configured | `NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY` |\n| `chatgpt` | OpenAI Responses via the ChatGPT Codex backend | `https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex` | sign-in only (**unofficial**) |\n| `copilot` | Chat Completions (Responses for `gpt-5*`) | `https://api.githubcopilot.com` | sign-in only (**unofficial**) |\n\n## Catalog providers (OpenAI-compatible, shipped as data)\n\n`cli/src/providers.catalog.json` declares these in the same schema as `providers.json`; select one with\n`--provider <id>` and give its key in the listed variable. `nexus providers` marks them `catalog`.\n\n| Provider id | Base URL | Key variable |\n|---|---|---|\n| `mistral` | `https://api.mistral.ai/v1` | `MISTRAL_API_KEY` |\n| `groq` | `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1` | `GROQ_API_KEY` |\n| `togetherai` | `https://api.together.ai/v1` | `TOGETHER_API_KEY` |\n| `deepseek` | `https://api.deepseek.com` | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` |\n| `xai` | `https://api.x.ai/v1` | `XAI_API_KEY` |\n| `fireworks-ai` | `https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1` | `FIREWORKS_API_KEY` |\n| `cerebras` | `https://api.cerebras.ai/v1` | `CEREBRAS_API_KEY` |\n| `perplexity` | `https://api.perplexity.ai` | `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY` |\n| `gemini` | `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai` | `GEMINI_API_KEY` |\n| `cloudflare-workers-ai` | yours: `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account id>/ai/v1` | `CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY` |\n| `azure-openai` | yours: `https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/<deployment>` (sends `api-key`, `api-version=2024-10-21`) | `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` |\n| `bedrock-openai` | yours: `https://bedrock-runtime.<region>.amazonaws.com/openai/v1` (bearer API key) | `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` |\n\nProviders marked \"yours\" depend on an account, resource or region: set `NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL` (the id in upper case, `-` as\n`_`, for example `NEXUS_AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL`) or pass `--base-url`. A definition of the same id in your own\n`providers.json` replaces the catalog entry. Each entry has a recorded-fixture test (text, tool call, reasoning,\ntruncation, error) against a local mock; none was exercised against the live service.\n\n## Your own providers (`~/.config/nexus/providers.json`)\n\nAny service that speaks one of the supported wire protocols can be declared without code. The file is read only from the\noperator's home directory; a `providers.json` in a project is never consulted. An invalid file is reported by\n`nexus doctor` (`config.valid`) and no provider is registered from it. Built-in ids cannot be redefined. Every error\nnames the field (for example `providers.azure-openai.authHeader`).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"azure-openai\": {\n      \"label\": \"Azure OpenAI\",\n      \"protocol\": \"openai-chat\",\n      \"baseUrl\": \"https://{resource}.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments/{deployment}\",\n      \"variables\": { \"resource\": \"acme\", \"deployment\": \"gpt-4o\" },\n      \"query\": { \"api-version\": \"2024-10-21\" },\n.git\nFILE_docs_ARCHITECTURE.md.released-20261115T215303Z\nFILE_docs_ARCHITECTURE.md.released-20261115T224557Z\nFILE_docs_CLIENT_GUIDE.md.released-20261105T142659Z\nFILE_docs_COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md\nFILE_docs_COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md.released-20261119-rd7\nFILE_docs_README.md.released-20261110T045010Z\nFILE_docs_REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md.released-20261105T142659Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261109T194217Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261109T195144Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T005132Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T022126Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T023630Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T032842Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T055233Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T060116Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T063339Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T063752Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T070402Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T072250Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261110T075448Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261115T215303Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261115T224557Z\nFILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md.released-20261119-rd7\nFILE_docs_releases_v1.0.0-rc.13.md.released-20261105T142659Z\nFILE_docs_releases_v1.0.0-rc.14.md.released-20261105T142659Z\nFILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md.released-20261103T025719Z\nFILE_docs_releases_v1