{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:23:09.014Z","ordinal":29919,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-98d67f2d-d6d4-4b84-928f-592927e76ae5","process_id":"25809","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"R2|R3|review contract|change-scope|TODO|remaining|not done|defer|unresolved|follow-up\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md /home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/docs/INVARIANTS.md --glob '!eval/**' | sed -n '1,200p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md | sed -n '68,78p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n \"R2|R3|review contract|change-scope|TODO|remaining|not done|defer|unresolved|follow-up\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md /home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/docs/INVARIANTS.md --glob '!eval/**' | sed -n '1,200p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md | sed -n '68,78p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/docs/INVARIANTS.md:23:| I-ACCEPT-2 | A reviewer's ACCEPT, an engineering assessment or any model text never overrides a deterministic gate: a failing or absent verifier, a scope violation, or an unproven criterion forces REJECT. The reviewer's ACCEPT is evidence, not acceptance authority. A work unit's outcome equals its turn's outcome except for one named case (`unitOutcome`: a tester that ran a passing verifier this turn on a turn that needed none). | `cli/src/core/independent_review.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` | `cli/test/independent_review.test.ts`, `cli/test/ceri_semantic_integrity.test.ts`, `cli/test/unit_outcome.test.ts` | Existing control (credited, not new): `parseIndependentReviewVerdict` fails closed. Pinned here so the review contract cannot weaken it. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/docs/INVARIANTS.md:27:| I-CHANGE-1 | The implementer prompt states the change-scope rules: smallest change, no abstraction nothing needs, a refactor keeps behaviour, find the reason before removing code, keep comments, tests and docs true, state side effects and unchecked assumptions. Instructions only: acceptance still rests on the verifier and the review. | `cli/src/agent.ts` | `cli/test/change_scope_prompt.test.ts` | Follow-up assignment 2026-11-17: nothing told the implementer about scope or rationale. The text is short on purpose: it is sent with every request and context-budget tests are calibrated against the prompt size. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/docs/INVARIANTS.md:58:| The change-cost scenarios (A to H) are mechanism-level, and the live runs of five matching tasks (`docs/evidence/change-cost-live-2026-11-18/`) found no measurable difference between the base and branch builds (37/50 each at 10 runs per cell; a 14 vs 20 gap at 5 runs per cell did not replicate). The CHANGE SCOPE prompt rule (I-CHANGE-1) is therefore unproven as a behaviour change. | One model, 15 runs per cell at most, two tasks at ceiling; the reviewer path is not exercised. | A second model and tasks that drive the review contract, before any claim that the rules change outcomes. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:46:| R2 | ARCH_DEBT | review verdict/prompt has no criteria for hidden side effects, abstraction justification, behaviour change inside refactor, rationale loss; `unresolvedAssumptions` stored but never rendered | M | extend existing verdict schema minimally (`changeRisk` findings, deterministic where possible: diff_boundary), render unresolvedAssumptions; reviewer ACCEPT stays evidence only |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:47:| R3 | ARCH_DEBT | implementer prompt/AGENTS.md lack scope-discipline / no-unneeded-abstraction / preserve-rationale rules; no task-kind classification | M | add short rules to the existing system prompt + AGENTS.md; kind classification only as a recorded field, not a new gate |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:66:1 U1,U2(+D5),U3,U4 (side effects/unknown outcome)  2 L1,L2,L3,E1 (state integrity)  3 R1,D6,D3,D2,D1 (acceptance + authorization)  4 P1..P4 (providers)  5 R2,R3 (review/agent guidance, existing contracts)  6 A1,A2,A4/A5,E2,E3,E4,D4 (invariant/consolidation with tests)  7 scenarios A..H in CERI fixture + diff_boundary eval tasks  8 INVARIANTS/rationale doc (code<->test<->rationale table, checked by a script like check_requirements) + roadmap rows + CHANGELOG  9 regression vs baseline, tsc, node 22/24 note.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:67:Scenario plan (follow-up §11): A..H become CERI `multi_file_refactoring`/`scoped_implementation` fixture entries driven deterministically (diff_boundary + test commands on fixture repos); real-Nexus runs only if the gateway claim is available (reported separately from fixture-only results).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:77:Done (rule ids in `docs/INVARIANTS.md`): U1 I-EFFECT-1; U2/D5 I-EFFECT-2; U3/U4 I-EFFECT-3; L1/L2/L3/E1/D4 I-LIFE-1; D3 I-AUTH-1; D1 I-AUTH-2 (reproduced at runtime first: every MCP call returned FAIL-001); A4 I-AUTH-3; D6 I-ACCEPT-1; E4 I-ACCEPT-2; P2 I-PROVIDER-1; P3 I-PROVIDER-2; D2 I-EFFECT-4; R2 I-CHANGE-2; R3 I-CHANGE-1; E3 one success predicate; A2 durable private writers; scenarios A-H (mechanism-level); INVARIANTS.md + checker + CI step; AGENTS.md; roadmap rows EI-1..7; CHANGELOG; stale doc headers (D7).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:101:- [x] Unstructured objective continued by \"continue\"-style follow-up keeps its tracking; new objective resets\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/invariants/tasks/todo.md:158:- [x] Owner follow-up: kept only branches with roadmap/planning content not on main (`v1/docs-v11-layered-memory`,\n| VC-5 | Re-check `verified` on resume (invalidate when the candidate identity differs) and persist the unbound-pass marker so a resumed task does not hit the \"no matching baseline\" refusal | resume test: edited workspace demotes `verified`; resume after an unbound pass completes as REGRESSION_FREE | S | P1 |\n| VC-6 | **Done 2026-11-18** (`cli/src/tester.ts`, `cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts`, `cli/src/git.ts`, `cli/test/vc6_typecheck_gaps.test.ts`; manual section \"Type-check evidence\"). Baseline run (tsc, go vet, pyright, mypy; cargo excluded as not cheap) so an untouched caller broken by the change blocks VERIFIED; shell-changed files counted via the workspace diff; Go and Python (when configured); missing tool is UNAVAILABLE, never a pass; NEXUS_TYPECHECK=off unchanged. Limits: one check per project (first found: tsc, cargo, go, then python), no baseline after a resume, a baseline needs the verifier baseline to have run. Type-check gaps: baseline run to catch callers broken in untouched files, count shell-changed files as modified (workspace diff, not edit tools), Go (`go vet`) and Python (pyright/mypy when configured) | a change that breaks an untouched caller blocks VERIFIED; opt-out stays | M | P2 |\n| VC-7 | Convergence on the `run_tests` path and for operator-configured verifiers | a `run_tests`-only loop stops with the history attached | S | P2 **Done 2026-11-18** (`dispatch_tool_call.ts` judges `convergenceSignal` after a recorded verifier attempt; `cli/test/vc7_run_tests_convergence.test.ts`, the main case was red before the fix). An operator-configured verifier is covered because it is recorded through the same path. |\n| VC-8 | Per-role tool allowlists beyond reviewer and researcher (old backlog REQ:259, accepted 2026-11-15): allowlists for implementer and tester, consistent with SI-2's tester scoping (`roleToolAllowList`, `cli/src/agent.ts:5490`) | each role's disallowed tool is refused with a reason; existing flows unchanged | S | P2 (v1.2.2) |\n| VC-9 | **Partly done 2026-11-18** (audit: `docs/v1.2.1/VC-9-needs-input-audit.md`; glue: `cli/src/core/needs_input.ts`, `--answer`). Done: tool approval (write, exec, egress), verification-file edit, verifier and type-check approval end BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT with a question and resume with `--answer`. **Not done** (design decisions, see the audit): a requirement marked blocked (changes the REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE contract; free-text answer), an unresolved steering conflict (sidecar-only; resolve-after-the-fact), a subagent's question. Headless needs-input audit (Anthropic 2026 trends report, trend 4: agents that learn when to ask for help): list every path where a headless run needs an operator decision (steering that negates a requirement, a requirement marked blocked, a denied approval, a verification-file edit) and give each the same resumable outcome, a stable `needs_input` reason carrying the question and resumable with the answer; build only the missing glue | each path ends BLOCKED with a machine-readable question and resumes with an answer; no path guesses | S | P2 |\n| VC-10 | Steering semantic judge (optional; evidence in `docs/research/steering-judgment/`): a judge provider interface (none by default, the configured gateway, or an explicit opt-in third party) asked, for each live requirement, whether the steering message withdraws, defers or changes it; conflict (the existing operator decision) if the regex hits or `withdraws` >= 0.7 whatever `defers` says, advisory note between 0.3 and 0.7, `defers` and `changes` informational only; an unavailable judge records `semanticJudge: unavailable` and keeps the regex decision; the steer stays held from the model until the operator decides and no text goes to a third party unless opted in | **gated**: build only after a larger evaluation (at least 100 judgments from real steering messages, with the owner's consent, labelled blind, on a fresh held-out split) shows union recall of at least 0.8 with at most 5% false positives on the non-withdrawals, and after the synchronous path can hold a steer while a judge answers (the pilot gateway judge took a median of about 17 s per message) | M | P2 (v1.2.2, gated) |\n\n### CS: containment and security\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":46859}},"started_at_ms":1795148589014,"completed_at_ms":1795148589014}}
