_outcome.test.ts             |  67 ++++++\n cli/test/start_record_durability.test.ts           |  51 +++++\n cli/test/subagent_capability_discovery.test.ts     |  52 +++++\n cli/test/unit_outcome.test.ts                      |  21 ++\n cli/test/upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts      |  19 +-\n cli/test/verification_guard.test.ts                |  27 +++\n docs/ARCHITECTURE.md                               |   4 +\n docs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md                      |   2 +-\n docs/INVARIANTS.md                                 |  58 ++++++\n .../evidence/change-cost-live-2026-11-18/README.md |  45 +++++\n .../run1-base-65c76b28.results.jsonl               |  25 +++\n .../run1-base.manifest.json                        | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++\n .../run1-branch-9b3aa434.results.jsonl             |  25 +++\n .../run1-branch.manifest.json                      | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++\n .../run2-base-65c76b28.results.jsonl               |  50 +++++\n .../run2-base.manifest.json                        | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++\n .../run2-branch-7aa7414a.results.jsonl             |  50 +++++\n .../run2-branch.manifest.json                      | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++\n .../v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md |   2 +-\n docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md                                |  14 ++\n scripts/check_invariants.mjs                       |  53 +++++\n tasks/lessons.md                                   |   7 +\n tasks/todo.md                                      |  86 ++++++++\n 77 files changed, 3267 insertions(+), 81 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":50858}},"started_at_ms":1795148641603,"completed_at_ms":1795148641604}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:24:01.748Z","ordinal":29959,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f732-75d4-7c62-a34a-22bd48966210","call_id":"call_50540251f78a49d092085cba5c4c9b62","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Engineering invariants audit (2026-11-17, branch v1/invariants-audit from origin/main 65c76b28)\n\nWorktree `~/nexus-wt/invariants`. `~/nexus-code` (owner checkout, 856 commits behind, foreign uncommitted edits) is untouched.\nMandate: lifecycle integrity, authority, side-effect semantics, unknown-outcome recovery, provider contracts, durable invariants.\nEvidence tags: OBSERVED = read in code / run; INFERRED = reasoning. Auditor claims were re-read before being acted on.\n\n## Gap analysis (classification; file:line in cli/src)\n| ID | Class | Finding | Sev |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| U1 | VERIFIED_DEFECT (OBSERVED) | `mcp.ts:339-351` HTTP/SSE `tools/call` re-POSTs the same payload to a second URL on ANY fetch failure (timeout, reset after server receipt): duplicate non-idempotent effect | M |\n| U2 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP (OBSERVED) | `core/spine.ts:597-614` drops `ExecutionResult.timedOut/cancelled`; receipt/`recordOperationEnd` say plain `failed`; RPC disconnect (`tools.ts:830`) reads as failure -> model retries. Unknown outcome is indistinguishable from confirmed failure | M |\n| U3 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP (OBSERVED app.ts:199) | plain `run --resume`/REPL resume discards `recovered.interrupted`; only prose guards re-issue of a non-idempotent `run_command`/MCP call in auto mode | M |\n| U4 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP | write-ahead record: no args hash, start record not fsynced, written before baseline capture (not-started vs dispatched collapse); fail-open on write error is pinned by durable_continuity.test.ts:1000 (documented, not changed) | M |\n| L1 | VERIFIED_DEFECT (reported, re-verify) | `operation resume`/`decide` load state before `acquire` (operation_cli.ts:298): stale snapshot can overwrite a COMPLETE record | M |\n| L2 | VERIFIED_DEFECT (reported, re-verify) | `operation run` with explicit existing `spec.id` overwrites the stored operation | L-M |\n| L3 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP | no executable transition table; operation doc status not validated at load (`operation_schema.ts`) | L-M |\n| P1 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP | failover probe treats 401/403/404 as available and never checks capabilities (client.ts:1670) | M |\n| P2 | VERIFIED_DEFECT (reported) | subagents never run capability discovery (agent.ts runSubagent) -> 64k default window | M |\n| P3 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP | openai-chat `finish_reason=content_filter` treated as complete answer | L-M |\n| P4 | VERIFIED_CONTROL_GAP | server that ignores `tools` is silently usable; `toolCall` snapshot flag is dead data | M |\n| X1 | reported | OAuth rotating-refresh race (client.ts:1044); plugin can mutate approved args (agent.ts:5860); checkpoint restore not journaled | L-M |\n| A1..A5 | ALREADY_ENFORCED (credited) | reviewer cannot self-accept (independent_review.ts); TurnResult invariants+frozen; upgrade journal recovery; operation lock + merge reconcile; per-endpoint egress/credential binding on failover; task-state atomic write; EXECUTION_UNKNOWN blocks replay for runner units |  |\nNOT_APPLICABLE: paused session executing tools (only --step ends turn); acceptance state never set by code.\n\n## Plan (dependency order; red test first; one concern per commit)\n- [ ] 0. Baseline: `run_tests.mjs` on untouched tree under SUITE claim (log in scratchpad); record pre-existing failures\n- [ ] 1. U1 MCP: `tools/call` never replayed after ambiguous failure; fall back only on definitive 404/405/501 from `/message`; ambiguous -> outcome-unknown error. Test: stub HTTP server counts deliveries (reset-after-receive, timeout, 404)\n- [ ] 2. U2 structured unknown outcome: `outcomeUnknown` carried tools.ts -> spine -> receipt/recordOperationEnd -> tool message; RPC disconnect/timeout/cancel for effectful tools = unknown, not failed. Tests with fake core / bridge hooks\n- [ ] 3. U3+U4: record `argsHash` (sha256 of canonical args, no secrets) + fsync start record; on resume with interrupted op, an identical re-issue (tool+argsHash) is refused without an explicit approval, even in auto mode. Test: SIGKILL child at dispatch->ack seam, resume, assert no silent re-dispatch; compat: old records without hash still load\n- [ ] 4. L1/L2: load-after-acquire in resume/decide; refuse `run` over existing id. Tests: stale-snapshot race, duplicate id\n- [ ] 5. L3: transition guard for unit/operation status writes (single assertTransition used by scheduler writers); doc status validated at load\n- [ ] 6. P1..P4 provider: probe requires 2xx/known-capability for failover; subagent capability refresh; content_filter -> refused finish; tools-ignored detection surfaced\n- [ ] 7. Scenarios: add invariant scenarios to `cli/test/fixtures/ceri/semantic_integrity.scenarios.json` (+sha256 manifest) with explicit state/trigger/invariant/evidence fields; driver cases; no second framework\n- [ ] 8. Docs: AGENTS.md short \"Invariants\" section (pointers, not prose copies); docs/INVARIANTS.md table (invariant -> enforcing code -> test); roadmap rows in docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md (VC-11 etc.); CHANGELOG [Unreleased]\n- [ ] 9. Full regression: cli suite, tsc, cargo (core untouched unless needed), diff failing set vs baseline; Node 22+24 note\n- [ ] 10. Commit on v1/invariants-audit; NOT pushed/merged (AGENTS.md: owner authority)\nNot done by design: X1 (OAuth/plugin/checkpoint) and fail-open->fail-closed on intent-write failure are recorded as residual risk with roadmap rows unless time permits.\n\n## Follow-up workstream: change-cost and architectural integrity (same branch; merged plan)\nPrior-workstream state verified 2026-11-17 07:06: branch has 0 commits ahead of origin/main; only this plan exists. No prior guarantee is implemented yet; all are reported as unimplemented, not credited.\nRule applied: each change needs a stated problem + test; no line-count/dedup-only changes. Justified duplication KEPT: repeated_calls.callKey vs execution_tracking.actionIdentity (different jobs), the two upgrade/operation acquire loops (only the liveness verdict is shared), optional v1.1 `?? []` reads (documented), FileGuard users, `dispatchToolCall` wrapper (instrumentation), protocols openai-chat lambdas (compat shim).\n\n| ID | Class | Finding (auditor-reported unless marked OBSERVED) | Sev | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 | WITHDRAWN (re-read) | independent_review.ts:412 is redundant with earlier verifier rejects, but the prompt states the policy (truncated diff => verifier evidence required; scope detection runs on the FULL diff), so behaviour matches intent; not a defect. At most: name the 20000 constant | - | no behaviour change |\n| R2 | ARCH_DEBT | review verdict/prompt has no criteria for hidden side effects, abstraction justification, behaviour change inside refactor, rationale loss; `unresolvedAssumptions` stored but never rendered | M | extend existing verdict schema minimally (`changeRisk` findings, deterministic where possible: diff_boundary), render unresolvedAssumptions; reviewer ACCEPT stays evidence only |\n| R3 | ARCH_DEBT | implementer prompt/AGENTS.md lack scope-discipline / no-unneeded-abstraction / preserve-rationale rules; no task-kind classification | M | add short rules to the existing system prompt + AGENTS.md; kind classification only as a recorded field, not a new gate |\n| D1 | VERIFIED_DEFECT? (static; reproduce first) | MCP/plugin tools offered to the model but not in CapabilityRegistry => spine returns FAIL-001 (agent.ts:1411-1416, spine.ts:309) | M-H | reproduce at runtime; if true register extension capabilities with explicit effect class; test tools/call end to end |\n| D2 | DEFECT (static) | dry-run simulates only 4 file tools + run_command; fetch_web/browser/manage_knowledge run for real with receipt `simulated:true` | M | short-circuit by effect class in spine |\n| D3 | DEFECT (static) | repo `.nexus-security.json` `verificationPaths.mode:\"off\"` honoured in untrusted workspaces (security.ts:246-262) | M | accept mode/allow only from operator config or trusted workspace |\n| D4 | DEBT | spine production hooks default to no-ops (processLifecycle/contextAdmission/evidenceEmission unwired => no receipts persisted); 9 direct bridge run_command sites bypass spine; switches in scheduler.ts:448,568 lack assertNever; persisted decision action kinds unvalidated | M | assertNever + validate action kinds (cheap, testable); document the bypass sites; do not rewire evidence in this pass |\n| D5 | DEFECT (static) | failed/timed-out mutating call => candidateMutated=false, unverified-change latch never set (spine.ts:577) | M | unknown/timeout on a mutating tool counts as mutated (pairs with U2) |\n| D6 | DEFECT (static) | task_completed receipt hard-codes exitCode 0 / constant stdoutHash; receipt persist failure leaves verifiedWorktreeCompletion true (agent.ts ~5083) | M | hash real verifier output; clear flag on persist failure |\n| E1 | DEFECT | validateOperationState admits missing dependsOn/requires/status enum etc.; ~12 sites throw TypeError on resume (operation_schema.ts:120) | L-M | validate at load (quarantine), then drop `?? []` at :120; test with corrupt record |\n| E2 | DEBT | task-state arrays not normalised on v>=1 load; redundant downstream guards (agent.ts:1795-1802, state.ts:1032-1034) | L | normalise in load path; delete only the guards proven redundant |\n| E3 | DEBT | `turnSucceeded` predicate re-spelled at agent.ts:7493,7890,8028, ui.ts:168 | L | call turnSucceeded; test |\n| E4 | DEBT | tester NOT_REQUIRED->VERIFIED rewrite in operation_runner_execution.ts:874-915 outside assertTurnResultInvariants | M | one named function + test (do not move into agent without evidence) |\n| A1 | DEFECT | upgrade.ts/upgrade_journal.ts lock liveness = pid-only (reboot + pid reuse wedges); doctor.ts:1506 acquireLock has no reclaim guard (empty-pid window steals live lock) | L-M | share liveness verdict only (host+boot+age); doctor uses FileGuard; tests |\n| A2 | DEBT | hand-rolled atomic writers skip fsync/cleanup: credentials.ts:176, workspace_trust.ts:74, models_refresh.ts:96 (+ceri evidence_store) | L-M | use writePrivateFile durable; add write tests |\n| A4/A5 | DEBT/DEFECT | provider headers duplicated (Copilot headers sent twice); config.providerBaseUrl accepts cleartext public http + query/fragment while validateBaseUrl is strict | L | route providerBaseUrl through validateBaseUrl; dedupe headers; tests |\n| F1 | DEBT | forwarders: core/app.ts getX accessors, registerWithCapabilities (no caller), executeSlashCommand dead cases | L | delete only proven-dead code (registerWithCapabilities); leave app.ts accessors (public API, compat) |\n| D7 | DOC | SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md header/line cites stale; ARCHITECTURE.md Rust file list stale; EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md header stale | L | correct; no append-only history |\nNot found/credited: reviewer cannot self-accept; failover authorization per endpoint; cancellation path; slash/protocol dispatch rejects unknown.\n\n### Merged execution order (correctness first; style last)\n1 U1,U2(+D5),U3,U4 (side effects/unknown outcome)  2 L1,L2,L3,E1 (state integrity)  3 R1,D6,D3,D2,D1 (acceptance + authorization)  4 P1..P4 (providers)  5 R2,R3 (review/agent guidance, existing contracts)  6 A1,A2,A4/A5,E2,E3,E4,D4 (invariant/consolidation with tests)  7 scenarios A..H in CERI fixture + diff_boundary eval tasks  8 INVARIANTS/rationale doc (code<->test<->rationale table, checked by a script like check_requirements) + roadmap rows + CHANGELOG  9 regression vs baseline, tsc, node 22/24 note.\nScenario plan (follow-up §11): A..H become CERI `multi_file_refactoring`/`scoped_implementation` fixture entries driven deterministically (diff_boundary + test commands on fixture repos); real-Nexus runs only if the gateway claim is available (reported separately from fixture-only results).\n\n## Review (measured 2026-11-17; nothing pushed or merged)\nBranch `v1/invariants-impl` (merged forward into `v1/invariants-audit`), based on origin/main 65c76b28; origin/main has since moved (e.g. #582), so a merge needs the owner's rebase/conflict pass (CHANGELOG, PLAN.md, agent.ts are the likely overlaps).\nRegression (all runs on this host, one at a time, throwaway HOME):\n- Clean base 65c76b28, Node 24: 4030 tests, 4014 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (`eval_version_probe_storage`: needs `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT`, only CI sets it).\n- Branch at b2418684 (before the last EI-3/EI-4/EI-7 changes), Node 24: 4082 tests, 4066 pass, 15 skipped, same single failure.\n- Branch at f7aa3919 (final), Node 24: 3441 tests in the completed segments, 3426 pass, same single failure; `compaction_continuity` timed out in the runner under host load (it also timed out in the first, untouched-base attempt) and passed alone: 34/34 in ~5 min. The branch adds no new failure.\n- Node 22.22.2 (nvm), final tree 91f69fb1 (code identical to f7aa3919; docs only since): 4089 tests, 4073 pass, 15 skipped, 1 fail (the same environment-only `eval_version_probe_storage`), no timeouts. An earlier Node 22 run on b2418684 had three files time out under host load (load average above 20 from other processes); each passed alone.\n- `tsc` clean; `scripts/check_invariants.mjs` and the leak-guard ratchet pass. CI matrix (test-matrix 22/24, linux-x86_64) not run: GitHub only.\nDone (rule ids in `docs/INVARIANTS.md`): U1 I-EFFECT-1; U2/D5 I-EFFECT-2; U3/U4 I-EFFECT-3; L1/L2/L3/E1/D4 I-LIFE-1; D3 I-AUTH-1; D1 I-AUTH-2 (reproduced at runtime first: every MCP call returned FAIL-001); A4 I-AUTH-3; D6 I-ACCEPT-1; E4 I-ACCEPT-2; P2 I-PROVIDER-1; P3 I-PROVIDER-2; D2 I-EFFECT-4; R2 I-CHANGE-2; R3 I-CHANGE-1; E3 one success predicate; A2 durable private writers; scenarios A-H (mechanism-level); INVARIANTS.md + checker + CI step; AGENTS.md; roadmap rows EI-1..7; CHANGELOG; stale doc headers (D7).\nWithdrawn/reclassified: R1 withdrawn (behaviour matches stated policy); P1 by design (probe means \"serving\"; 401 must surface, not be waited out).\nEI-2 closed (audit premise disproved: the state store already fsyncs file and directory on every write; pinned). EI-3 partly done: plugin args mutation (I-AUTH-4) and the in-process OAuth refresh race (I-AUTH-5) were reproduced with failing tests and fixed. EI-1 decided (not a gap): the intent write stays fail-open because the failure is loud and fails operation units (see `docs/INVARIANTS.md`, Decided).\nNot done, recorded as residual risk with roadmap rows: (EI-3 and EI-4 are done: cross-process OAuth refresh I-AUTH-5, restore journal event, upgrade and doctor lock liveness I-LIFE-3), A5 duplicate Copilot headers (unverified), P4 tools-ignored flag and tools-ignored flag (EI-6 remainder; browser_click is now mutating), spine production hooks / E2 guards (EI-7), live-model runs of the change-cost tasks (EI-5) done 2026-11-18: base and branch tie at 37/50 (10 runs per cell); an earlier 14/25 vs 20/25 (5 runs per cell) did not replicate, so there is no evidence the prompt rule changes model behaviour; see `docs/evidence/change-cost-live-2026-11-18/README.md` (scenarios A-H in CERI remain mechanism-level).\nLessons: see `tasks/lessons.md` (process liveness via pgrep). A prompt addition changed context-budget tests: a 150-token rule broke `context_convergence`; shortened rather than retuned.\n\n\n---\n(previous content of this file follows)\n\n# Compaction and task-continuity hardening (2026-10-13)\n\nWorktree `/home/mike/nexus-cc`, branch `feat/compaction-continuity` from `origin/main` a58f860.\n`~/nexus-code` (installed launcher target) is left untouched: it held foreign uncommitted edits written during this\nsession (instruction-precedence work, plus a partial unbounded-budget change), so this work is isolated.\n\nGateway reference (read-only): `/home/mike/Projects/aihost` fb1a2cd, deployed release t5820-gateway-b72a4f5.\n\n## A. Continuity without a step ceiling\n- [x] Default continuation unbounded (no 300-step / 120-min default); explicit operator limits still apply\n- [x] No \"step N of M, finish now\" notes unless the operator set a step limit\n- [x] spawn_subagent loop: progress-based, parent cancellation, no 8/15 cap\n- [x] team / work units: inherit unbounded continuation; work-unit capacity no longer defaults to 65536\n- [x] Persisted objective-scoped execution tracking in the ledger (bounded, loop evidence never evicted)\n- [x] Unstructured objective continued by \"continue\"-style follow-up keeps its tracking; new objective resets\n\n## B. State-aware repetition\n- [x] Action identity (canonical args), outcome identity (volatile tokens, duration_ms, exit_code), state identity (content + index + deps)\n- [x] Progress = new state / new information / new ledger state; not plan edits, reformatted args, identical writes\n- [x] Transient vs deterministic failures; polling backoff; unknown state reported as unknown\n- [x] (live finding) re-reads after compaction are re-acquisition / context thrash, not repetition\n\n## C. Durable compaction boundary\n- [x] Commit order: archive (fsync) → task state → session, synced; compaction ids named in each record\n- [x] Recovery: uncommitted archive entries filtered; torn lines reported; settled tool calls only\n- [x] Failures visible (CLI/TUI); turn stopped (PERSISTENCE_FAILED) on auto-commit failure\n- [x] /compact queued during work; ack + outcome; dedupe, bound, cancel, shutdown, turn-end; --llm too\n- [x] Thrash detection across steps (low-yield hold), separate from repetition\n- [x] (live finding) tracking record shared in place, never replaced mid-turn\n\n## D. Provider capabilities and token accounting\n- [x] Discover context/output/limits_version from /models (gateway, vLLM max_model_len); refresh on change\n- [x] Count via /v1/tokenize when advertised, with the exact outbound payload builder\n- [x] Sources: exact_admitted, exact_sampled_worker, gateway_conservative, client_estimate\n- [x] Strict counting opt-in; standalone defaults; headroom policy labelled as policy\n\n## Validation / deliverables\n- [x] Tests per area (65 new tests across 4 files); full `make test` on final snapshot (see review)\n- [x] Live local-inference multistep run across compaction boundaries (3 runs; run 3 completed)\n- [x] Operator + developer docs, acceptance ledger, gateway capability handoff\n\n## Review\n- Live runs found two real defects scripted tests had missed (re-reads after compaction stopped as loops; compaction\n  orphaning the live tracker) plus a wasted second count per step. All fixed with regression tests.\n- Not done: commit/merge (operator's decision), live standalone run against a non-gateway server, live capacity /\n  worker-change observation, `graphify update` (no graph in the worktree; the main checkout was not touched).\n\n# Output-truncation recovery (2026-10-14)\n\nBranch `fix/output-truncation-recovery` from main 1c3afbd. Trigger: live session `session_20261014_074807_hmo7` ended\n`FAILED / INFERENCE_FAILED (output_truncated/client)` at step 54 when one reply used the whole 8192-token output\nallowance inside a tool call (about 173 s of generation); output_truncated was always fatal to the turn.\n\n- [x] 1. Truncated reply → bounded retry: nothing from it runs; a Nexus note names the tool/path, the allowance, and asks\n      for the content in parts; the turn continues at the next step (new request id)\n- [x] 2. Bound: a second consecutive truncation ends the turn exactly as before; the truncated step counts as no progress\n- [x] 3. Prevention: write_file/edit_file descriptions say a reply's output is limited and long content goes in parts\n- [x] 4. Tests: truncated tool call → chunked write completes; two in a row → fails as before; truncated prose never\n      accepted as final; no tool from a truncated reply runs\n- [ ] Full `make test` on a snapshot; docs (USER_MANUAL / COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY) updated\n\n# Post-v1.1.3 housekeeping (2026-11-05)\n\nBranch `chore/housekeeping-post-v113` from main 46fd5045 (v1.1.3 stable, published).\n\n- [x] Root clutter (check-in scripts, session dumps, continuity-validation, stale root package-lock.json) moved to\n      `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/root-clutter/`; `.gitignore` now ignores `/nexus-session-*.json`\n- [x] 220 stale claims renamed `*.released-<UTC>` and logged; `GATEWAY` (codex-root, RC15 E5, 2026-10-31) left active\n- [x] Worktrees 875 → 137: 657 clean removed; 81 dirty archived to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/worktrees/`\n      (tracked.patch + untracked.tgz + meta.txt) then removed; 136 detached-HEAD trees kept (commits on no ref)\n- [x] Local branches 596 → 206: 364 merged into main deleted; 31 unmerged with a remote copy deleted\n- [x] Owner follow-up: kept only branches with roadmap/planning content not on main (`v1/docs-v11-layered-memory`,\n      `backup/agent-work-product-ae474637` with LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md) plus `v1/v113-plan`; the other 202 local branches\n      bundled to `~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/unmerged-branches.bundle` (tips in `branch-tips.txt`) then deleted\n- [x] Last stale claim (`GATEWAY`) released; no unreleased claims remain\n- [x] 4 stashes archived (`~/nexus-archive/housekeeping-20261105/stashes/`) and dropped; ~154 ancestor-merged remote branches deleted\n      (`v1/integration` is rule-protected and stays); 136 orphaned detached worktrees removed (22 dirty ones archived; all 118\n      distinct heads bundled in `orphan-heads.bundle`); missing orphan fixes recorded as v1.1.4 WP-1306 (local anchors `recovery/orphan-*`)\n- [x] Issue #69 (Harness2) review written: `docs/v1.1.4/HARNESS2-REVIEW.md` on PR #404 (WP-1307)\n- [ ] Open: 47 remote branches that are not ancestors of main (4 have merged PRs); issue #69 stays open until the write-up merges\n .