{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:27:05.949Z","ordinal":30089,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-598cc2b6-385d-4974-845a-e1fd09a62ba8","process_id":"48502","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '44,52p' docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md; find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf '%f\\n' | rg '^(GATEWAY|CLOUD|SUITE|.*mq|.*benchmark)$'; rg --files scripts cli/test docs | rg -i 'benchmark|harbor|terminal.?bench|mq-1|mq-2' | head -100; command -v docker || true; command -v podman || true; git status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '44,52p' docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md; find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -printf '%f\\n' | rg '^(GATEWAY|CLOUD|SUITE|.*mq|.*benchmark)$'; rg --files scripts cli/test docs | rg -i 'benchmark|harbor|terminal.?bench|mq-1|mq-2' | head -100; command -v docker || true; command -v podman || true; git status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"### MQ: measure and qualify\n\n| Unit | What | Accept | Size | Pri |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MQ-0 | Run the G1.1-4 matrix on the v1.2.0 release-candidate archive under the GATEWAY claim; record `docs/evidence/v1.2.0/…` and add the figure to the rc notes (closes GA-03) | evidence file with archive sha256, per-alias counts, repaired / invalid counts; notes updated by a docs PR | S | P0 |\n| MQ-1 | Benchmark adapter: a Harbor / Terminal-Bench runner for Nexus (template: Goose `evals/harbor/`), plus a SWE-bench-style adapter if the task format allows a hermetic run | `nexus` runs a pinned subset in task containers with no network leaks; results JSON with task ids, model, gateway alias, Nexus version, seed or sampling, wall time, and the raw verdicts (VERIFIED / REGRESSION_FREE / UNVERIFIED / BLOCKED) | M | P0 |\n| MQ-2 | False-completion metric: for every run record Nexus's own verdict and the benchmark's ground truth; report pass rate, **claimed-done-but-wrong rate**, and **verified-but-wrong rate** with Wilson 95% intervals (the repo already has the interval code in `eval/score.mjs`); compare against the same model through at least one peer harness already adapted in `eval/configs/pilot-*.json` | a report where a false VERIFIED is named and explained; the notes state the sample size and that it is self-run | M | P0 |\n| MQ-3 | Real-project smoke: a nightly job that runs a scripted task on pinned copies of representative repositories (a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project, a Python project, a Rust project, and the owner's own repositories where licensing allows) and fails when `task_completed` errors, hangs or ends UNVERIFIED for an avoidable reason. This is the test that would have caught the v1.1.4 every-completion error before release | job red on a seeded regression (a repo whose verifier cannot be bound must complete as REGRESSION_FREE). **Done 2026-11-17** (branch `v1/mq3`): `scripts/real_project_smoke.mjs`, `cli/test/real_project_smoke.test.ts`, nightly `.github/workflows/real-project-smoke.yml` (not required), `docs/REAL_PROJECT_SMOKE.md`. Covers a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project with 140 referenced files, a 24-deep tree and a pytest project; red when a completion errors, hangs or is not REGRESSION_FREE/VERIFIED; mutation-checked against a reintroduced unbindable-verifier block. **Does not cover:** a live model (the gateway is a scripted mock), real third-party or owner repositories (all synthetic), a Rust project, sandbox, worktree or resume modes | M | P0 **First hosted run 2026-11-18 (schedule, main 3c54e601): 3 of 4 repositories passed, the pytest one failed on a setup defect (pytest installed with `pip install --user` was invisible to the isolated HOME); fixed, rerun to be recorded.** **Validated on a hosted runner 2026-11-18 (manual run 44314195365 on a7c07e74: all four repositories REGRESSION_FREE) after the pytest setup fix.** |\n| MQ-4 | Scheduled model conformance: a nightly or weekly job that runs the tool-call matrix against the configured gateway aliases and alerts on a drop; claim protocol so it never collides with a human run (template: Goose `model-toolcall-conformance.yml`) | one alert path tested with a forced failure | S | P1 |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_JOURNAL_COMPLEXITY_RECOVERY/benchmark.txt\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/benchmark.tap\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/first-schema2-benchmark.tap\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_BASELINE/benchmark.tap\n/usr/bin/docker\n## main...origin/main\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":73773}},"started_at_ms":1795148825948,"completed_at_ms":1795148825948}}
