{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:31:50.883Z","ordinal":30238,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8d0d633e-1b41-4a86-9884-970935840e65","process_id":"46901","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"resume.*type.?check|type.?check.*resume|typecheckBaseline\" cli/test --glob '!eval/**'; rg -n \"typecheck baseline|resume\" docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md | head -50"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/vc6-resume-baseline","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'resume.*type.?check|type.?check.*resume|typecheckBaseline' cli/test --glob '!eval/**'","query":"resume.*type.?check|type.?check.*resume|typecheckBaseline","path":"test"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'typecheck baseline|resume' docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md docs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md","query":"typecheck baseline|resume","path":"BACKLOG.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"cli/test/code_evaluators_pinned_workspace.test.ts:48:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators_pinned_workspace.test.ts:54:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators_pinned_workspace.test.ts:79:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts:34:  const [result] = await runner.runCodeEvaluators({ task: { evaluators: [\"build\"], build }, candidateWorkspace: candidate, typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline });\ncli/test/code_evaluators_budgets.test.ts:90:    const run = (maxFileBytes: number) => runner.runCodeEvaluators({ task: { evaluators: [{ type: \"build\", command: process.execPath, args: [\"-e\", script], maxFileBytes }] }, candidateWorkspace: candidate, typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline });\ncli/test/code_evaluators_budgets.test.ts:105:    const run = (maxFileBytes: number) => runner.runCodeEvaluators({ task: { evaluators: [{ type: \"typecheck_clean\", command: process.execPath, args: [\"-e\", script], maxFileBytes }] }, candidateWorkspace: candidate, typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline });\ncli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:276:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:284:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:309:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ncli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:681:      typecheckBaselineWorkspace: baseline,\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:51:| MQ-3 | Real-project smoke: a nightly job that runs a scripted task on pinned copies of representative repositories (a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project, a Python project, a Rust project, and the owner's own repositories where licensing allows) and fails when `task_completed` errors, hangs or ends UNVERIFIED for an avoidable reason. This is the test that would have caught the v1.1.4 every-completion error before release | job red on a seeded regression (a repo whose verifier cannot be bound must complete as REGRESSION_FREE). **Done 2026-11-17** (branch `v1/mq3`): `scripts/real_project_smoke.mjs`, `cli/test/real_project_smoke.test.ts`, nightly `.github/workflows/real-project-smoke.yml` (not required), `docs/REAL_PROJECT_SMOKE.md`. Covers a JS project with `node_modules`, a Makefile project with 140 referenced files, a 24-deep tree and a pytest project; red when a completion errors, hangs or is not REGRESSION_FREE/VERIFIED; mutation-checked against a reintroduced unbindable-verifier block. **Does not cover:** a live model (the gateway is a scripted mock), real third-party or owner repositories (all synthetic), a Rust project, sandbox, worktree or resume modes | M | P0 **First hosted run 2026-11-18 (schedule, main 3c54e601): 3 of 4 repositories passed, the pytest one failed on a setup defect (pytest installed with `pip install --user` was invisible to the isolated HOME); fixed, rerun to be recorded.** **Validated on a hosted runner 2026-11-18 (manual run 44314195365 on a7c07e74: all four repositories REGRESSION_FREE) after the pytest setup fix.** |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:56:| MQ-8 | Long-horizon and A/B measurement (the Anthropic trends report, trend 3; `agent-rules-books` and the context-management post both report gains without a methodology): one multi-hour scripted task on a pinned repository with a resume part-way, and paired runs of the same scenarios with an instruction file, or tool-output clearing, on and off; report completion, claimed-done-but-wrong rate, tokens and wall time with Wilson 95% intervals | results JSON with the paired runs, model, gateway alias, Nexus version and seeds; no effect claimed unless the interval excludes zero (needs MQ-1 and MQ-2) | M | P2 (v1.2.2) |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:68:| VC-5 | Re-check `verified` on resume (invalidate when the candidate identity differs) and persist the unbound-pass marker so a resumed task does not hit the \"no matching baseline\" refusal | resume test: edited workspace demotes `verified`; resume after an unbound pass completes as REGRESSION_FREE | S | P1 |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:69:| VC-6 | **Done 2026-11-18** (`cli/src/tester.ts`, `cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts`, `cli/src/git.ts`, `cli/test/vc6_typecheck_gaps.test.ts`; manual section \"Type-check evidence\"). Baseline run (tsc, go vet, pyright, mypy; cargo excluded as not cheap) so an untouched caller broken by the change blocks VERIFIED; shell-changed files counted via the workspace diff; Go and Python (when configured); missing tool is UNAVAILABLE, never a pass; NEXUS_TYPECHECK=off unchanged. Limits: one check per project (first found: tsc, cargo, go, then python), no baseline after a resume, a baseline needs the verifier baseline to have run. Type-check gaps: baseline run to catch callers broken in untouched files, count shell-changed files as modified (workspace diff, not edit tools), Go (`go vet`) and Python (pyright/mypy when configured) | a change that breaks an untouched caller blocks VERIFIED; opt-out stays | M | P2 |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:72:| VC-9 | **Partly done 2026-11-18** (audit: `docs/v1.2.1/VC-9-needs-input-audit.md`; glue: `cli/src/core/needs_input.ts`, `--answer`). Done: tool approval (write, exec, egress), verification-file edit, verifier and type-check approval end BLOCKED / NEEDS_INPUT with a question and resume with `--answer`. **Not done** (design decisions, see the audit): a requirement marked blocked (changes the REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE contract; free-text answer), an unresolved steering conflict (sidecar-only; resolve-after-the-fact), a subagent's question. Headless needs-input audit (Anthropic 2026 trends report, trend 4: agents that learn when to ask for help): list every path where a headless run needs an operator decision (steering that negates a requirement, a requirement marked blocked, a denied approval, a verification-file edit) and give each the same resumable outcome, a stable `needs_input` reason carrying the question and resumable with the answer; build only the missing glue | each path ends BLOCKED with a machine-readable question and resumes with an answer; no path guesses | S | P2 |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:105:| CX-2 | Compaction state stored separately from the canonical transcript and validated by a hash of the covered prefix on resume (reference: Cline `sdk/ARCHITECTURE.md:643-665`); the record names the covered event ids, the summary and where it is inserted, so a compaction can be audited and undone (reference: OpenHands `Condensation` event, docs 2026-11-15) | resume with a corrupted compaction file falls back to the full transcript; the record lists the covered ids | M | P1 |\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:144:| RD-6 | Session fork (reference: Cline `core/src/session/fork-metadata.ts`) | fork test: two divergent continuations, both resumable | M | P2 | Note 2026-11-18: PARTIAL. Done: `SessionManager.forkSession(sourceId, {atMessage?, newId?})` (`cli/src/session.ts`) and `/fork [message-count]` in the TUI catalogue and the REPL. The source is only read (tests compare its record, message log and archive byte for byte after a fork and after the fork continues). The cut backs up to the last complete tool exchange. Compactions whose summary is still in the kept conversation keep their record and archive lines (copied verbatim, so `auditCompactionsOnResume` verifies the fork); a compaction whose summary the cut removed is left out of the fork (otherwise resume would undo it into history the operator did not choose). The fork records `forkedFrom`. Test: two divergent continuations, both resumable and both auditing clean. Decisions: the objective ledger is carried only by a fork of the whole conversation (a truncated fork never reached the source's later state); worktree binding, in-flight operation, provider recovery and last turn are not carried. Update 2026-11-18: the start flag is done: `nexus run --fork-session <task> [--fork-at <n>]` (task store, as `--resume`), `nexus repl --fork-session <id>` and `nexus --fork-session <id>` (opens the REPL, not the TUI: the TUI binary is not given a session to open). Flag errors (unknown source, bad `--fork-at`, `--fork-session` with `--resume`) exit 2. Forking a session bound to a worktree is REFUSED, by design: the binding names one checkout and a fork would share it (either session's merge or discard would pull it from under the other); `/fork` refuses while a worktree is active. Not done: carrying a worktree binding (needs a decision on creating a second checkout), keeping `forkedFrom` after the fork's own turns are saved, and an automated test of the REPL `/fork` worktree refusal (the TUI slash path is tested).\ndocs/v1.2.1/PLAN.md:283:The qualification evidence from 2026-10-12 and the v1.0.0 readiness document were read on 2026-11-16 (DH-5); the October findings were re-checked against current `main` by grep only, nothing was built or run, and the qualification files themselves were made against an October build, so they are not evidence of current behaviour. Peer behaviour is as read in source on the clone dates in `GAP_ANALYSIS.md`; OpenHands was read at documentation level on 2026-11-15 (architecture, security, condenser and stuck-detection pages; not its source), the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report was read in full (a vendor document with no methodology and customer-reported figures), and Claude Code was not read. Still missing: any measurement that instruction files or tool-output clearing change outcomes, and any record of a multi-hour run with a resume (MQ-8).\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:19:| VC-6 | Baseline for untouched callers, shell-changed files, `go vet`, pyright and mypy, `UNAVAILABLE` for a missing tool | One check runs per project (tsc, then cargo, go, python); a resumed task has no baseline; cargo is excluded from the baseline as not cheap |\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:20:| VC-9 | Audit with file:line for 14 paths; BLOCKED/NEEDS_INPUT with a machine-readable question and `--answer` resume for tool approvals, verification-file edits and the verifier or type-check at completion; a delegated subagent's question is returned to the parent and ends the parent's headless run BLOCKED/NEEDS_INPUT (`spawn_subagent` only); the requirement-verifier approval has its own test | A requirement marked blocked (changes the `REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE` contract and needs a free-text answer); an unresolved steering conflict (sidecar protocol decision) |\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:24:| RD-6 | `SessionManager.forkSession` and `/fork [n]` (source never mutated, compaction archive verified on resume); `--fork-session`/`--fork-at` on `run`, `repl` and the top level; a worktree-bound session is refused | Carrying a worktree binding into a fork (today it is refused: a fork would share the checkout; needs a decision on making a second checkout); `forkedFrom` is lost once the fork's own turns are saved; the REPL `/fork` worktree refusal has no automated test (the `--fork-session` flag is done: run, repl, top level) |\ndocs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md:45:- Headless review-mode runs that need an approval nobody can give now end `BLOCKED` with `NEEDS_INPUT` and a machine-readable question (resume with `nexus run --resume <task> --answer <id>=approve|decline`); before, the model could route around the refusal. `--yes` and auto runs and subagents are unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":903963116}},"started_at_ms":1795149109978,"completed_at_ms":1795149110883}}
