{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:34:09.945Z","ordinal":30325,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3cb1ce21-5a9b-4cd8-b240-d17a74125280","process_id":"37792","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff origin/main...origin/v1/v1.2x-cs6-pin-servers -- .github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff origin/main...origin/v1/v1.2x-cs6-pin-servers -- .github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml b/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\nindex f3d9de6c..09b7296c 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\n@@ -5,9 +5,8 @@ name: LSP real servers\n # The ordinary suite exercises the client only against a fake server. Not a required check. See docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n # for what it covers and what it does not.\n #\n-# typescript-language-server and pyright are installed with npm at pinned versions and are REQUIRED here\n-# (NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE): a missing one fails the job. rust-analyzer and gopls are best-effort installs; if one cannot be\n-# installed its case skips with a reason in the log.\n+# All four real servers and their language toolchains are pinned and REQUIRED here (NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE): a missing or\n+# unusable server fails the job instead of silently reducing coverage.\n on:\n   schedule:\n     - cron: \"17 4 * * 1\"\n@@ -29,26 +28,25 @@ jobs:\n       - uses: actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1 # v7.1.0\n         with:\n           node-version: 22.22.1\n+      - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n+        with:\n+          go-version: 1.27.4\n       # Installed system-wide (npm -g puts them on an absolute PATH entry): the tests run under a throwaway HOME, where\n       # per-user installs (pip --user) are invisible (the MQ-3 first-run failure).\n       - name: Install typescript-language-server and pyright\n         run: npm install --global --no-audit --no-fund typescript@5.6.3 typescript-language-server@4.3.4 pyright@1.1.390\n-      - name: Install rust-analyzer (best effort)\n-        continue-on-error: true\n+      - name: Install pinned rust-analyzer toolchain\n         run: |\n-          # The product launches the server in a fixture directory outside this repository, where rustup uses the DEFAULT toolchain,\n-          # not the one the repository's rust-toolchain.toml pins: add the component there (from a directory with no override).\n-          (cd \"$RUNNER_TEMP\" && rustup component add rust-analyzer)\n+          # The product launches the server in a fixture outside this repository. Pin its default rustup toolchain there too.\n+          rustup toolchain install 1.95.0 --profile minimal --component rust-analyzer\n+          rustup default 1.95.0\n           # The rustup proxy finds its toolchain through RUSTUP_HOME / CARGO_HOME; the tests' throwaway HOME hides the defaults.\n           echo \"RUSTUP_HOME=$(rustup show home)\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n           echo \"CARGO_HOME=${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n-      - name: Install gopls (best effort)\n-        continue-on-error: true\n+      - name: Install pinned gopls\n         run: |\n-          # Not pinned: an old gopls stops building when the runner image moves to a newer Go (gopls v0.16.2 failed to build on 2026-11-18); this job exists to meet the current servers.\n-          # @latest may need a newer Go than the runner has and download that toolchain; the proxy can fail transiently (a stream error on 2026-11-18), so retry.\n           for attempt in 1 2 3; do\n-            GOBIN=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/gobin\" go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@latest && break\n+            GOBIN=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/gobin\" go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@v0.24.0 && break\n             [ \"$attempt\" = 3 ] && exit 1\n             sleep 15\n           done\ndiff --git a/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md b/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\nindex 75d0db3b..4e883069 100644\n--- a/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n+++ b/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ cd cli && node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts\n NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE=1 node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts   # missing server = failure\n ```\n \n-The suite runs under a throwaway HOME, so a tool installed only for the current user (`pip install --user`, `~/.cargo/bin` reached through the real HOME) is invisible. The workflow installs with `npm -g`, and sets `RUSTUP_HOME` and `CARGO_HOME` for the rustup proxy.\n+The suite runs under a throwaway HOME, so a tool installed only for the current user (`pip install --user`, `~/.cargo/bin` reached through the real HOME) is invisible. The workflow installs with `npm -g`, and sets `RUSTUP_HOME` and `CARGO_HOME` for the rustup proxy. The real-server workflow pins Node 22.22.1, Go 1.27.4, Rust 1.95.0 with its rust-analyzer component, gopls v0.24.0, TypeScript 5.6.3, typescript-language-server 4.3.4, and pyright 1.1.390. All four servers are required; an installation or startup failure fails the run.\n \n ## What it found\n \n@@ -38,3 +38,7 @@ The first real run showed the default launch commands for TypeScript, JavaScript\n - **Three-file navigation extension:** hosted run [44606102675](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44606102675) on commit `99c6049f` (2026-11-19) passed all 10 tests with `NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE=typescript,python,go,rust`: all four real servers passed the diagnostics and navigation cases, with 0 failures, skips, or todos. This is a small three-source-file chain, not evidence for large-project behavior.\n - **Hover and definition (CS-6 follow-up):** each real server is asked, through the product, to hover and go to the definition through a three-source-file project (positions are 1-based, as `lsp_hover` and `lsp_definition` take them); the call is retried until the case timeout because servers answer only after analysis, and the definition must point into the defining file. This checks a small import/re-export chain; it does not establish behavior on large projects.\n - **Cost and limit:** a first Rust diagnostics call on a large crate can take as long as the project load, and is bounded by the caller's timeout, after which the existing \"published no diagnostics\" `unavailable` applies. Later calls return as soon as progress is quiet. A change to an already-open file is not waited on separately: the latest published list is returned.\n+\n+## Pinned hosted environment (2026-11-20)\n+\n+The workflow now pins the Go toolchain and gopls to Go 1.27.4 and gopls v0.24.0, matching hosted run [44606741719](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44606741719), which resolved those versions and passed all four real-server cases. It installs Rust 1.95.0 with the rust-analyzer component and makes that the default toolchain because the product starts rustup's proxy from fixture directories outside the repository. The workflow makes TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust mandatory, so setup drift cannot silently turn a missing server into a skipped test. The updated workflow itself still requires a fresh hosted run before this change is considered verified.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":35901}},"started_at_ms":1795149249944,"completed_at_ms":1795149249944}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:34:10.096Z","ordinal":30326,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f73b-be2f-7a92-a19f-db769cbe3fda","call_id":"call_6aeddcc062fd4fc0bdc62073bde94f66","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml b/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\nindex f3d9de6c..09b7296c 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/lsp-real-servers.yml\n@@ -5,9 +5,8 @@ name: LSP real servers\n # The ordinary suite exercises the client only against a fake server. Not a required check. See docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n # for what it covers and what it does not.\n #\n-# typescript-language-server and pyright are installed with npm at pinned versions and are REQUIRED here\n-# (NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE): a missing one fails the job. rust-analyzer and gopls are best-effort installs; if one cannot be\n-# installed its case skips with a reason in the log.\n+# All four real servers and their language toolchains are pinned and REQUIRED here (NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE): a missing or\n+# unusable server fails the job instead of silently reducing coverage.\n on:\n   schedule:\n     - cron: \"17 4 * * 1\"\n@@ -29,26 +28,25 @@ jobs:\n       - uses: actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1 # v7.1.0\n         with:\n           node-version: 22.22.1\n+      - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n+        with:\n+          go-version: 1.27.4\n       # Installed system-wide (npm -g puts them on an absolute PATH entry): the tests run under a throwaway HOME, where\n       # per-user installs (pip --user) are invisible (the MQ-3 first-run failure).\n       - name: Install typescript-language-server and pyright\n         run: npm install --global --no-audit --no-fund typescript@5.6.3 typescript-language-server@4.3.4 pyright@1.1.390\n-      - name: Install rust-analyzer (best effort)\n-        continue-on-error: true\n+      - name: Install pinned rust-analyzer toolchain\n         run: |\n-          # The product launches the server in a fixture directory outside this repository, where rustup uses the DEFAULT toolchain,\n-          # not the one the repository's rust-toolchain.toml pins: add the component there (from a directory with no override).\n-          (cd \"$RUNNER_TEMP\" && rustup component add rust-analyzer)\n+          # The product launches the server in a fixture outside this repository. Pin its default rustup toolchain there too.\n+          rustup toolchain install 1.95.0 --profile minimal --component rust-analyzer\n+          rustup default 1.95.0\n           # The rustup proxy finds its toolchain through RUSTUP_HOME / CARGO_HOME; the tests' throwaway HOME hides the defaults.\n           echo \"RUSTUP_HOME=$(rustup show home)\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n           echo \"CARGO_HOME=${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n-      - name: Install gopls (best effort)\n-        continue-on-error: true\n+      - name: Install pinned gopls\n         run: |\n-          # Not pinned: an old gopls stops building when the runner image moves to a newer Go (gopls v0.16.2 failed to build on 2026-11-18); this job exists to meet the current servers.\n-          # @latest may need a newer Go than the runner has and download that toolchain; the proxy can fail transiently (a stream error on 2026-11-18), so retry.\n           for attempt in 1 2 3; do\n-            GOBIN=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/gobin\" go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@latest && break\n+            GOBIN=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/gobin\" go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@v0.24.0 && break\n             [ \"$attempt\" = 3 ] && exit 1\n             sleep 15\n           done\ndiff --git a/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md b/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\nindex 75d0db3b..4e883069 100644\n--- a/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n+++ b/docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md\n@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ cd cli && node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts\n NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE=1 node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts   # missing server = failure\n ```\n \n-The suite runs under a throwaway HOME, so a tool installed only for the current user (`pip install --user`, `~/.cargo/bin` reached through the real HOME) is invisible. The workflow installs with `npm -g`, and sets `RUSTUP_HOME` and `CARGO_HOME` for the rustup proxy.\n+The suite runs under a throwaway HOME, so a tool installed only for the current user (`pip install --user`, `~/.cargo/bin` reached through the real HOME) is invisible. The workflow installs with `npm -g`, and sets `RUSTUP_HOME` and `CARGO_HOME` for the rustup proxy. The real-server workflow pins Node 22.22.1, Go 1.27.4, Rust 1.95.0 with its rust-analyzer component, gopls v0.24.0, TypeScript 5.6.3, typescript-language-server 4.3.4, and pyright 1.1.390. All four servers are required; an installation or startup failure fails the run.\n \n ## What it found\n \n@@ -38,3 +38,7 @@ The first real run showed the default launch commands for TypeScript, JavaScript\n - **Three-file navigation extension:** hosted run [44606102675](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44606102675) on commit `99c6049f` (2026-11-19) passed all 10 tests with `NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE=typescript,python,go,rust`: all four real servers passed the diagnostics and navigation cases, with 0 failures, skips, or todos. This is a small three-source-file chain, not evidence for large-project behavior.\n - **Hover and definition (CS-6 follow-up):** each real server is asked, through the product, to hover and go to the definition through a three-source-file project (positions are 1-based, as `lsp_hover` and `lsp_definition` take them); the call is retried until the case timeout because servers answer only after analysis, and the definition must point into the defining file. This checks a small import/re-export chain; it does not establish behavior on large projects.\n - **Cost and limit:** a first Rust diagnostics call on a large crate can take as long as the project load, and is bounded by the caller's timeout, after which the existing \"published no diagnostics\" `unavailable` applies. Later calls return as soon as progress is quiet. A change to an already-open file is not waited on separately: the latest published list is returned.\n+\n+## Pinned hosted environment (2026-11-20)\n+\n+The workflow now pins the Go toolchain and gopls to Go 1.27.4 and gopls v0.24.0, matching hosted run [44606741719](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44606741719), which resolved those versions and passed all four real-server cases. It installs Rust 1.95.0 with the rust-analyzer component and makes that the default toolchain because the product starts rustup's proxy from fixture directories outside the repository. The workflow makes TypeScript, Python, Go, and Rust mandatory, so setup drift cannot silently turn a missing server into a skipped test. The updated workflow itself still requires a fresh hosted run before this change is considered verified.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","create_time":1795149250.0959556}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":13386,"sampled_through_sequence":13383,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
