{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:40:36.182Z","ordinal":30485,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_05793ea695c2aa2c016affcf42abb087d2b57d31a34ee583fe","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found a narrower, safe VC-6 improvement: when no trusted type-check baseline exists, diagnostics in untouched files can currently be labelled `PREEXISTING` even though Nexus cannot know whether they predate the task. I’ll make that case explicit and blocking for enforced checks, while leaving clean results and known pre-existing diagnostics with an actual baseline unchanged. This avoids trusting mutable saved state."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":80,"started_at_ms":1795149634800,"completed_at_ms":1795149636181}}
