/lsp-progress\",\"number\":619,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"feat(lsp): progress-aware diagnostics for staged servers: Rust no longer reports a broken file as clean\"},{\"headRefName\":\"v1/rust-ra\",\"number\":618,\"state\":\"CLOSED\",\"title\":\"fix(ci): real language-server job: Rust default-toolchain component, gopls@latest; record the rust-analyzer diagnosis\"},{\"headRefName\":\"v1/lsp-fix\",\"number\":617,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"fix(ci): language-server job requires typescript/python/go, Rust as a todo; record hosted results (CS-6, MQ-3)\"},{\"headRefName\":\"v1/cs6\",\"number\":616,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"test(lsp): real language servers in a non-required weekly job (CS-6); fix missing --stdio\"},{\"headRefName\":\"v1/backlog2\",\"number\":615,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"docs(v1.2.2): backlog update after the unit PRs landed\"},{\"headRefName\":\"v1/smoke-fix\",\"number\":614,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"fix(ci): real-project smoke: system-wide pytest and a probe that sees the isolated HOME (MQ-3)\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":560795183}},"started_at_ms":1795150743717,"completed_at_ms":1795150744279}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T04:59:04.424Z","ordinal":31202,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1f752-8b67-7c22-a967-927ac01189c5","call_id":"call_927700b65add4a2b9419b98d758bc350","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4269)\nTotal output lines: 212\n\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n## v1/invariants-audit...origin/main [ahead 35, behind 173]\n9fa18cfd (HEAD -> v1/invariants-audit, v1/invariants-impl) eval: deep pilot config uses the model's advertised 12288 output limit\n9b05ac1d eval: pilot config for the second gateway model (engineering/deep)\ne743ac2d fix(cli): report a connection that cannot make tool calls even when required (I-PROVIDER-3, EI-6)\nc9cc1139 eval: second live change-cost run (10 per cell): base and branch tie at 37/50; run 1 gap did not replicate\n7aa7414a eval: cc-deliberate-abstraction objective says quotes are not part of the value\nfae50f80 eval: five change-cost tasks and the first live run (base 14/25, branch 20/25; suggestive, n=5 per cell)\n9b3aa434 docs(tasks): Node 22 full suite on the final tree\n91f69fb1 docs(tasks): final regression record\nf7aa3919 docs: no document claims a hash-chained audit; correct the gap table\n492033e6 docs: decide EI-7 (spine hooks stay extension seams; guards stay), tidy known-gaps table\n .github/workflows/ci.yml                           |   1 +\n AGENTS.md                                          |   6 +\n CHANGELOG.md                                       |   3 +\n cli/src/agent.ts                                   |  57 +++++-\n cli/src/client.ts                                  |  30 ++-\n cli/src/config.ts                                  |   5 +-\n cli/src/core/capability_definitions/browser.ts     |   5 +-\n cli/src/core/extension_capabilities.ts             |  39 ++++\n cli/src/core/independent_review.ts                 |  67 +++++-\n cli/src/core/models_refresh.ts                     |   6 +-\n cli/src/core/operation.ts                          |   8 +-\n cli/src/core/operation_identity.ts                 |  29 +++\n cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts                   |  25 ++-\n cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts         |  13 +-\n cli/src/core/operation_runner_persistence.ts       |  10 +-\n cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts                   |  46 ++++-\n cli/src/core/scheduler.ts                          |   6 +\n cli/src/core/spine.ts                              |  42 +++-\n cli/src/core/state.ts                              |   4 +\n cli/src/credentials.ts                             |   9 +-\n cli/src/doctor.ts                                  |  10 +-\n cli/src/mcp.ts                                     |  65 ++++--\n cli/src/oauth.ts                                   |  20 +-\n cli/src/oauth_shared_refresh.ts                    |  58 ++++++\n cli/src/operation_cli.ts                           |  48 ++++-\n cli/src/plugins.ts                                 |   3 +-\n cli/src/security.ts                                |  20 +-\n cli/src/tools.ts                                   |   4 +-\n cli/src/types.ts                                   |   5 +\n cli/src/ui.ts                                      |   4 +-\n cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts                         |  26 ++-\n cli/src/workspace_trust.ts                         |   5 +-\n cli/test/ceri_semantic_integrity.test.ts           |  68 ++++++-\n cli/test/change_scope_prompt.test.ts               |  30 +++\n cli/test/client_robustness.test.ts                 |  25 +++\n cli/test/completion_receipt_binding.test.ts        |  69 +++++++\n cli/test/content_tool_call.test.ts                 |  36 ++++\n cli/test/doctor_lock_window.test.ts                |  48 +++++\n cli/test/dry_run_effects.test.ts                   |  62 ++++++\n cli/test/durable_private_writers.test.ts           |  47 +++++\n .../ceri/semantic_integrity.scenarios.json         |  96 +++++++++\n .../ceri/semantic_integrity.scenarios.sha256       |   2 +-\n cli