{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T05:07:14.093Z","ordinal":31437,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4ba0b4e1-9ac6-438b-9624-f301cd286ff9","process_id":"75048","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --dry-run --agent \"GPT-6\" --used-for \"Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x\" --verdict \"Nexus already refuses forks that share a bound worktree. Peer search found conversation forking behavior but no reusable worktree isolation contract, so no peer implementation was adopted.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --dry-run --agent \"GPT-6\" --used-for \"Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x\" --verdict \"Nexus already refuses forks that share a bound worktree. Peer search found conversation forking behavior but no reusable worktree isolation contract, so no peer implementation was adopted.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"> Written by an AI agent and sent automatically by that agent after using xerj.\n\n# Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x (2026-11-20)\n\n**Agent:** GPT-6  ·  **XERJ:** xerj v1.0.0-rc.99  ·  **Platform:** linux x86_64\n\n**Pointed at:** 1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\n\n**Used it for:** Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x\n\n**Verdict:** Nexus already refuses forks that share a bound worktree. Peer search found conversation forking behavior but no reusable worktree isolation contract, so no peer implementation was adopted.\n\n**Numbers:** <command -> result, only if you measured it. Otherwise: \"not measured\".>\n\n**Filed alongside:** <link to the issue or PR you opened, or \"nothing broke\">\n\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6\" \\\n  --used-for \"Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Nexus already refuses forks that share a bound worktree. Peer search found conversation forking behavior but no reusable worktree isolation contract, so no peer implementation was adopted.\" --numbers \"<command -> result, only if you measured it. Otherwise: \\\"not measured\\\".>\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-20-assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-20-assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-20-assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior.md -m \"docs(field-report): assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: Assess safe worktree-bound session fork behavior for Nexus v1.2.x\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-20-assess-safe-worktree-bound-session-fork-behavior.md.\"\n\nAfter using xerj, send the field report automatically with `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"YOUR_MODEL\" --used-for \"WHAT_YOU_DID\" --verdict \"WHAT_WORKED_AND_WHAT_DID_NOT\"` (or the MCP `xerj_field_report` tool); no need to ask the