ecution_tracking.ts      |   6 +-\n cli/src/core/objective.ts               |   5 +\n cli/src/core/run_turn.ts                |  35 +++++--\n cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts          |   1 +\n cli/src/index.ts                        |  12 +--\n cli/src/parser.ts                       |  14 ++-\n cli/src/types.ts                        |  28 ++++--\n cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts  |  22 +++--\n cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts     |  16 ++--\n cli/test/harness.test.ts                |   9 +-\n cli/test/nonprogress_recovery.test.ts   |  13 ++-\n cli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts | 163 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts    |  51 +++++++++-\n cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts        |   1 +\n docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md       |  26 ++---\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md                     |  14 ++-\n 19 files changed, 434 insertions(+), 82 deletions(-)\ncli/src/agent.ts\ncli/src/client.ts\ncli/src/config.ts\ncli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts\ncli/src/core/objective.ts\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts\ncli/src/index.ts\ncli/src/parser.ts\ncli/src/types.ts\ncli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\ncli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts\ncli/test/harness.test.ts\ncli/test/nonprogress_recovery.test.ts\ncli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts\ncli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts\ncli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts\ndocs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:14:2. A continuation budget is evaluated against a local per-invocation step counter. Durable `cumulativeSteps` is reported but explicitly “never a limit”; starting a resumed turn constructs a fresh local step counter. Thus explicit `maxTotalSteps` and `maxTurnMinutes` do not bound a task across operator or process resumes (`cli/src/core/run_turn.ts:137-145`, `:220-267`, `:1019-1041`; `cli/src/core/turn.ts:348-359`).\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:114:1. Put a **task-level budget ledger** next to `ContinuationBudget` and durable objective/operation state. Pass the remaining budget into `runTurn`, subagents, provider recovery, tools and work-unit retries. Use monotonic elapsed time in-process and persisted elapsed/deadline accounting across restart. Preserve intentional resumability by requiring an operator-issued new budget when exhausted; do not silently reset it.\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:79:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:108:2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":54645497}},"started_at_ms":1795156111330,"completed_at_ms":1795156111385}}
