{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T06:29:35.108Z","ordinal":32464,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","response_id":"resp_05793ea695c2aa2c016affe8cac19887d2b9bf33c4f2c63003","usage":{"input_tokens":134711,"cached_input_tokens":133248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":205,"reasoning_output_tokens":33,"total_tokens":134916},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":51266955,"cached_input_tokens":50873984,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":93755,"reasoning_output_tokens":47980,"total_tokens":51360710},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":676102502,"cached_input_tokens":668727552,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1433831,"reasoning_output_tokens":754937,"total_tokens":677536333}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T06:29:36.107Z","ordinal":32465,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6b907e48-f0b0-4a0b-85d9-9c8d110a1828","process_id":"56489","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,85p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md; git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD; git log --oneline --reverse origin/main..HEAD; sed -n '1,260p' cli/src/core/objective.ts; rg -n 'cumulativeSteps|maxTotalSteps|maxTurnMinutes|totalRequests|deadline|budget' cli/src/agent.ts cli/src/core/run_turn.ts cli/src/core/objective.ts cli/src/client.ts | head -n 180"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-wp-p10-02-durable-budget","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,85p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md; git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD; git log --oneline --reverse origin/main..HEAD; sed -n '1,260p' cli/src/core/objective.ts; rg -n 'cumulativeSteps|maxTotalSteps|maxTurnMinutes|totalRequests|deadline|budget' cli/src/agent.ts cli/src/core/run_turn.ts cli/src/core/objective.ts cli/src/client.ts | head -n 180"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Power of Ten Remediation Implementation Specification\n\n**Planning baseline:** `origin/main` `a0329e72ea796a306ea138ab2870d15920e4af61`. This is an implementation handoff, not authorization to change production code. No dates are assigned.\n\n## Design constraints\n\nReuse `ContinuationBudget`, `ExecutionTracker`, `ProviderRecoveryController`, `ResourceRegistry`, `TurnResult`, completion-oracle receipts, `DurableStateManager`, `OperationStore`, `FlightRecorder`, and existing GitHub rulesets. Do not add a parallel orchestrator, verifier, or evidence store. Every work package must preserve non-success outcomes for interruption, unknown side effects, failed verification, and missing mandatory evidence.\n\n## WP-P10-01 — Protect the independent acceptance authority\n\n**Priority:** P0 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none.\n\n**Current operating constraint (2026-11-19):** This is a single-user repository; the nominated account is suspended and no second human reviewer is available. Keep the independent-approval acceptance criterion open and report it as unavailable. This does not block publishing PRs or progressing other work packages. Do not present self-approval, bot review, or green CI as independent human approval; any merge path that requires this gate remains subject to the repository's configured rules until the owner changes that policy.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** A candidate can modify `.github/workflows/ci.yml` or verifier/test harness definitions while the live branch ruleset requires zero approvals. The active ruleset requires checks but does not bind their implementation to an independently protected version. Evidence: GitHub ruleset 25340146 (read 2026-11-18); `.github/workflows/ci.yml`; `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts:75-160`.\n\n**Affected surfaces:** repository ruleset, `.github/CODEOWNERS`, workflow/test/verifier paths, PR template and documented merge policy.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Use GitHub’s existing ruleset and CODEOWNERS; do not build an in-repo policy service. Require at least one independent approval, require code-owner review for workflow, verifier, security policy, and CI harness changes, dismiss approvals after relevant pushes, require latest commit approval, and enable strict status checks. If supported by owner policy, run required checks from a protected reusable workflow pinned to a protected ref.\n\n**Implementation steps:**\n\n1. Enumerate the paths that define acceptance (`.github/workflows/**`, test runner scripts, verifier discovery/oracle code, security gate scripts, lockfiles/build config).\n2. Add CODEOWNERS for those paths; add tests that assert the path list matches governance documentation.\n3. Update ruleset to require review/code-owner approval and strict check freshness. Keep bypass actors empty or explicitly owner-controlled.\n4. Add a canary PR/harness mutation that removes a required check or makes it unconditional and demonstrate merge is blocked by independent policy.\n5. Document emergency bypass ownership and audit record.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** API readback confirms required approvals >=1, code-owner approval, strict status checks, no unapproved bypass actor. Seeded workflow change without approval cannot merge. A normal workflow change with independent approval and green required checks can merge. Exact SHA and ruleset JSON archived.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Existing open PRs may require new approvals and reruns. Rollback is ruleset restoration only by repository owner; retain the last known ruleset export. Residual risk: repository administrators can alter rulesets outside source control.\n\n## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\n\n**Priority:** P0 · **Complexity:** L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-01 recommended first; can be implemented independently.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** `DEFAULT_CONTINUATION` sets total steps and minutes to Infinity (`cli/src/types.ts:182-188`); `runTurnImpl` checks a local `currentStep` (`run_turn.ts:137-145,220-267`); `runSubagent` uses an unbounded `for (;;)` (`agent.ts:4440-4457`); resumed invocation recreates local counters while cumulative steps are observational only (`turn.ts:348-359`).\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `types.ts`, `config.ts`, `run_turn.ts`, subagent execution in `agent.ts`, provider recovery, tool deadlines, durable objective/task state, operation runner and CLI/UI reporting.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Extend `ContinuationBudget` and existing durable objective/operation records with a task budget id, maximum total steps/tool invocations/inference submissions/elapsed time/tokens, per-tool deadline and delegation depth. Persist consumed counters before/after side effects with `withDurableSync`. Child agents inherit the parent’s remaining budget; provider retry consumes the same inference allowance. A resumed task cannot regain budget. Require explicit operator-authorized budget renewal after exhaustion.\n\n**Implementation steps:**\n\n1. Define additive schema fields with migration defaults that do not silently claim prior counters are zero; old tasks resume in a conservative bounded mode or require explicit operator choice.\n2. Add a shared budget tracker passed through direct turns, subagents, work units, provider recovery and tool dispatch.\n3. Enforce before dispatch and before any retry; classify exhaustion as `BLOCKED`/`LIMIT_REACHED`, never `VERIFIED` or successful operation completion.\n4. Add ceilings for response streaming and whole-turn wall time, including a finite total timeout for local inference streams; idle timeout remains separate.\n5. Report dimension, configured limit, consumed amount and resume behavior in CLI/TUI result.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Model emits distinct writes indefinitely: run stops at exact step/tool/token/time budget with nonzero/non-success result. Nested subagent shares remaining budget. Repeated provider failures consume retry allowance. Exhaustion followed by process restart and resume does not reset counters. Resume near limit permits only remaining budget. A hung local tool and slow-drip stream stop by configured deadline. Budget persistence write failure prevents new side-effectful dispatch.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** New config defaults may shorten formerly unlimited runs; provide an explicit operator override with a hard documented maximum, not Infinity. Keep old records readable. Rollback must not turn persisted exhausted state into zero; older binaries should refuse unsupported budget schema versions. Residual risk: already-running external calls may finish after cancellation or have unknown outcomes.\n\n## WP-P10-03 — Acceptance evidence integrity and export\n\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-01 for independent policy identity.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** Flight events are append-only by convention, but append failures are ignored (`cli/src/flight.ts:77-108`); no chain/signature verification exists. `TurnResult` has `candidateId` and output SHA but not complete environment/policy identity (`cli/src/core/turn.ts:191-219`).\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `flight.ts`, `evidence.ts`, completion oracle, durable state and audit commands.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Add an evidence manifest to existing receipt/event structures. Chain each event over prior digest; include candidate tree/commit identity, verifier definition/config digest, command, tool/runtime versions, exit code, timestamp, actor/model/provider identity and policy version. Use an operator-supplied signing key only if explicitly configured; unsigned bundles must say “integrity checked, not signed.” Required acceptance evidence write failure must produce a visible non-success result; optional telemetry remains best effort and explicitly marked.\n\n**Implementation steps:**\n\n1. Define canonical event encoding and versioned manifest.\n2. Chain existing records and add offline `verify` over an exported bundle; do not duplicate existing state storage.\n3. Bind verification receipt to exact candidate and current policy/workflow identity.\n4. Add redaction before hashing/export and retention controls.\n5. Distinguish required acceptance receipts from optional flight telemetry.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Alter, delete, reorder, truncate or append an event; verification names the first broken sequence. Candidate mutation after verification invalidates receipt. Simulated disk-full/permission error prevents verified acceptance when the receipt is mandatory. Secret fixture remains absent from export. Exact manifest contains source revision, candidate digest, command, exit code and tool versions.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Legacy logs remain readable but classify `integrity=unverified_legacy`; never silently “upgrade” them to verified. Keep old export path read-only during migration. Residual risk: same-user can delete both evidence and local chain unless an external signed/immutable copy is retained.\n\n## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** Output/context and some sandbox process limits are bounded, but no product-wide active memory, session count, retained disk, provider token/spend or concurrent operation budget was demonstrated. Operation runner batches all ready assignments through `Promise.all` (`operation_runner.ts:276-299`).\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `core/resources.ts`, operation scheduler/runner, client leases, tool runner, durable state/compaction and process cleanup.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Add admission to existing `ResourceRegistry` and scheduler; cap concurrency by operator-configured memory/provider budget. Reuse Rust process registry, output ring buffer, sandbox pids limit, `client_lease`, per-operation lock and session archival. Do not create a parallel resource manager.\n cli/src/agent.ts                        |  67 ++++++++++++-\n cli/src/client.ts                       |  18 +++-\n cli/src/config.ts                       |  15 +--\n cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts      |   6 +-\n cli/src/core/objective.ts               |   5 +\n cli/src/core/run_turn.ts                |  35 +++++--\n cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts          |   1 +\n cli/src/index.ts                        |  12 +--\n cli/src/parser.ts                       |  14 ++-\n cli/src/types.ts                        |  28 ++++--\n cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts  |  22 +++--\n cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts     |  16 ++--\n cli/test/harness.test.ts                |   9 +-\n cli/test/nonprogress_recovery.test.ts   |  13 ++-\n cli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts | 163 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts    |  51 +++++++++-\n cli/test/verifier_gating.test.ts        |   1 +\n docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md       |  26 ++---\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md                     |  14 ++-\n 19 files changed, 434 insertions(+), 82 deletions(-)\n01a76010 fix(continuation): enforce durable finite step budget\na70ca2ec feat(agent): cap tool fan-out per response\ndc2b22ad fix(inference): enforce finite total request deadline\n113eb380 fix(agent): persist delegated task budget before inference\ncb46c4cc fix(agent): retain default step limit for programmatic callers\nfb92da2e test(agent): align recovery fixtures with shared budget\n/**\n * The objective ledger: what the operator asked for, and how far the work has got against it.\n *\n * The plan (`update_plan`) is the agent's own roadmap and may be coarser than the request. The ledger keeps the\n * request itself — verbatim — and the acceptance criteria seeded from it, so a reduced plan can never stand in for\n * them. Requirements change state only with evidence, scope changes are recorded explicitly, operator steering is\n * kept until applied, and verifier attempts are remembered against the exact workspace inputs they ran on.\n *\n * Pure data and pure functions; the agent owns persistence and presentation.\n */\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport type { VerificationStatus } from \"./turn.js\";\nimport { DEFAULT_CONVERGENCE_ATTEMPTS } from \"../types.js\";\nimport type { CanonicalCapability } from \"./capabilities.js\";\nimport { isFilteredVerifierCommand } from \"../tester.js\";\nimport { redactSecrets, safeTerminal } from \"../ui.js\";\nimport { replayObligations, type RegressionObligation, type ReferenceDeclaration, type DifferentialRecord } from \"./regression_obligations.js\";\nimport { createTracking, ExecutionTracker, normalizeTracking, type ExecutionTracking } from \"./execution_tracking.js\";\n\nexport const LEDGER_VERSION = 1;\nexport const PINNED_LEDGER_PREFIX = \"[Objective Ledger - pinned by Nexus; never summarised]\";\nexport const STEERING_PREFIX = \"[Operator steering\";\n/** Objectives longer than this are pinned in full only while the original message has left the context. */\nexport const MAX_PINNED_OBJECTIVE_CHARS = 24_000;\n/** Operator follow-ups and steering pinned verbatim, newest first, up to this many characters (or the block's budget). */\nconst MAX_PINNED_OPERATOR_CHARS = 12_000;\nconst MAX_REQUIREMENT_TEXT = 240;\nconst MAX_EVIDENCE_ITEMS = 6;\nconst MAX_EVIDENCE_CHARS = 300;\nconst MAX_VERIFIER_CHARS = 400;\nconst MAX_TEST_LINKS = 6;\nconst MAX_TEST_LINK_CHARS = 120;\n\nexport type RequirementKind = \"feature\" | \"constraint\" | \"invariant\";\nconst REQUIREMENT_KINDS: readonly string[] = [\"feature\", \"constraint\", \"invariant\"];\n\n/** Verifier and test-link text comes from the operator or the model: one line, no control characters, capped. */\nconst oneLine = (text: string) => text.replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\u2028\\u2029]+/g, \" \").trim();\nconst cleanLine = (text: string, max: number) => clip(oneLine(text), max);\n/** Text shown in the pinned ledger as a code span: nothing inside it can read as ledger structure. */\nconst span = (text: string, max: number) => `\\`${cleanLine(text, max).replace(/`/g, \"'\")}\\``;\n\n/** A command that exits 0 whatever the workspace holds checks nothing. */\nexport function isConstantVerifier(command: string): boolean {\n  return /^(?:true|:|exit\\s+0|\\/(?:usr\\/)?bin\\/true)$/.test(command.trim().replace(/\\s*;+\\s*$/, \"\"));\n}\n\n/** Constraints and invariants hold for the whole task; unlike a feature they are not done on the model's word. */\nexport function isHardRequirement(r: Pick<Requirement, \"kind\">): boolean {\n  return r.kind === \"constraint\" || r.kind === \"invariant\";\n}\n\n/** Claimed implemented, but neither verified by its own verifier nor accepted by the operator. */\nfunction unverifiedHard(r: Requirement): boolean {\n  return isHardRequirement(r) && r.status === \"implemented\" && r.operatorAccepted !== true;\n}\n\nexport type RequirementStatus = \"open\" | \"in_progress\" | \"implemented\" | \"verified\" | \"blocked\" | \"descoped\";\n/** Statuses that need no further work in this task. `blocked` is terminal for the turn but never \"done\". */\nexport const DONE_STATUSES: ReadonlySet<RequirementStatus> = new Set([\"implemented\", \"verified\", \"descoped\"]);\n\n/**\n * Done for the purpose of completion. Descoping reduces what the operator asked for, so only the operator can make\n * it count: a descoped operator or steering requirement stays unresolved until `operatorAccepted` is set (by the\n * operator's `/requirements accept`), while a sub-requirement the agent added itself may be descoped freely.\n */\nexport function requirementDone(r: Requirement): boolean {\n  if (r.status === \"verified\") return true;\n  if (r.status === \"implemented\") return !unverifiedHard(r);\n  return r.status === \"descoped\" && (r.source === \"model\" || r.operatorAccepted === true);\n}\n\nexport interface Requirement {\n  id: string;\n  /** Heading line (capped), for lists. */\n  text: string;\n  /** The requirement's complete wording from the operator's message (nested items included), never truncated. */\n  detail?: string;\n  status: RequirementStatus;\n  /** Absent means a feature (ledgers written before typed requirements). */\n  kind?: RequirementKind;\n  /** Command that checks a constraint or invariant; `verified` needs a passing run of it after the last change. */\n  verifier?: string;\n  /** Who set the verifier. One the model declared is advisory: its run is evidence, never `verified`. */\n  verifierSource?: \"operator\" | \"model\";\n  /** Tests (names or paths) that exercise this requirement. */\n  tests?: string[];\n  /** Where it came from: the operator's objective, operator steering, or the model (added sub-requirement). */\n  source: \"objective\" | \"steering\" | \"model\";\n  /** Implementation and validation evidence (file paths, commands, test names). */\n  evidence: string[];\n  /** Who produced each evidence item, keyed by its text. Items without an entry are the model's claim. */\n  evidenceSources?: Record<string, \"tool\" | \"model\">;\n  /** Reason for blocked/descoped; required for both. */\n  note?: string;\n  /** The operator accepted this requirement's descoping (only the operator's own command sets this). */\n  operatorAccepted?: boolean;\n  /**\n   * The passing verifier run that a `verified` status rests on, recorded on the then-current workspace. Nexus can\n   * show that this run passed on these inputs; it cannot prove the verifier exercises this particular requirement.\n   */\n  verifiedBy?: { attempt: number; command: string; inputs: string; at: string };\n  updatedAt: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ScopeChange {\n  at: string;\n  requirement: string;\n  from: RequirementStatus;\n  to: RequirementStatus;\n  reason: string;\n}\n\nexport interface SteeringRecord {\n  id: string;\n  text: string;\n  receivedAt: string;\n  status: \"queued\" | \"applied\" | \"cancelled\";\n  appliedAt?: string;\n  appliedAtStep?: number;\n}\n\n/** Steering that negates a requirement: held out of the conversation and the ledger until the operator decides. */\nexport interface SteeringConflict {\n  id: string;\n  text: string;\n  requirements: string[];\n  receivedAt: string;\n  /** `unresolved`: no operator was available, so the ledger is unchanged and the negation was not applied. */\n  status: \"pending\" | \"approved\" | \"declined\" | \"unresolved\";\n  decidedAt?: string;\n}\n\n/** Requirements of an earlier objective still unmet when a new request replaced it; the operator decides what happens to them. */\nexport interface SupersededObjective {\n  at: string;\n  objective: string;\n  objectiveSha256: string;\n  requirements: Array<{ id: string; text: string; status: RequirementStatus }>;\n  status: \"pending_decision\";\n}\n\nexport interface VerificationAttempt {\n  n: number;\n  command: string;\n  /** Candidate identity of the workspace the verifier ran on (tracked and untracked, non-ignored files). */\n  inputs: string;\n  /**\n   * What else must be unchanged before a prior failure is reused: the agent process that ran it, the count of\n   * mutating tool calls (any edit, write or shell command) at that time, and a fingerprint of inputs git ignores\n   * (PATH, dependency install markers, .env files).\n   */\n  epoch?: string;\n  mutationSeq?: number;\n  external?: string;\n  status: VerificationStatus | \"SKIPPED_UNCHANGED_INPUTS\";\n  isDeliverableBound?: boolean;\n  /** False when the run passed but nothing independent of the agent shows the change (see core/independent_check). */\n  independent?: boolean;\n  filtered?: boolean;\n  /** Set when the run was a constraint's own verifier: it is evidence for that requirement only, never a general test run. */\n  requirementId?: string;\n  at: string;\n  /** First failing line of the verifier's output, when it failed. */\n  failedCheck?: string;\n  /** ENVIRONMENT: the verifier could not run (tool missing, exit 126/127, sandbox error); it says nothing about the candidate. */\n  classification?: \"ENVIRONMENT\" | \"CANDIDATE_FAILED\";\n  /** The verifier process's exit code; absent when it never ran or was killed. */\n  exitCode?: number;\n  /** Names of the failing tests (redacted, capped). */\n  failingTests?: string[];\n  /** How many distinct failing tests the run named, uncapped (up to MAX_COUNTED_FAILING_TESTS); absent on older attempts. */\n  failingTotal?: number;\n  /** True when `failingTests` holds fewer names than the run reported. */\n  failingTruncated?: boolean;\n  /** Redacted tail of the verifier's output, capped at MAX_ATTEMPT_EXCERPT_BYTES. */\n  excerpt?: string;\n  /** Lineage (DV-4): the previous real attempt (a skipped re-report is never a parent) and the hash of the step from its inputs to these. */\n  parent?: number;\n  /** sha256 of `parent.inputs NUL inputs`: it identifies the transition between two candidate identities, it is not a content diff. */\n  diffHash?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ObjectiveOutcome {\n  status: \"completed\" | \"incomplete\" | \"blocked\";\n  reason: string;\n  failedCheck?: string;\n  remaining: string[];\n  nextAction?: string;\n  at: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ContinuationState {\n  /** Segments of `segmentSteps` steps the current turn has run (1 for an ordinary turn). */\n  segments: number;\n  /** Steps run against this objective across turns. */\n  totalSteps: number;\n  /** Step (within the current turn) of the last observed progress. */\n  lastProgressStep: number;\n  stopReason?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ObjectiveLedger {\n  version: number;\n  /** Work unit id when this ledger is scoped to a work unit in an operation or team (REQ-AGT-102/103). */\n  unitId?: string;\n  objective: string;\n  objectiveSha256: string;\n  startedAt: string;\n  requirements: Requirement[];\n  scopeChanges: ScopeChange[];\n  steering: SteeringRecord[];\n  steeringConflicts?: SteeringConflict[];\n  superseded?: SupersededObjective[];\n  verification: VerificationAttempt[];\n  /** Operator-authorised regression obligations (core/regression_obligations.ts); absent in ledgers written before DV-3. */\n  obligations?: RegressionObligation[];\n  /** Operator-authorised behavioural references, by requirement (DV-4 gate). */\n  references?: ReferenceDeclaration[];\n  /** Latest VC-3 differential run per requirement; finite agreement, never equivalence. */\n  differentials?: DifferentialRecord[];\n  continuation: ContinuationState;\n  /** The model's own statement of what comes next (update_requirements next_action). */\n  nextAction?: string;\n  /** Attempts numbered up to this were already judged non-converging and stopped the work; the next judgement starts after it. */\n  convergenceResetAfter?: number;\n  outcome?: ObjectiveOutcome;\n  /** Short follow-up messages the operator sent as new turns while this objective was unresolved. */\n  amendments: Array<{ at: string; text: string }>;\n  /**\n   * Objective-scoped execution tracking (core/execution_tracking.ts): cumulative steps, progress, repetition,\n   * failed approaches, interventions and compactions. Absent in ledgers written before it existed; `trackingOf` fills it.\n   */\n  execution?: ExecutionTracking;\n}\n\n/** The ledger's execution tracking, created (or completed, for a ledger restored from an earlier version) on first use. */\nexport function trackingOf(ledger: ObjectiveLedger): ExecutionTracker {\n  ledger.execution = normalizeTracking(ledger.execution);\n  // `ContinuationState.totalSteps` predates the richer execution record. Preserve its count when resuming a legacy\n  // task instead of normalizing a missing execution field to a false zero and granting fresh budget.\n  if (Number.isSafeInteger(ledger.continuation?.totalSteps) && ledger.continuation.totalSteps > ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps) {\n    ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps = ledger.continuation.totalSteps;\n  }\n  return new ExecutionTracker(ledger.execution);\n}\n\nconst now = () => new Date().toISOString();\nconst sha256 = (text: string) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(text).digest(\"hex\");\nconst clip = (text: string, max: number) => (text.length <= max ? text : `${text.slice(0, max - 1)}…`);\n\n/**\n * Acceptance criteria as written: top-level numbered items (`1.`, `2)`, `R3:`) of the objective. Each keeps its\n * heading line; the full wording stays in the verbatim objective. Fewer than two items means the objective is a\n * single request and is tracked as one requirement.\n */\nexport function seedRequirements(objective: string): Array<{ id: string; text: string; detail: string; kind?: RequirementKind; verifier?: string; verifierSource?: \"operator\"; note?: string }> {\n  const lines = objective.replace(/\\r\\n?/g, \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\");\n  const items: Array<{ indent: number; text: string; line: number }> = [];\n  lines.forEach((line, index) => {\ncli/src/client.ts:351:/** Whole-inference deadline, including streams that continue sending chunks and never become idle. */\ncli/src/client.ts:899:   * budgeted: a resend that fails again is charged to its endpoint and kind of request (probe or POST), at most\ncli/src/client.ts:902:   * stale connections each still get their resend. Once the budget is spent the failure is reported as any other.\ncli/src/client.ts:911:        // Only an answer that is not a server error hands the budget back: a 5xx means the server was reached and unhealthy.\ncli/src/client.ts:925:    let budget = this.staleResends.get(key);\ncli/src/client.ts:926:    if (!budget || now - budget.since > STALE_RESEND_WINDOW_MS) budget = { used: 0, since: now };\ncli/src/client.ts:927:    if (failedResend) budget.used++;\ncli/src/client.ts:928:    this.staleResends.set(key, budget);\ncli/src/client.ts:929:    return budget.used < STALE_RESEND_BUDGET;\ncli/src/client.ts:1132:  /** The clock of the resend budget; a test replaces it. */\ncli/src/client.ts:1144:    // A zero or invalid setting cannot disable the whole-request deadline. Keep the first-byte and idle\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:25:/** Operator follow-ups and steering pinned verbatim, newest first, up to this many characters (or the block's budget). */\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:241:  // task instead of normalizing a missing execution field to a false zero and granting fresh budget.\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:242:  if (Number.isSafeInteger(ledger.continuation?.totalSteps) && ledger.continuation.totalSteps > ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps) {\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:243:    ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps = ledger.continuation.totalSteps;\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:979:  budgetChars = MAX_PINNED_OBJECTIVE_CHARS,\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:985:    if (ledger.objective.length <= budgetChars) {\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:991:        `Operator objective (${ledger.objective.length} chars; the original message left the context and the whole text exceeds this block's budget). ` +\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:994:      let room = budgetChars;\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:1013:  // Operator follow-ups and steering are carried verbatim, newest first within their budget; what does not fit is named\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:1020:  let operatorRoom = Math.min(MAX_PINNED_OPERATOR_CHARS, budgetChars);\ncli/src/core/objective.ts:1165:  out.push(\"Recovery budget:\", `- ${remaining} refusal(s) left of ${r.allowedDenials} in episode ${r.episode}; another refused attempt beyond that stops the turn${stagnation}.`);\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:103:  // Step notices speak for the turn that issued them; this turn has its own step budget.\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:141:  const budget = this.config.continuation;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:143:  const maxTotalSteps = budget ? budget.maxTotalSteps : segmentSteps;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:221:    // Continuation: `maxSteps` is a segment, a durable checkpoint. The total-step budget is objective-scoped and\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:224:    const turnDeadline = budget && Number.isFinite(budget.maxTurnMinutes) ? Date.now() + budget.maxTurnMinutes * 60_000 : Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:230:    const allowedDenials = budget ? Math.max(1, budget.maxRecoveries) : 0;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:237:        tracker.operatorInput(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, `operator follow-up: ${promptText.slice(0, 160)}`);\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:259:      const taskStepLimitReached = budget\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:260:        ? tracker.data.cumulativeSteps >= maxTotalSteps\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:261:        : currentStep > maxTotalSteps;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:263:        stopReason = budget ? \"STEP_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\" : \"STEP_LIMIT_REACHED\";\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:264:        stopDetail = budget\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:265:          ? `objective step limit ${maxTotalSteps} reached (${tracker.data.cumulativeSteps} steps consumed across runs)`\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:271:        stopDetail = `operator time limit ${budget!.maxTurnMinutes} min`;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:274:      if (budget && tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress >= budget.stagnationSteps) {\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:279:        tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"no_progress\", stopDetail);\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:288:      // and notice paths alike; a stop set by the cycle or by the checks above (STAGNATION_DETECTED, a budget, a cancel)\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:310:      if (budget && currentStep > 1 && (currentStep - 1) % segmentSteps === 0) {\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:324:      if (this.objective && this.durable) this.objective.continuation.totalSteps = tracker.data.cumulativeSteps;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:326:      // consumed budget, stop here: a resume must not repeat an unaccounted request.\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:328:        persistenceFailure = this.turnPersistenceFailures.at(-1) ?? \"The objective step budget could not be saved before inference.\";\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:423:        if (!budget) return;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:444:        const transition = tracker.recordUnproductive(cumulativeStep, verdict.record.action, inputState, budget.maxRecoveries, allowedDenials);\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:454:          this.observer?.onContinuation?.({ kind: \"recovery\", n: transition.note, max: budget.maxRecoveries, detail: name });\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:456:        const header = `[Nexus recovery ${transition.note}/${budget.maxRecoveries}] You have ${what} on an unchanged workspace and received the same result each time. Repeating it will not change the outcome.`;\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:463:              ? ` The RECOVERY_REQUIRED section of the pinned objective ledger lists the evidence you already have, what is refused, what is permitted and the budget left; it is kept current on every request.`\ncli/src/core/run_turn.ts:464:              : `\\n\\n${this.recoveryContext(tracker, budget.stagnationSteps, promptTex