currentStep, \"subagent\", onConfirm);\n4687:  private async submitGenAiRequest<T>(client: LocalLlmClient, submit: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n    // the workspace path and project sections must not sit above the operating rules.\n    return `You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\nYou solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by iteratively exploring, reading, editing, and verifying files.\n\n### Operating Rules:\n1. EXPLORE FIRST: Before editing files, always explore the workspace using \\`file_tree\\`, \\`list_dir\\`, \\`find_files\\`, \\`search_code\\`, or \\`read_file\\`. For large files, use \\`outline_file\\` first to inspect class/function signatures without loading the entire file into context.\n2. HIGH-EFFICIENCY BATCHING: Prefer \\`batch_read\\` to read multiple files concurrently in a single turn, and \\`file_info\\` to inspect metadata without loading whole files.\n3. PRECISE EDITS & PATCHES: When modifying existing files, use \\`edit_file\\` with unique snippets or \\`patch_file\\` with unified diffs.\n4. PLANNING: Use \\`update_plan\\` only for work with three or more distinct phases (not for a fix and its test); update it alongside other tool calls.\n5. VERIFICATION: After making code changes, use \\`run_command\\` with bash/zsh commands to run tests, builds, or linting (e.g. \\`cargo check\\`, \\`cargo test\\`, \\`npm test\\`, \\`pytest\\`).\n6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\n7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke \\`task_completed\\` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\n8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\n${fewShotSection}${tddSection}${roleSection}\nAlways explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\n\n### Shell Environment:\n- Active Shell: ${this.config.shell} (standard GNU/Linux shell environment)\n- Workspace directory: ${this.config.workspace}\n${verifierCommand ? `- Test command (Nexus verifies with it): \\`${verifierCommand}\\`\\n` : \"\"}${this.objective?.requirements.length ? `\n### Acceptance Requirements:\nThe pinned Objective Ledger lists the operator's requirements; your plan never replaces them. Record progress with \\`update_requirements\\` (implemented/verified only with evidence; blocked/descoped only with a reason). Steering messages from the operator apply on top of the objective.\n` : \"\"}${rulesSection}${skillsSection}${knowledgeSection}\n\n${NEXUS_RUNTIME_IDENTITY}`;\n  }\n\n  private setupSpineHandlers(): void {\n    return setupSpineHandlersImpl.call(this);\n  }\n\n  private async dispatchToolCall(\n    call: ToolCall,\n    currentStep: number,\n    actor: \"agent\" | \"subagent\" = \"agent\",\n    onConfirm?: ConfirmHandler\n  ): Promise<{ receipt: ExecutionReceipt; shouldExit: boolean }> {\n    const toolName = call.function.name;\n    const span = this.safeStartTraceSpan(\"nexus.agent.tool\", {\n      \"nexus.tool.name\": toolName,\n      \"nexus.tool.actor\": actor,\n      \"nexus.tool.step\": currentStep,\n    });\n    try {\n      const result = await this.dispatchToolCallImpl(call, currentStep, actor, onConfirm);\n      this.safeEndTraceSpan(span, result.receipt.success ? \"ok\" : \"error\", {\n        \"nexus.tool.success\": result.receipt.success,\n        \"nexus.tool.duration_ms\": result.receipt.durationMs,\n      });\n      return result;\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.safeEndTraceSpan(span, \"error\", { \"nexus.tool.success\": false });\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n\n  private async dispatchToolCallImpl(\n    call: ToolCall,\n    currentStep: number,\n    actor: \"agent\" | \"subagent\" = \"agent\",\n    onConfirm?: ConfirmHandler\n  ): Promise<{ receipt: ExecutionReceipt; shouldExit: boolean }> {\n    return dispatchToolCallImpl.call(this, call, currentStep, actor, onConfirm);\n  }\n\n  private workspaceAvailableBytes(): number | null {\n    try {\n      const stats = fs.statfsSync(this.config.workspace);\n      const available = Number(stats.bavail) * Number(stats.bsize);\n      return Number.isSafeInteger(available) && available >= 0 ? available : null;\n    } catch {\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Operator stop request. This is an authority event: once recorded, no new inference request or tool\n   * dispatch is admitted for the active turn. A command already running is ended by the runner (its whole process\n   * group, through the bridge's turn signal) and awaited until it settles; background processes earlier commands of\n   * this session left running are ended too (REQ-AGT-109).\n   * Returns false when no turn is active or cancellation was already requested.\n   */\n  public requestCancel(reason: string = \"operator\"): boolean {\n    const turn = this.activeTurn;\n    if (!turn || turn.cancelRequestedAt) return false;\n    turn.cancelRequestedAt = new Date().toISOString();\nexport interface ContinuationState {\n  /** Segments of `segmentSteps` steps the current turn has run (1 for an ordinary turn). */\n  segments: number;\n  /** Steps run against this objective across turns. */\n  totalSteps: number;\n  /** Step (within the current turn) of the last observed progress. */\n  lastProgressStep: number;\n  stopReason?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ObjectiveLedger {\n  version: number;\n  /** Work unit id when this ledger is scoped to a work unit in an operation or team (REQ-AGT-102/103). */\n  unitId?: string;\n  objective: string;\n  objectiveSha256: string;\n  startedAt: string;\n  requirements: Requirement[];\n  scopeChanges: ScopeChange[];\n  steering: SteeringRecord[];\n  steeringConflicts?: SteeringConflict[];\n  superseded?: SupersededObjective[];\n  verification: VerificationAttempt[];\n  /** Operator-authorised regression obligations (core/regression_obligations.ts); absent in ledgers written before DV-3. */\n  obligations?: RegressionObligation[];\n  /** Operator-authorised behavioural references, by requirement (DV-4 gate). */\n  references?: ReferenceDeclaration[];\n  /** Latest VC-3 differential run per requirement; finite agreement, never equivalence. */\n  differentials?: DifferentialRecord[];\n  continuation: ContinuationState;\n  /** The model's own statement of what comes next (update_requirements next_action). */\n  nextAction?: string;\n  /** Attempts numbered up to this were already judged non-converging and stopped the work; the next judgement starts after it. */\n  convergenceResetAfter?: number;\n  outcome?: ObjectiveOutcome;\n  /** Short follow-up messages the operator sent as new turns while this objective was unresolved. */\n  amendments: Array<{ at: string; text: string }>;\n  /**\n   * Objective-scoped execution tracking (core/execution_tracking.ts): cumulative steps, progress, repetition,\n   * failed approaches, interventions and compactions. Absent in ledgers written before it existed; `trackingOf` fills it.\n   */\n  execution?: ExecutionTracking;\n}\n\n/** The ledger's execution tracking, created (or completed, for a ledger restored from an earlier version) on first use. */\nexport function trackingOf(ledger: ObjectiveLedger): ExecutionTracker {\n  ledger.execution = normalizeTracking(ledger.execution);\n  // `ContinuationState.totalSteps` predates the richer execution record. Preserve its count when resuming a legacy\n  // task instead of normalizing a missing execution field to a false zero and granting fresh budget.\n  if (Number.isSafeInteger(ledger.continuation?.totalSteps) && ledger.continuation.totalSteps > ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps) {\n    ledger.execution.cumulativeSteps = ledger.continuation.totalSteps;\n  }\n  return new ExecutionTracker(ledger.execution);\n  /** Recovery notes issued since the last operator input (a later episode resumes from this count). */\n  notes: number;\n  /** Equivalent observations refused in the current episode. */\n  denials: number;\n  /** Denials allowed per episode before recovery is exhausted (fixed when the episode is constrained). */\n  allowedDenials: number;\n  enteredStep?: number;\n  /** Workspace state identity the episode concerns (refusals apply only while the workspace is still in it). */\n  state?: string;\n  /** Readable action that triggered the current episode. */\n  trigger?: string;\n  /** Step of the last escalation: several unproductive calls in one batch are one event, not several. */\n  lastEscalationStep?: number;\n  /** Correlated recovery evidence: non_progress_detected, recovery_advisory_issued, recovery_constrained, ... */\n  events: TrackingEvent[];\n}\n\nexport interface ExecutionTracking {\n  version: number;\n  /** Steps charged to this objective across turns and in-turn delegated agents. */\n  cumulativeSteps: number;\n  turns: number;\n  /** Consecutive steps without progress, across turns; operator input resets it. */\n  stepsWithoutProgress: number;\n  lastProgressStep: number;\n  repetitions: RepetitionRecord[];\n  progress: TrackingEvent[];\n  stagnation: TrackingEvent[];\n  failedApproaches: TrackingEvent[];\n  interventions: TrackingEvent[];\n  compactions: CompactionEvent[];\n  /** Consecutive pressure compactions that yielded little (thrashing evidence; reset by a useful one). */\n  lowYieldCompactions: number;\n  seenStates: string[];\n  seenObservations: string[];\n  seenLedgerStates: string[];\n  coverage: CoverageSegment[];\n  equivalents: EquivalenceRecord[];\n  recovery: RecoveryState;\n  evicted: { states: number; observations: number; ledgerStates: number; repetitions: number; events: number; coverage: number };\n}\n\nfunction createRecovery(): RecoveryState {\n  return { stage: \"normal\", episode: 0, notes: 0, denials: 0, allowedDenials: 0, events: [] };\n}\n\nexport function createTracking(): ExecutionTracking {\n  return {\n    version: TRACKING_VERSION,\n    cumulativeSteps: 0,\n    turns: 0,\n    stepsWithoutProgress: 0,\n    lastProgressStep: 0,\n    repetitions: [],\n    progress: [],\n    stagnation: [],\n    failedApproaches: [],\n    interventions: [],\n    compactions: [],\n    lowYieldCompactions: 0,\n    seenStates: [],\n    seenObservations: [],\n    seenLedgerStates: [],\n    coverage: [],\n    equivalents: [],\n    recovery: createRecovery(),\n    evicted: { states: 0, observations: 0, ledgerStates: 0, repetitions: 0, events: 0, coverage: 0 },\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Fills, in place, fields a tracking record written by an earlier version lacks (restored ledgers), and returns the\n * same object: every holder (the running turn's tracker, compaction, the ledger) must share one record.\n */\nexport function normalizeTracking(raw: unknown): ExecutionTracking {\n  if (!raw || typeof raw !== \"object\") return createTracking();\n  const t = raw as Record<string, any>;\n  const base = createTracking() as unknown as Record<string, any>;\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(base)) {\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n      if (!Array.isArray(t[key])) t[key] = [];\n    } else if (typeof value === \"number\") {\n      if (typeof t[key] !== \"number\" || !Number.isFinite(t[key])) t[key] = value;\n    } else if (key === \"evicted\") {\n      t[key] = { ...value, ...(t[key] && typeof t[key] === \"object\" ? t[key] : {}) };\n    } else if (key === \"recovery\") {\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Checks made before a content-bearing request leaves: model and credential present (provider connections), and the\n   * shared cloud spending limits. Shows the disclosure notice the first time a cloud origin is used in this process.\n   */\n  private preflight(url: string, requestId: string, payloadChars: number): void {\n    if (this.conn.providerId) {\n      if (!this.model) {\n        throw new InferenceError(\"configuration_error\", \"client\", `Provider '${this.conn.providerId}' needs an explicit model: pass --model or set NEXUS_MODEL.`, { requestId, failoverEligible: false });\n      }\n      if (this.conn.auth !== \"none\" && this.conn.auth !== \"sigv4\" && !this.credentialFor(url) && !this.declaredAuthless()) {\n        const variable = operatorSettingKeyForAuth(this.conn.providerId);\n        throw new InferenceError(\"configuration_error\", \"client\", `No credential for provider '${this.conn.providerId}': set ${variable}. Nexus never substitutes another provider's or the appliance's credential.`, {\n          requestId,\n          failoverEligible: false,\n          condition: \"AUTH_FAILURE\",\n        });\n      }\n    }\n    if (this.disclosureOf(url) !== \"cloud\") return;\n    // Spending limits cover provider connections, whose requests are recorded; the legacy endpoint path has no receipts.\n    if (this.conn.providerId) {\n      this.reservations.push(requestId);\n      const reason = UsageLedger.global().admit(requestId, Math.ceil(payloadChars / 4) + this.maxOutputTokens, this.conn.usage === \"openrouter\", this.conn.providerId, this.model);\n      if (reason) throw new InferenceError(\"policy_denied\", \"client\", `Cloud spending limit: ${reason}.`, { requestId, failoverEligible: false });\n    }\n    const origin = originOf(url) ?? url;\n    if (!announcedDestinations.has(origin)) {\n      announcedDestinations.add(origin);\n      const locality = classifyLocality(url);\n      this.emitDiagnostic(\"error\", pc.dim(`[nexus] Cloud inference: ${this.conn.label} (${origin}, locality: ${locality.reason}), model ${this.model || \"(unset)\"}. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.`));\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** `compatible` connections may run without a key only when the operator declares it (NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH=none). */\n  private declaredAuthless(): boolean {\n    return this.conn.providerId === \"compatible\" && authoritySetting(\"NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH\") === \"none\";\n  }\n\n  /** Records a receipt for an inference request (local endpoint or provider connection). */\n  private async withReceipt<T>(requestId: string, purpose: string | undefined, run: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n    this.pending = undefined;\n    this.reservations = [];\n    const pending = (): PendingRequest | undefined => this.pending;\n    const base = () => {\n      const p = pending();\n      const ep = p?.endpoint ?? this.endpoint;\n      const disclosure = this.disclosureOf(ep);\n      return {\n        at: new Date().toISOString(),\n        requestId,\n        role: purpose ?? this.role,\n        providerId: this.conn.providerId ?? \"local\",\n        selectedModel: this.model,\n        ...(p?.effectiveModel ? { effectiveModel: p.effectiveModel } : {}),\n        endpointOrigin: originOf(ep) ?? \"\",\n        protocol: this.conn.protocol,\n        disclosure,\n        origin_class: (disclosure === \"cloud\" ? \"cloud\" : \"local\") as \"local\" | \"cloud\",\n        ...(p?.executions ? { executions: p.executions } : {}),\n        ...(p?.providerRequestId ? { providerRequestId: p.providerRequestId } : {}),\n        ...(p?.usage ? { usage: p.usage } : {}),\n        costConfidence: p?.usage?.costUsd !== undefined ? (\"provider-reported\" as const) : (\"unknown\" as const),\n      };\n    };\n    const releaseAll = () => {\n      for (const id of this.reservations) UsageLedger.global().release(id);\n      this.reservations = [];\n    };\n    try {\n      const result = await run();\n      releaseAll();\n      this.markSucceeded(pending()?.endpoint ?? this.endpoint);\n      this.lastUsageReport = pending()?.usage;\n      UsageLedger.global().record({ ...base(), outcome: \"completed\", usageConfidence: pending()?.usage ? \"provider\" : \"uncertain\" }, this.workspace);\n      return result;\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      releaseAll();\n      const notSent = err instanceof InferenceError && (err.kind === \"policy_denied\" || err.kind === \"configuration_error\");\n      const maybeBilled = !(err instanceof InferenceError) || err.execution !== \"NOT_EXECUTED\";\n      UsageLedger.global().record({\n        ...base(),\n        outcome: err instanceof InferenceError && err.kind === \"aborted\" ? \"aborted\" : \"failed\",\n        failureKind: err instanceof InferenceError ? err.kind : \"error\",\n        usageConfidence: pending()?.usage ? \"provider\" : notSent || !maybeBilled ? \"none\" : \"uncertain\",\n      }, notSent ? undefined : this.workspace);\n      throw err;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * `fetch` that resends when a reused keep-alive connection was closed under the request (TUI audit D-20). On a healthy\n   * server an idle timeout can fire as the next request is written; the request then fails with `UND_ERR_SOCKET: other\n   * side closed` or ECONNRESET, which classified as a temporary outage and made the turn wait and print a notice.\n   * RFC 9112 section 9.3.1 allows resending in that case. It is done only for a URL under a configured endpoint (the\n   * tokenize fallback is not) that has answered before (a first-use reset is a real failure), within moments of the\n   * attempt (a server that dies mid-generation fails later), and not after an abort or timeout; only a thrown fetch is\n   * resent, never a response. A server that reads a request and then dies would see it again and again, so resends are\n   * budgeted: a resend that fails again is charged to its endpoint and kind of request (probe or POST), at most\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":34638}},"started_at_ms":1795156577971,"completed_at_ms":1795156577971}}
