{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T06:40:44.822Z","ordinal":32839,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6830f0ed-1387-4973-b3d5-cb7aea1fc322","process_id":"40786","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh run view 44670790609 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs,url; sed -n '28,43p' docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md; sed -n '200,275p' cli/test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v1-2x-backlog-reconcile","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh run view 44670790609 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs,url; sed -n '28,43p' docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md; sed -n '200,275p' cli/test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"headSha\":\"f87ff07f09db90d4de14783547e859da55863f7b\",\"jobs\":[{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:36Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"databaseId\":136070985173,\"name\":\"lsp\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"steps\":[{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:05Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Set up job\",\"number\":1,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:04Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:08Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1\",\"number\":2,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:05Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:13Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1\",\"number\":3,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:08Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:14Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e\",\"number\":4,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:13Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:16Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Install typescript-language-server and pyright\",\"number\":5,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:14Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:24Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Install pinned rust-analyzer toolchain\",\"number\":6,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:16Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:58Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Install pinned gopls\",\"number\":7,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:24Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:59Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run npm ci --prefix cli\",\"number\":8,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:58Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Versions on the runner\",\"number\":9,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:54:59Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:33Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Run the real-server tests\",\"number\":10,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:00Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:33Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Post Run actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e\",\"number\":18,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:33Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:34Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Post Run actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1\",\"number\":19,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:33Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:34Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Post Run actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1\",\"number\":20,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:34Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"completedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:34Z\",\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"Complete job\",\"number\":21,\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-20T03:55:34Z\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44670790609/job/136070985173\"}],\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44670790609\"}\nThe first real run showed the default launch commands for TypeScript, JavaScript and Python were missing `--stdio`; both servers print a usage error and exit without it, so `lsp_diagnostics` for those files was always `unavailable` in practice. Fixed in `getServerForFile`; a test that needs no server pins the arguments.\n\n## What it does not cover\n\n- The trust and sandbox gates with a real server (they are tested with the fake server; a gated manager never starts one).\n- A larger real project: navigation uses three source files, but there is no large workspace-wide diagnostics fixture, incremental-edit sequence, or server crash/restart scenario.\n- Server versions other than the pinned ones (typescript 5.6.3, typescript-language-server 4.3.4, pyright 1.1.390; gopls (`@latest`: v0.16.2 stopped building on a newer runner Go on 2026-11-18) and the runner's rust-analyzer are unpinned).\n- Hosted-runner result (manual run 44323291710 on `3732d911`, 2026-11-18): **typescript-language-server, pyright and gopls passed** (a deliberate error reported, a clean file a real empty report, a broken server `unavailable`), which also confirms on real servers that the default launch needs `--stdio`. **rust-analyzer failed**: the product reported \"not installed or failed to start\" although the rustup proxy answered `--version` in the test's probe. The cause is not diagnosed (it needs a host with the rust-analyzer component to reproduce); the Rust case therefore runs as a `todo` (reported, not failing the job) unless `NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE` names it, and the workflow requires `typescript,python,go`. A manual run of that change on its branch (run 44323915622) completed successfully: 5 pass, 0 fail, 1 todo (Rust).\n- **rust-analyzer (2026-11-18, reproduced locally in an isolated rustup home):** two separate problems, both fixed. (1) *Setup:* the workflow added the component to the toolchain pinned by the repository's `rust-toolchain.toml`, but the product launches the server in a fixture directory outside the repository, where rustup uses the **default** toolchain, which had no rust-analyzer (\"failed to start\" in about 150 ms); the test's `--version` probe ran from the repository and could not see it. The probe now runs in the fixture directory and the workflow adds the component from a directory with no override. (2) *Product behaviour:* `lsp_diagnostics` used to return on the first `publishDiagnostics`, which rust-analyzer sends **empty** before it has loaded the Cargo project and analysed types, so a file with a type error was reported clean. A server can now be marked `awaitProgress` (rust-analyzer is, in the built-in table): the client advertises `window.workDoneProgress`, answers the server's own requests (`window/workDoneProgress/create`, `workspace/configuration`, ...), tracks `$/progress`, and after the first publish waits until the server's progress has ended and been quiet for 1.5 s (or, if it reports none, a 4 s grace), always within the caller's timeout. Server-free tests (`lsp_progress.test.ts`) pin it with a fake staged server (four mutations each fail a test); the real-server case passes locally against rust-analyzer 1.100.0 (about 13 s for a first call on a tiny crate).\n- **Hosted validation of this change:** manual run 44334778543 on the branch (2026-11-18): typescript-language-server, pyright, gopls and rust-analyzer all pass (6 tests, 0 fail, 0 todo; Rust about 18 s). Earlier runs of the same workflow found the setup mismatch (44323291710), the empty-first-publish behaviour (44332636397) and a `gopls@v0.16.2` build break on the runner's newer Go (now `@latest`).\n- **Three-file navigation extension:** hosted run [44606102675](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44606102675) on commit `99c6049f` (2026-11-19) passed all 10 tests with `NEXUS_LSP_REQUIRE=typescript,python,go,rust`: all four real servers passed the diagnostics and navigation cases, with 0 failures, skips, or todos. This is a small three-source-file chain, not evidence for large-project behavior.\n- **Hover and definition (CS-6 follow-up):** each real server is asked, through the product, to hover and go to the definition through a three-source-file project (positions are 1-based, as `lsp_hover` and `lsp_definition` take them); the call is retried until the case timeout because servers answer only after analysis, and the definition must point into the defining file. This checks a small import/re-export chain; it does not establish behavior on large projects.\n- **Cost and limit:** a first Rust diagnostics call on a large crate can take as long as the project load, and is bounded by the caller's timeout, after which the existing \"published no diagnostics\" `unavailable` applies. Later calls return as soon as progress is quiet. A change to an already-open file is not waited on separately: the latest published list is returned.\n\n## Pinned hosted environment (2026-11-20)\n\n});\n\ntest(\"the default servers for typescript and python are launched with --stdio (they exit without it)\", () => {\n  const dir = writeFixture({});\n  const mgr = new LspBridgeManager(dir);\n  try {\n    for (const f of [\"a.ts\", \"a.tsx\", \"a.js\", \"a.py\"]) assert.deepEqual(mgr.getServerForFile(f)?.args, [\"--stdio\"], f);\n    for (const f of [\"a.rs\", \"a.go\"]) assert.equal(mgr.getServerForFile(f)?.args, undefined, f);\n  } finally {\n    mgr.shutdownAll();\n  }\n});\n\n// Navigation (hover and definition) against the same real servers: a function defined in one file and called in another.\n// A server answers these only once it has analysed the project, so the call is retried until a deadline; a server that never\n// answers is a failure, and an answer is checked for what it names, not merely for existing.\ninterface NavCase {\n  id: string;\n  files: Record<string, string>;\n  /** The call site (1-based line and character, as the product's lsp_hover/lsp_definition take them, on the callee's name) and the file that defines it. */\n  at: { file: string; line: number; character: number };\n  definedIn: string;\n  hoverMentions: RegExp;\n}\n\nconst NAV: NavCase[] = [\n  {\n    id: \"typescript\",\n    files: {\n      \"tsconfig.json\": JSON.stringify({ compilerOptions: { strict: true, noEmit: true, target: \"es2022\", module: \"esnext\", moduleResolution: \"bundler\" }, include: [\"*.ts\"] }),\n      \"lib.ts\": \"export function greet(name: string): string {\\n  return name;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"service.ts\": 'export { greet } from \"./lib\";\\n',\n      \"use.ts\": 'import { greet } from \"./service\";\\nexport const msg: string = greet(\"a\");\\n',\n    },\n    at: { file: \"use.ts\", line: 2, character: 30 },\n    definedIn: \"lib.ts\",\n    hoverMentions: /greet/,\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"python\",\n    files: {\n      \"pyrightconfig.json\": JSON.stringify({ typeCheckingMode: \"basic\" }),\n      \"lib.py\": \"def greet(name: str) -> str:\\n    return name\\n\",\n      \"service.py\": \"from lib import greet\\n\",\n      \"use.py\": 'from service import greet\\n\\nmsg: str = greet(\"a\")\\n',\n    },\n    at: { file: \"use.py\", line: 3, character: 13 },\n    definedIn: \"lib.py\",\n    hoverMentions: /greet/,\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"rust\",\n    files: {\n      \"Cargo.toml\": '[package]\\nname = \"lspnav\"\\nversion = \"0.0.0\"\\nedition = \"2021\"\\n',\n      \"src/util.rs\": \"pub fn greet(name: &str) -> String {\\n    name.to_string()\\n}\\n\",\n      \"src/service.rs\": \"pub use crate::util::greet;\\n\",\n      \"src/main.rs\": 'mod service;\\nmod util;\\nfn main() {\\n    let _ = service::greet(\"a\");\\n}\\n',\n    },\n    at: { file: \"src/main.rs\", line: 4, character: 25 },\n    definedIn: \"src/util.rs\",\n    hoverMentions: /greet/,\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"go\",\n    files: {\n      \"go.mod\": \"module lspnav\\n\\ngo 1.21\\n\",\n      \"lib.go\": \"package main\\n\\nfunc greet(name string) string {\\n\\treturn name\\n}\\n\",\n      \"service.go\": \"package main\\n\\nfunc welcome(name string) string {\\n\\treturn greet(name)\\n}\\n\",\n      \"main.go\": 'package main\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\t_ = welcome(\"a\")\\n}\\n',\n    },\n    at: { file: \"main.go\", line: 4, character: 7 },\n    definedIn: \"service.go\",\n    hoverMentions: /welcome/,\n  },\n];\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":664237735}},"started_at_ms":1795156843157,"completed_at_ms":1795156844822}}
