{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T06:41:21.417Z","ordinal":32867,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05793ea695c2aa2c016affeb8b7f3087d2925597ba064d5199","status":"completed","call_id":"call_19d7086b2dbd45928d5c2355039f452e","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v1-2x-backlog-reconcile/docs/v1.2.2/BACKLOG.md\\n@@\\n-| CS-6 | Test `cli/test/lsp_real_servers.test.ts`, weekly non-required workflow `lsp-real-servers.yml`, `docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md`; typescript-language-server and pyright validated locally (pass; mutation-checked); fixed the missing `--stdio` for TS/JS/Python | The workflow has not yet run on a hosted runner; rust-analyzer and gopls cases are written but have run nowhere (not installed on the dev host), so treat them as unvalidated; hover, definition, the trust and sandbox gates and multi-file projects are not exercised against real servers; versions of rust-analyzer and gopls are not pinned by the test |\\n+| CS-6 | Real-server diagnostics, hover and definition for TypeScript, Python, Go and Rust; three-source-file navigation; pinned hosted toolchains. Evidence: hosted run [44670790609](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/44670790609) passed on `f87ff07f`; see `docs/LSP_REAL_SERVERS.md`. | Still untested against real servers: trust/sandbox refusal paths, large workspace diagnostics, incremental edits, and server crash/restart. The current hosted result covers small three-file projects only. |\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1f730-5dda-7050-8748-e755b63ef781","create_time":1795156875.4992938}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":14512,"sampled_through_sequence":14510,"client_authored":false}}
